1
00:00:04,472 --> 00:00:07,608
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2
00:00:07,642 --> 00:00:11,045
♪ NEXT SUNDAY, A.D. ♪

3
00:00:11,078 --> 00:00:13,682
♪ THERE WAS A GUY
NAMED JOEL ♪

4
00:00:13,715 --> 00:00:17,185
♪ NOT TOO DIFFERENT
FROM YOU OR ME ♪

5
00:00:17,218 --> 00:00:20,255
♪ HE WORKED
AT GIZMONIC INSTITUTE ♪

6
00:00:20,288 --> 00:00:23,492
♪ JUST ANOTHER FACE
IN A RED JUMPSUIT ♪

7
00:00:23,525 --> 00:00:26,227
♪ HE DID A GOOD JOB
CLEANING UP THE PLACE ♪

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:27,828
♪ BUT HIS BOSSES
DIDN'T LIKE HIM ♪

9
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:30,065
♪ SO THEY SHOT HIM
INTO SPACE ♪

10
00:00:32,567 --> 00:00:35,703
♪ WE'LL SEND HIM
CHEESY MOVIES ♪

11
00:00:35,737 --> 00:00:39,107
- ♪ THE WORST WE CAN FIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

12
00:00:39,140 --> 00:00:41,777
♪ HE'LL HAVE TO SIT
AND WATCH THEM ALL ♪

13
00:00:41,810 --> 00:00:45,247
- ♪ AND WE'LL MONITOR HIS MIND ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

14
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:48,282
♪ NOW KEEP IN MIND
JOEL CAN'T CONTROL ♪

15
00:00:48,315 --> 00:00:51,485
- ♪ WHERE THE MOVIES
BEGIN OR END ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

16
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:54,522
♪ BECAUSE HE USED
THOSE SPECIAL PARTS ♪

17
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:57,292
♪ TO MAKE HIS ROBOT FRIENDS ♪

18
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:01,095
LET'S GO.

19
00:01:01,128 --> 00:01:02,363
- CAMBOT.
- PAN LEFT.

20
00:01:02,397 --> 00:01:03,665
HI, GIRL.

21
00:01:03,698 --> 00:01:05,467
WHAT A COOL GUY.

22
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:07,235
A WISECRACKER.

23
00:01:07,268 --> 00:01:10,238
♪ IF YOU'RE WONDERING HOW
HE EATS AND BREATHES ♪

24
00:01:10,272 --> 00:01:12,873
- ♪ AND OTHER SCIENCE FACTS ♪
- ♪ LA LA LA ♪

25
00:01:12,907 --> 00:01:16,110
♪ THEN REPEAT TO YOURSELF
"IT'S JUST A SHOW ♪

26
00:01:16,143 --> 00:01:19,280
♪ "I SHOULD REALLY
JUST RELAX ♪

27
00:01:19,313 --> 00:01:22,150
♪ FOR... ♪

28
00:01:34,228 --> 00:01:37,298
ALL RIGHT.
IN THROUGH THE MOUTH.

29
00:01:37,332 --> 00:01:40,568
AND OUT THROUGH THE NOSE
OR ITS EQUIVALENT.

30
00:01:40,602 --> 00:01:42,203
GOOD, GOOD, ALL RIGHT.

31
00:01:42,237 --> 00:01:44,205
NOW WE LOOSEN THE LIPS
ON A "P."

32
00:01:44,238 --> 00:01:47,175
[ALL] PPPPPPP.

33
00:01:47,208 --> 00:01:49,377
GOOD, GOOD, GOOD, NOW,
LET'S LOOSEN UP THAT JAW.

34
00:01:49,410 --> 00:01:51,645
AFTER ME, PUMPERNICKEL.

35
00:01:51,678 --> 00:01:55,417
[ALL] PUMPERNICKEL,
PUMPERNICKEL, PUMPERNICKEL.

36
00:01:55,450 --> 00:01:57,252
VERY GOOD, AND NOW,
FOR THE EPIGLOTTIS.

37
00:01:57,285 --> 00:02:00,755
"THE WIRE IS WOUND
AROUND THE WHEEL."

38
00:02:00,788 --> 00:02:04,258
[ALL]
THE WIRE IS WOUND
AROUND THE WHEEL.

39
00:02:04,292 --> 00:02:05,560
OH, HI, EVERYBODY.

40
00:02:05,593 --> 00:02:07,395
WELCOME TO
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE.

41
00:02:07,428 --> 00:02:09,397
TOM SERVO'S JUST
TEACHING US THE IMPORTANCE

42
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:11,165
AND THE PROPER EXERCISE

43
00:02:11,198 --> 00:02:13,535
TO WARM US UP BEFORE
WE GO INTO THE EXPERIMENT.

44
00:02:13,568 --> 00:02:16,203
COMMERCIAL SIGN
IN 15 SECONDS.

45
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:18,272
NO, NO,
PRONOUNCE EVERY WORD.

46
00:02:18,305 --> 00:02:20,708
MAKE A NICE, ROUND "O"
WITH THE LIPS.

47
00:02:20,742 --> 00:02:23,477
COMMERCIAL "SIIIGN."

48
00:02:23,512 --> 00:02:24,778
COMMERCIAL "SIIIGN."

49
00:02:24,812 --> 00:02:27,248
COMMERCIAL "SIIIGN."

50
00:02:27,282 --> 00:02:29,217
COMMERCIAL "SIIIGN."

51
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,083
- ALL RIGHT.
- GOOD, GOOD, GOOD.

52
00:02:30,117 --> 00:02:32,220
WE ACTUALLY HAVE
COMMERCIAL SIGN, THOUGH.

53
00:02:32,253 --> 00:02:34,588
UH, JOEL,
COMMERCIAL "SIIIGN."

54
00:02:34,622 --> 00:02:35,590
COMMERCIAL SIGN.

55
00:02:35,623 --> 00:02:37,392
COMMERCIAL "SIIIGN."

56
00:02:37,425 --> 00:02:38,860
DON'T PUSH IT, OKAY?

57
00:02:38,893 --> 00:02:39,960
- OH.
- IS IT TIME
TO TOUCH PELVISES?

58
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,028
WE GOT COMMERCIAL SIGN.

59
00:02:41,062 --> 00:02:43,297
- I SLIT THE SHEET--
- [BOTS] THE SHEET I SLIT--

60
00:02:50,338 --> 00:02:52,640
AND FIVE AND SIX
AND SEVEN AND GOOD.

61
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:54,908
OKAY, SHAKE IT LOOSE,
EVERYBODY, SHAKE IT OUT.

62
00:02:54,942 --> 00:02:56,743
- VERY GOOD.
- HI, EVERYBODY.

63
00:02:56,777 --> 00:02:59,213
WELCOME TO
THE SATELLITE OF LOVE AGAIN.

64
00:02:59,247 --> 00:03:02,350
UH, WHILE TOM AND CROW FINISH
THEIR STRETCHING EXERCISES,

65
00:03:02,383 --> 00:03:04,285
I'M GOING TO ENJOY
A DELICIOUS SALAD.

66
00:03:04,318 --> 00:03:06,753
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT MIGHT
BE NICE AT THIS POINT?

67
00:03:06,787 --> 00:03:09,323
HOW ABOUT A NICE BACKRUB,
EVERYBODY, HMM?

68
00:03:09,357 --> 00:03:10,425
EVERYBODY RUB
EACH OTHER'S BACK, HMM?

69
00:03:10,458 --> 00:03:11,825
UH, I HAVE AN IDEA.

70
00:03:11,858 --> 00:03:13,393
- OH, YOU DO?
- YEAH.

71
00:03:13,427 --> 00:03:15,530
UH, LET'S DO THAT
TRUST EXERCISE YOU TAUGHT US.

72
00:03:15,563 --> 00:03:17,465
- YOU KNOW, WHERE YOU
LEAN BACK AND I CATCH YOU?
- OH, SAY, GREAT!

73
00:03:17,498 --> 00:03:18,633
- OKAY, ME FIRST,
OKAY, HERE WE GO.
- OKAY? OKAY.

74
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:20,402
OKAY, NOW, WHEN YOU FEEL IT,

75
00:03:20,435 --> 00:03:22,370
- JUST-- JUST TRUST.
- I'M FEELING IT,
I'M LETTING GO.

76
00:03:22,403 --> 00:03:23,605
- ALL RIGHT.
- I'M LETTING GO.
- AND SO AM I.

77
00:03:23,638 --> 00:03:25,473
- [TOM SERVO SCREAMS]
OH, YOU LITTLE--

78
00:03:25,507 --> 00:03:27,608
TOE MONSTER!
TOE MONSTER! WOO!

79
00:03:27,642 --> 00:03:29,310
OH. WELL, ANYWAY.

80
00:03:29,343 --> 00:03:31,745
I THOUGHT I'D ENJOY
A DELICIOUS SALAD.

81
00:03:31,778 --> 00:03:34,282
THE PROBLEM-- THIS IS ALSO
MY INVENTION EXCHANGE.

82
00:03:34,315 --> 00:03:36,717
THE PROBLEM WITH TAKEOUT
ENDLESS SALAD BARS

83
00:03:36,750 --> 00:03:39,487
IS, ONCE YOU LEAVE
THE ENDLESS SALAD BAR

84
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:40,922
WITH YOUR
TAKE-OUT CONTAINER,

85
00:03:40,955 --> 00:03:42,523
IT CEASES TO BE
AN ENDLESS SALAD BAR

86
00:03:42,557 --> 00:03:45,627
AND STARTS BEING A SALAD BAR
WITH REALLY STRICT RULES.

87
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,928
SO I DESIGNED THIS SPECIAL
TAKE-OUT CONTAINER.

88
00:03:47,962 --> 00:03:49,663
IT'S GOT BAFFLES
AND AIR CHANNELS.

89
00:03:49,697 --> 00:03:51,432
IT'D TAKE A SCIENTIST
TO EXPLAIN IT,

90
00:03:51,465 --> 00:03:52,733
AND I'M FROM THE HUMANITIES.

91
00:03:52,767 --> 00:03:54,935
BUT ALL I KNOW IS,
WHEN YOU TAKE OUT THE SALAD,

92
00:03:54,968 --> 00:03:56,537
IT'S LIKE THERE'S REALLY

93
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,707
A WHOLE BUNCH
OF SALAD IN THERE.

94
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:00,508
LIKE THAT, SEE, WHOOPS.

95
00:04:00,542 --> 00:04:02,743
SPILLED A LITTLE. THERE.

96
00:04:02,777 --> 00:04:04,412
WHAT DO YOU THINK, SIRS?

97
00:04:04,445 --> 00:04:06,647
OH, WE THINK IT'S LOVELY.
DON'T WE, FRANK?

98
00:04:06,680 --> 00:04:08,415
YES, VERY.

99
00:04:08,448 --> 00:04:09,650
WELL, WE HAVE NOTHING

100
00:04:09,683 --> 00:04:11,485
BIG AND FLASHY
TO SHOW YOU THIS WEEK.

101
00:04:11,518 --> 00:04:13,955
YOU CAUGHT US IN THE MIDDLE
OF OUR HOME ACTIVITIES.

102
00:04:13,988 --> 00:04:15,290
UH, FRANK, WHY DON'T YOU
SHOW THEM THAT

103
00:04:15,323 --> 00:04:16,923
BIRDCAGE THING
YOU'RE WORKING ON?

104
00:04:16,958 --> 00:04:18,993
NOW, HERE'S SOMETHING I THINK
YOU'LL REALLY LIKE.

105
00:04:19,027 --> 00:04:21,462
NOW, EVERYBODY LOVES PETS,
RIGHT?

106
00:04:21,495 --> 00:04:23,865
I SURE DO, BUT THE ONLY PROBLEM
WITH PETS IS--

107
00:04:23,898 --> 00:04:25,500
THEY'RE KIND OF UNSANITARY,
YOU KNOW?

108
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:27,668
IT'S HARD
TO CLEAN UP AFTER THEM.

109
00:04:27,702 --> 00:04:29,070
SO WHAT I'VE DONE
IS I'VE INVENTED

110
00:04:29,103 --> 00:04:32,307
THIS VACUUM CLEANER
FOR CLEANING UP BIRDCAGES.

111
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:34,042
WE'LL JUST
TURN THIS ON HERE.

112
00:04:34,075 --> 00:04:36,343
NOW, IT CLEANS UP NEWSPAPERS

113
00:04:36,377 --> 00:04:37,545
AND BIRDSEEDS

114
00:04:37,578 --> 00:04:39,947
AND ANY... OOH!

115
00:04:44,385 --> 00:04:46,053
WELL, BACK TO PLANET EARTH.

116
00:04:46,087 --> 00:04:48,022
YOUR EXPERIMENT
THIS WEEK, JOEL,

117
00:04:48,055 --> 00:04:51,525
IS THE FIRST IN THE FAMOUS
GAMERA TURTLE MOVIES.

118
00:04:51,558 --> 00:04:52,760
IT'S A LOVE STORY ABOUT

119
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:55,430
A GIANT TURTLE
AND DOWNTOWN TOKYO.

120
00:04:55,463 --> 00:04:57,465
UH, FRANK, BE A TREAS
AND SEND THAT UP, WON'T YOU?

121
00:04:57,498 --> 00:04:59,000
[FRANK CHUCKLES]

122
00:04:59,033 --> 00:05:01,402
- THE BIRD--
- OH CRIMINY, I'LL DO IT.

123
00:05:01,435 --> 00:05:03,838
I GOTTA DO EVERYTHING
AROUND HERE.

124
00:05:03,872 --> 00:05:04,972
[ALARM BLARES]

125
00:05:05,005 --> 00:05:07,675
OH, WE GOT MOVIE SIGN!

126
00:05:17,085 --> 00:05:18,552
WOW, YOU GUYS
TOOK KIND OF A SPILL.

127
00:05:18,585 --> 00:05:19,853
WE'RE OKAY.

128
00:05:19,887 --> 00:05:21,755
WATER, THE SOURCE
OF ALL LIFE.

129
00:05:21,788 --> 00:05:23,590
OUR STORY STARTS HERE.

130
00:05:23,623 --> 00:05:24,858
HEY, SANDY FRANK,
ISN'T THAT WHEN

131
00:05:24,892 --> 00:05:26,393
YOU DROP YOUR HOT DOG
AT THE BEACH?

132
00:05:26,427 --> 00:05:27,662
I-- HUH?

133
00:05:27,695 --> 00:05:30,632
- A "DAIEEEEE" MOTION PICTURE.
- AAH!

134
00:05:30,665 --> 00:05:32,367
BLUB BLUB
BLUB BLUB BLUB BLUB.

135
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,835
[JOEL WASHES FACE]

136
00:05:33,868 --> 00:05:36,537
REFRESHING.

137
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:38,538
- CAMERA!
- UH, IT'S GAMERA.

138
00:05:38,572 --> 00:05:41,008
- OH.
- UM, M-C-M-L-X-V

139
00:05:41,042 --> 00:05:42,643
"DAIEEEEE"
INTERNATIONAL FILMS.

140
00:05:45,813 --> 00:05:46,980
MR. McPICKLE WHIPS.

141
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:48,482
HIDEMASA NAGATA,

142
00:05:48,515 --> 00:05:50,752
THAT'S JAPANESE FOR
"IN-A-GADDA-DA-VIDA."

143
00:05:50,785 --> 00:05:52,453
OH, I SEE TH-- HUH?

144
00:05:52,487 --> 00:05:55,423
OR "I GOT INTO THE GOUDA."

145
00:05:55,457 --> 00:05:56,890
PLANNING, YOU KNOW,
I'D LIKE TO BE AN ACTOR,

146
00:05:56,923 --> 00:05:59,460
BUT I REALLY WANNA PLAN.

147
00:05:59,493 --> 00:06:02,597
- PLAN.
- I'M STARTING TO GET
CINEMA-SICK HERE.

148
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:05,098
♪ FUMI TAKAHASHI
MR. KOBASHI! ♪

149
00:06:05,132 --> 00:06:08,837
- [CROW GIGGLES]
- THAT'S DUMB.

150
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:11,572
♪ NORIAKI YUASA
MR. BABUSHKA! ♪

151
00:06:11,605 --> 00:06:13,507
YEAH, OKAY, OKAY, YEAH.
THAT'S CUTE.

152
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:15,677
THAT'S CUTE...

153
00:06:17,778 --> 00:06:21,082
TITLES BY
THE ATLANTIC OCEAN.

154
00:06:21,115 --> 00:06:24,452
THE INDIAN OCEAN, WHATEVER.

155
00:06:24,485 --> 00:06:26,120
SPECIAL EFFECTS.
HE MUST BE THE GUY

156
00:06:26,153 --> 00:06:27,822
CHURNING THE WATER OVER THERE.

157
00:06:27,855 --> 00:06:30,558
YEAH.
RUNNING THE AGITATOR.

158
00:06:30,592 --> 00:06:32,193
AGITATING MAN.

159
00:06:32,227 --> 00:06:33,862
♪ TATSUJI NAKAHUJI ♪

160
00:06:33,895 --> 00:06:35,897
- ♪ MR. B. B. RABUDZI ♪
- NOW YOU'RE GETTING IT.

161
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:37,765
GUYS, THAT'S
REALLY ANNOYING.

162
00:06:37,798 --> 00:06:39,700
- SORRY.
- OH.

163
00:06:42,670 --> 00:06:43,938
YOU KNOW, THEY COULD
TELL US ANYTHING,

164
00:06:43,972 --> 00:06:45,440
- AND WE'D BELIEVE IT.
- YEAH, WE HAVE TO.

165
00:06:45,473 --> 00:06:47,775
WE'RE AT THEIR MERCY,
BASICALLY.

166
00:06:47,808 --> 00:06:49,877
[TOM SERVO HUMS]

167
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,812
[CROW HUMS ALONG]

168
00:06:51,845 --> 00:06:55,617
♪ UTARO HOJO RISIN' ♪

169
00:06:55,650 --> 00:06:57,618
JUNE HAMLIN.

170
00:06:57,652 --> 00:06:59,720
OH, DEATH FROM ON HIGH.

171
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:03,157
HEY, GUYS.

172
00:07:03,190 --> 00:07:07,128
THE RAYTHEON CORPORATION
WELCOMES YOU.

173
00:07:07,162 --> 00:07:08,695
MICRO MACHINES
AT 12 O'CLOCK!

174
00:07:08,728 --> 00:07:11,232
AND G.I. JOE IS THERE!

175
00:07:11,265 --> 00:07:13,033
MERCY. [GROWLS]

176
00:07:17,538 --> 00:07:19,573
WOOF.

177
00:07:19,607 --> 00:07:21,208
- THERE GOES
THE NEIGHBORHOOD.
- HERE WE ARE.

178
00:07:21,242 --> 00:07:22,877
IT LOOKS WILD.

179
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:26,013
- YOU CAN SAY THAT AGAIN.
- [ALL] IT LOOKS WILD.

180
00:07:26,047 --> 00:07:27,215
LET'S START UNLOADING
THE EQUIPMENT.

181
00:07:27,248 --> 00:07:28,917
ANTHONY QUINN?

182
00:07:28,950 --> 00:07:30,552
- WE WON'T NEED
EVERYTHING AT ONCE.
- LITTLE RICHARD?

183
00:07:30,585 --> 00:07:32,487
RUFF.

184
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,888
ARF.

185
00:07:33,922 --> 00:07:35,690
HELLO, HOW DO YOU DO, SIR?

186
00:07:35,723 --> 00:07:36,957
- OH, I MAKE A GOOD LIVING.
- WE ARE FROM

187
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,927
THE EXPLORATION SHIP,
JIDORI MARU.

188
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,728
I KNOW, I KNOW.

189
00:07:40,762 --> 00:07:42,095
LOOK, LOOK, UP THERE!

190
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:45,098
WHAT DO YOU SEE, SQUEAKY?

191
00:07:45,132 --> 00:07:47,602
DEATH FROM ON HIGH AGAIN.
HEY BOYS.

192
00:07:47,635 --> 00:07:49,003
[MAN GASPS]

193
00:07:49,037 --> 00:07:51,805
THE DEVIL'S BIRDS!

194
00:07:51,838 --> 00:07:53,942
- IT'S JUST A PLANE.
- THE ENGINES ARE SILENT

195
00:07:53,975 --> 00:07:56,543
BECAUSE THEY'RE AVOIDING
THE FIGHTER PLANES.

196
00:07:56,577 --> 00:07:57,845
I WONDER WHOSE THEY ARE.

197
00:07:57,878 --> 00:07:59,080
OH, IT'S THE NELSON BOYS.

198
00:07:59,113 --> 00:08:00,682
- THEIR PARENTS
BUY THEM EVERYTHING.
- THE WAR EVEN COMES

199
00:08:00,715 --> 00:08:02,283
TO THIS ESKIMO VILLAGE.

200
00:08:02,317 --> 00:08:04,585
SOON THERE WON'T
BE ANY PEACE ANYWHERE.

201
00:08:04,618 --> 00:08:06,720
- HMM.
- TOO BAD.

202
00:08:06,753 --> 00:08:10,658
RED BALL HITS.

203
00:08:10,692 --> 00:08:12,058
HEY, TOY BOAT, TOY BOAT.

204
00:08:12,092 --> 00:08:14,228
[ALL] TOY BOAT,
TOY BOAT, TOY BOAT.

205
00:08:14,262 --> 00:08:16,797
UNIQUE NEW YORK.

206
00:08:16,830 --> 00:08:18,698
- CAPTAIN.
- YES?

207
00:08:18,732 --> 00:08:20,100
- CAPTAIN.
- [JOEL] YES?
- THE ICE IS GETTING THICKER.

208
00:08:20,133 --> 00:08:21,902
- OH CAPTAIN, MY CAPTAIN.
- SHOULD WE KEEP GOING?

209
00:08:21,935 --> 00:08:24,572
- OF COURSE.
WE MUST GET THROUGH.
- HUH.

210
00:08:24,605 --> 00:08:26,807
DO YOU THINK DR. HIDAKA WILL
LEARN ANYTHING FROM THE ESKIMOS?

211
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,275
- OH, GET REAL.
- I CERTAINLY HOPE HE DOES.

212
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:30,912
YES.

213
00:08:30,945 --> 00:08:33,080
HEY, LOOK OUT, THERE'S A PATCH
OF WATER OUT THERE!

214
00:08:33,113 --> 00:08:35,917
HUH.

215
00:08:35,950 --> 00:08:37,218
- HUH?
- CAPTAIN!

216
00:08:37,252 --> 00:08:40,287
LOOK, WHAT IS THAT?

217
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:42,022
IT'S DEATH FROM ON HIGH,
I TOLD YOU.

218
00:08:42,055 --> 00:08:43,690
[MORSE KEY BEEPS]

219
00:08:43,723 --> 00:08:45,927
UM, IF... YOU'RE NOT...

220
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:49,130
WEARING... ANY UNDERWEAR...

221
00:08:49,163 --> 00:08:50,530
UH, SMILE.

222
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:55,135
IF YOU'RE NOT...

223
00:08:55,168 --> 00:08:57,305
WEARING... ANY...

224
00:08:57,338 --> 00:08:59,807
UH, THEY PULLED THE UNDERWEAR
GAG ON US, SIR.

225
00:09:03,377 --> 00:09:05,145
UNIDENTIFIED AIRCRAFT, SIR.

226
00:09:05,178 --> 00:09:07,315
AMERICANS, WHAT'RE THEY
DOING IN THE FILM?

227
00:09:09,683 --> 00:09:11,918
HAVE YOU SPOTTED ANYTHING
ON YOUR RADAR SCREEN?

228
00:09:11,952 --> 00:09:14,022
NO, SIR.
IT MUST BE COATED WITH

229
00:09:14,055 --> 00:09:16,023
ANTI... ELECTRIC
WAVE PAINT, SIR.

230
00:09:16,057 --> 00:09:17,892
- CUT! CUT!
LET'S DO THAT AGAIN.
- OKAY.

231
00:09:17,925 --> 00:09:19,327
OPERATOR, HAND ME THE MIKE.

232
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,195
- YES, SIR.
- HEY, IT'S CURLY JOE
AS THE GENERAL.

233
00:09:21,228 --> 00:09:23,797
CALLING ALL PLANES,
FIGHTER PLANES,

234
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:25,767
BASED IN THE ARCTIC OCEAN.

235
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,802
- HEY MOE!
- THIS IS YOUR COMMANDER
CALLING.

236
00:09:27,835 --> 00:09:29,737
OVER.

237
00:09:29,770 --> 00:09:32,172
THIS IS THE STRATEGIC FIRE,
OVER.

238
00:09:32,205 --> 00:09:33,907
- THERE IS AN UNIDENTIFIED
AIRCRAFT

239
00:09:33,942 --> 00:09:36,210
HE SOUNDS LIKE BUDDY HACKETT.

240
00:09:36,243 --> 00:09:37,278
EIGHT-FOUR-POINT-
TWO-SEVEN-THREE --

241
00:09:37,312 --> 00:09:39,180
LOOK, HE'S GOT
FRANKENBERRY HANDS.

242
00:09:39,213 --> 00:09:40,782
- ...LATITUDE.
- FRANKENBERRY.

243
00:09:40,815 --> 00:09:43,783
AT ONE-SEVEN-SIX-POINT-
FIVE-EIGHT DEGREES.

244
00:09:43,817 --> 00:09:45,887
EAST LONGITUDE.

245
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,788
- UH, GENERAL,
YOU'RE DRUNK, AREN'T YOU?
- INTERCEPT,

246
00:09:47,822 --> 00:09:49,657
AND ESCORT IT TO THE BASE.

247
00:09:49,690 --> 00:09:51,825
IF IT RESISTS,
SHOOT IT DOWN.

248
00:09:51,858 --> 00:09:53,327
ROGER.

249
00:10:01,268 --> 00:10:03,070
CAPTAIN, WILL THEY
ATTACK US?

250
00:10:03,103 --> 00:10:04,705
MM... I DOUBT IT.

251
00:10:04,738 --> 00:10:08,775
THEY'RE MODELS.

252
00:10:08,808 --> 00:10:10,745
GROUND CONTROL
TO MAJOR WONG.

253
00:10:14,248 --> 00:10:16,983
- TALLY-HO!
- TALLY-HO, YOU LITTLE VIXENS.

254
00:10:22,323 --> 00:10:24,058
ANSWER.

255
00:10:24,092 --> 00:10:25,793
ANSWER.

256
00:10:25,827 --> 00:10:27,662
WHAT IS YOUR NATIONALITY
AND FLIGHT PURPOSE?

257
00:10:27,695 --> 00:10:29,197
PHRASE IT IN THE FORM
OF A QUESTION.

258
00:10:29,230 --> 00:10:31,065
IF YOU DON'T ANSWER,

259
00:10:31,098 --> 00:10:32,733
WE WILL TAKE YOU
TO THE AMERICAN AIRBASE.

260
00:10:32,767 --> 00:10:35,268
HE ASKED ME! HE ASKED ME!

261
00:10:35,302 --> 00:10:37,237
BREAK OFF. GIVE CHASE.

262
00:10:38,972 --> 00:10:40,842
HE GIVES GOOD CHASE.

263
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:47,313
ANSWER IMMEDIATELY!

264
00:10:47,348 --> 00:10:49,183
WHAT IS YOUR NATIONALITY
AND FLIGHT PURPOSE?

265
00:10:49,217 --> 00:10:50,852
ARE YOU KNOWN FOR YOUR
WORK IN THE THEATER?

266
00:10:53,987 --> 00:10:55,422
UH, YOU LOST YOUR MUFFLER.

267
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:57,758
ALL PLANES,
PREPARE FOR ACTION.

268
00:10:57,792 --> 00:11:01,195
FIRE!

269
00:11:01,228 --> 00:11:03,063
JUST A COUPLE MISSILES,
THAT'S ALL.

270
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,970
AND THAT'S JUST A WARNING.

271
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:12,005
UH, BREAK-NINER, WE GOT
MRS. O'LEARY'S COW

272
00:11:12,038 --> 00:11:14,208
COMING ON INTO RUNWAY THREE.

273
00:11:16,443 --> 00:11:17,745
[ALL] OOH.

274
00:11:17,778 --> 00:11:21,182
[ALL] AHH.

275
00:11:21,215 --> 00:11:23,317
PRETTY.

276
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:25,152
GROUND SHOW.

277
00:11:25,185 --> 00:11:27,422
IT LOOKS LIKE THAT AIRPLANE
CARRIED ATOMIC WEAPONS.

278
00:11:27,455 --> 00:11:29,757
- YEAH, YEAH,
I THINK YOU'RE RIGHT.
- WHICH MEANS WE'RE ALL DEAD.

279
00:11:29,790 --> 00:11:32,860
DID YOU SEE THE FORCE OF THAT
EXPLOSION AS IT HIT THE GROUND?

280
00:11:32,893 --> 00:11:35,897
- WHAT A GREAT STORY.
- MERCY. [JOEL GROWLS]

281
00:11:35,930 --> 00:11:38,065
BE CAREFUL, THOUGH,
DON'T GO INTO THAT AREA.

282
00:11:38,098 --> 00:11:39,733
THERE'S RADIATION THERE.

283
00:11:39,767 --> 00:11:41,368
AND, AS EVERYBODY KNOWS,
IT CAN ONLY AFFECT YOU

284
00:11:41,402 --> 00:11:42,803
IF YOU TOUCH IT.

285
00:11:46,007 --> 00:11:48,875
- AAH.
- OH!

286
00:11:48,908 --> 00:11:51,278
JEEZ, I HATE THE SOUND
OF SQUEAKY STYROFOAM.

287
00:11:51,312 --> 00:11:53,080
YEAH, WHEN YOU SLICE IT
WITH A BREAD KNIFE?

288
00:11:53,113 --> 00:11:56,383
OH.

289
00:11:56,417 --> 00:11:58,918
AND SO,
IN FEAR AND HOT WATER,

290
00:11:58,952 --> 00:12:02,523
THE FIRST SLURPEE IS BORN.

291
00:12:02,557 --> 00:12:05,125
SOMEBODY'S GOT
A TORO SNOWBLOWER DOWN THERE.

292
00:12:05,158 --> 00:12:06,393
- CHECK IT OUT.
- THAT'S NEAT.

293
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:14,868
GOOD MORNING.

294
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:22,477
- [GAMERA ROARS]
- NOW WHY CAN'T I HAVE
A CUTE SHAPE LIKE THAT?

295
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:24,278
KEEP WORKING ON IT.

296
00:12:24,312 --> 00:12:26,380
ALL RIGHT,
QUIT THROWING STUFF AT ME.

297
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:27,815
THAT'S GOOD, THAT'S ENOUGH.

298
00:12:27,848 --> 00:12:29,117
THANK YOU,
I'M HERE ALL WEEK.

299
00:12:29,150 --> 00:12:30,818
THANK YOU, ENJOY THE--

300
00:12:33,387 --> 00:12:35,923
CALLING FIGHTER PLANES,
ANSWER.

301
00:12:35,957 --> 00:12:37,423
CALLING FIGHTER PLANES,
ANSWER.

302
00:12:37,458 --> 00:12:39,227
HEY, MOE! WOOP WOO-WOO-WOO,

303
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,062
WOOP WOO-WOO-WOO.

304
00:12:41,095 --> 00:12:43,997
IMPOSSIBLE TO MAKE
CONTACT, SIR.

305
00:12:44,030 --> 00:12:45,967
I'M HERE, UNCLE DAVE.

306
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,935
- KEEP TRYING.
- YES, SIR.

307
00:12:47,968 --> 00:12:49,303
SIR, I THINK SOMEBODY

308
00:12:49,337 --> 00:12:51,005
IS SENDING OUT
RADIO-JAMMING WAVES.

309
00:12:51,038 --> 00:12:52,573
WHAT ARE YOU DOING ABOUT IT?

310
00:12:52,607 --> 00:12:54,275
- FIND OUT WHERE
IT'S COMING FROM.
- YES, SIR.

311
00:12:54,308 --> 00:12:55,208
YES, SIR.

312
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:05,018
IS THE RADIO WORKING?
CAN YOU CONTACT THE SHIP?

313
00:13:05,052 --> 00:13:07,153
I'VE BEEN TRYING,
BUT THE ATMOSPHERIC CONDITIONS

314
00:13:07,187 --> 00:13:08,922
ARE BAD, AND I CAN'T
MAKE CONTACT.

315
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:10,892
AND THIS LITTLE KID KEEPS
TWISTING ALL THE DIALS.

316
00:13:10,925 --> 00:13:12,125
WHAT'LL WE DO?

317
00:13:12,158 --> 00:13:13,493
ALL RIGHT, DAN, LET'S GO BACK.

318
00:13:13,527 --> 00:13:15,997
- RIGHT.
- YES.

319
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:17,463
- GOODBYE, CHIEF.
- GOODBYE, McCLOUD.

320
00:13:17,498 --> 00:13:19,900
THANK YOU.

321
00:13:19,933 --> 00:13:22,068
- BYE.
- ...DAVEY.

322
00:13:22,102 --> 00:13:24,938
I'LL SEE YOU IN HELL.

323
00:13:24,972 --> 00:13:27,140
HMM.

324
00:13:27,173 --> 00:13:29,577
OR NOT.

325
00:13:29,610 --> 00:13:31,912
HERE, HAVE SOME
MAGGOTY MEAT.

326
00:13:31,945 --> 00:13:33,313
MR. HIDAKA?

327
00:13:33,347 --> 00:13:35,482
YES?

328
00:13:35,515 --> 00:13:38,318
THIS IS THE LEGENDARY STONE.

329
00:13:38,352 --> 00:13:41,388
- YOU PASSED THAT STONE?
- HANDED DOWN FROM
OUR FATHERS.

330
00:13:41,422 --> 00:13:43,090
LOOKS LIKE A MEDIUM-RARE
PORTERHOUSE.

331
00:13:43,123 --> 00:13:46,160
THEN IS THIS THE TURTLE THAT
LIVED ON THE ARCTIC CONTINENT?

332
00:13:46,193 --> 00:13:48,195
- I JUST TOLD YOU THAT.
- YES.

333
00:13:48,228 --> 00:13:49,897
IT IS...

334
00:13:49,930 --> 00:13:51,498
THE DEVIL'S ENVOY.

335
00:13:51,532 --> 00:13:55,135
- KISSINGER?
- GAMERA!
- OH.

336
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:56,603
KIDS GO RUNNING FOR
THE RICH TASTE OF GAMERA.

337
00:13:56,637 --> 00:13:59,540
GAMERA? THEN MY THEORY
WAS RIGHT AFTER ALL.

338
00:13:59,573 --> 00:14:01,875
STEAK KEEPS.

339
00:14:01,908 --> 00:14:03,377
BUT YOU SEE THAT
WAVE-LIKE PATTERN?

340
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:05,312
IT DOESN'T MATCH
THE OTHER CARBON.

341
00:14:05,345 --> 00:14:08,248
- OH, JUST TRIM THAT AWAY.
ADD THAT TO THE SOUP.
- EXCUSE ME, CHIEF.

342
00:14:08,282 --> 00:14:10,885
- WHERE IS IT FROM?
- I DON'T KNOW.

343
00:14:10,918 --> 00:14:12,553
I KNOW...

344
00:14:12,587 --> 00:14:15,322
IT BRINGS EVIL.

345
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:17,357
WE MAY HAVE HIT UPON
SOMETHING VERY IMPORTANT.

346
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:19,058
- REFRIGERATION.
- COULD IT BE A CREATURE

347
00:14:19,092 --> 00:14:20,393
THAT'S NOT KNOWN?

348
00:14:20,427 --> 00:14:22,195
IT'S HARD TO SAY.

349
00:14:22,228 --> 00:14:23,997
THERE ARE WAVES AROUND IT.

350
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:26,033
- IT MUST BE AQUATIC.
- LIKE A DUCK, SIR?

351
00:14:26,067 --> 00:14:28,268
DO YOU THINK
THAT IT COULD BE

352
00:14:28,302 --> 00:14:30,570
A PREHISTORIC CREATURE
OR FROM ANOTHER PLANET?

353
00:14:30,603 --> 00:14:32,138
ANYTHING'S POSSIBLE.

354
00:14:32,172 --> 00:14:34,140
WHEN YOU DREAM.

355
00:14:34,173 --> 00:14:36,210
BEEF. REAL FOOD
FOR REAL PEOPLE.

356
00:14:36,243 --> 00:14:37,578
WHAT DO YOU THINK
IT IS, CAPTAIN?

357
00:14:37,612 --> 00:14:39,547
UH, A COUPLE OF ESKIMOS
LOOKING AT A STEAK.

358
00:14:39,580 --> 00:14:43,150
I'VE NEVER SEEN ANYTHING
LIKE IT. VERY STRANGE.

359
00:14:43,183 --> 00:14:45,318
IT LOOKS LIKE IT'S
A KIND OF A SEA CREATURE.

360
00:14:45,352 --> 00:14:47,553
AND YOU LOOK LIKE
A WHO FROM WHOVILLE.

361
00:14:49,690 --> 00:14:52,092
MORNING. LIKE MY SNOW FORT?

362
00:14:55,128 --> 00:14:57,197
GENTLEMEN, YOU SEEM
A LITTLE TENSE.

363
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:59,232
LET ME BREAK THE ICE.
[CROW LAUGHS]

364
00:14:59,267 --> 00:15:01,135
- BREAK THE...
- [SERVO CHUCKLES]

365
00:15:01,168 --> 00:15:02,402
[GAMERA ROARS]

366
00:15:02,435 --> 00:15:04,638
- UH-OH.
- ABANDON SHIP,
ABANDON SHIP!

367
00:15:04,672 --> 00:15:06,107
OH YEAH,
ABANDON SHIP TO WHERE?

368
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:09,142
--ABANDON SHIP!

369
00:15:09,175 --> 00:15:11,278
ABANDON SHIP IMMEDIATELY!

370
00:15:11,312 --> 00:15:13,013
ABANDON SHIP IMMEDIATELY!

371
00:15:13,047 --> 00:15:15,148
ABANDON SHIP IMMEDIATELY!

372
00:15:15,182 --> 00:15:18,252
[ALL] ABANDON TOY!
ABANDON TOY!

373
00:15:18,285 --> 00:15:20,687
HEY, THERE'S ERNIE DOUGLAS
AS SPARKS, CHECK IT OUT.

374
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:24,592
THEY'RE ABANDONING SHIP!

375
00:15:24,625 --> 00:15:28,062
AND HE'S IN PAIN.

376
00:15:28,095 --> 00:15:29,430
IF I HAD A WISDOM TOOTH
LIKE THAT,

377
00:15:29,463 --> 00:15:31,132
- I'D BE IN PAIN TOO.
- THE WHEEL, THE WHEEL!

378
00:15:31,165 --> 00:15:32,667
I'VE INVENTED THE WHEEL!

379
00:15:32,700 --> 00:15:34,735
EVERYBODY OFF,
I SAID EVERYBODY OFF!

380
00:15:34,768 --> 00:15:38,072
- LET'S GO, LET'S GO!
- THAT'S MY WHEEL.

381
00:15:38,105 --> 00:15:40,140
EMERGENCY, S.O.S! S.O.S!

382
00:15:40,173 --> 00:15:42,175
EMER-GENCY, EMER-GENCY.

383
00:15:46,647 --> 00:15:49,650
OUT OF THE FRYING PAN,
INTO THE ICEBOX.

384
00:15:49,683 --> 00:15:51,385
ECHO.

385
00:15:51,418 --> 00:15:53,120
LOOK AT THOSE LITTLE GUYS
DOWN THERE.

386
00:15:53,153 --> 00:15:55,188
- OOH!
- HOW ABOUT A LITTLE
FIRE, SCARECROW?

387
00:16:00,093 --> 00:16:01,595
- [CROW COUGHS]
- COMMANDER!

388
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:04,063
UH, I MEAN, DAD?

389
00:16:04,097 --> 00:16:06,267
LAST MESSAGE FROM
THE JIDORI MARU.

390
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:07,668
UH, WOULD YOU SIGN THIS,
'CAUSE...

391
00:16:07,702 --> 00:16:10,403
- SO I CAN GO ON
A FIELD TRIP AND STUFF?
- HUGE TURTLE.

392
00:16:10,437 --> 00:16:11,672
- DON'T READ IT.
- 60 METERS.
- IT'S OKAY.

393
00:16:11,705 --> 00:16:13,340
WHAT'S GOING ON AROUND HERE?

394
00:16:13,373 --> 00:16:14,575
I DON'T KNOW, SIR.

395
00:16:14,608 --> 00:16:16,477
LOOKS LIKE A HUGE TURTLE
MADE ITS APPEARANCE.

396
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:19,278
A GIANT TURTLE WOULD BE GOOD
AS FUDGIE THE WHALE.

397
00:16:19,312 --> 00:16:21,582
- ENJOY CARVEL ICE CREAM!
- ...FIND OUT WHAT'S GOING ON.

398
00:16:23,183 --> 00:16:25,185
ICE STATION TITAN.

399
00:16:27,688 --> 00:16:30,223
HEY, IT'S A RAGTAG
BAND OF MISFITS!

400
00:16:31,792 --> 00:16:33,760
I CAN'T SEE A DAMN THING.

401
00:16:33,793 --> 00:16:37,597
I DON'T KNOW WHAT'S GOING ON
HERE, IT'S PITCH-BLACK IN HERE.

402
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:38,698
OH, OH, THAT'S BETTER.

403
00:16:38,732 --> 00:16:42,335
I FOUND THE SPOT WHERE
THE RESEARCH SHIP WENT DOWN.

404
00:16:42,368 --> 00:16:44,237
BUT CAN'T SEE EITHER THE CREW
OR THE GIANT TURTLE.

405
00:16:46,307 --> 00:16:48,242
UH, LOOKS LIKE
THEY'RE FLYING OVER

406
00:16:48,275 --> 00:16:49,777
THE PLOTHOLE FOR THE FILM.

407
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:52,012
- OH, THERE IT IS.
- THAT'S BIG ENOUGH.

408
00:16:54,615 --> 00:16:56,050
UNIQUE NEW YORK.

409
00:16:56,083 --> 00:16:58,518
[ALL] UNIQUE NEW YORK,
UNIQUE NEW YORK.

410
00:16:58,552 --> 00:17:01,422
OOH, NEW YORK "NEWS STUD."

411
00:17:01,455 --> 00:17:03,057
- HELLO, LADIES.
- GOOD AFTERNOON.

412
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:05,125
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
WE HAVE SPECIAL NEWS

413
00:17:05,158 --> 00:17:06,727
AND AN EXTRA GUEST,
DR. HIDAKA.

414
00:17:06,760 --> 00:17:08,762
NEIL SEDAKA?

415
00:17:08,795 --> 00:17:11,132
- GOOD AFTERNOON.
- THANK YOU, DOCTOR.

416
00:17:11,165 --> 00:17:11,798
- THANK YOU.
- GOOD AFTERNOON.

417
00:17:11,832 --> 00:17:13,367
- YOKO.
- PLEASE SIT DOWN.

418
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,568
- THANK YOU.
- LOOKIN' FINE.

419
00:17:14,602 --> 00:17:16,570
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN,
DR. HIDAKA,

420
00:17:16,603 --> 00:17:18,172
A JAPANESE ZOOLOGIST,

421
00:17:18,205 --> 00:17:20,307
WILL NOW COMMENT
ON THE GREAT TURTLE

422
00:17:20,340 --> 00:17:23,443
WHICH MADE HIS APPEARANCE
IN THE ARCTIC OCEAN RECENTLY.

423
00:17:23,477 --> 00:17:26,313
- AND THEN I'M GOING ALL COY.
- DR. HIDAKA, PLEASE.

424
00:17:26,347 --> 00:17:29,115
- [ALL FEIGN JAPANESE]
- LADIES AND GENTLEMEN--

425
00:17:29,148 --> 00:17:31,652
HERRO, WELCOME TO REGIS
AND KATHIE REE!

426
00:17:31,685 --> 00:17:35,688
A VERY GREAT CONTINENT
IN THE NORTHERN ARCTIC REGION.

427
00:17:35,722 --> 00:17:39,225
AN EXTRAORDINARY CREATURE
LIVED THERE, WHOSE NAME WAS--

428
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:41,728
- TODD.
- GAMERA. A GIANT TURTLE.

429
00:17:41,762 --> 00:17:43,797
A MONSTER OF ANOTHER AGE.

430
00:17:43,830 --> 00:17:45,865
- SWEET.
- AND THIS IS
A LEGENDARY STONE

431
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:48,368
HANDED DOWN BY THE ESKIMOS.

432
00:17:48,402 --> 00:17:50,337
THIS GAMERA IS--
- NOW, WE PREPARED THIS STEAK

433
00:17:50,370 --> 00:17:52,372
- BEFORE THE SHOW.
- ...FOR THOUSANDS OF YEARS,

434
00:17:52,405 --> 00:17:55,142
IMPRISONED UNDER AN ICEBERG.

435
00:17:55,175 --> 00:17:56,743
- HOWEVER--
- SLEEP! SLEEP!

436
00:17:56,777 --> 00:17:59,312
HE REVIVED AFTER
THE ICEBERG EXPLODED.

437
00:17:59,345 --> 00:18:02,783
AS THE RESULT OF A...
OF AN ATOMIC BOMB.

438
00:18:02,817 --> 00:18:05,652
HMM, LOOKS LIKE KATHIE'S
MEDICATION SEEMS TO BE WORKING.

439
00:18:05,685 --> 00:18:08,422
...RESEARCH SHIP WE WERE USING,
KILLING EVERY ONE OF THE CREW.

440
00:18:08,455 --> 00:18:10,323
WE THREE WERE
NOT ON BOARD THEN.

441
00:18:10,357 --> 00:18:12,225
- AND SO MY DAUGHTER AND I--
- UH, OVER HERE.

442
00:18:12,258 --> 00:18:14,193
...WERE SPARED,
AND ALSO A YOUNG REPORTER.

443
00:18:14,227 --> 00:18:15,528
OH, YOU MEAN "NEWS STUD."

444
00:18:15,562 --> 00:18:16,897
I WARN ALL OF YOU

445
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:18,865
THAT GAMERA IS VIOLENT

446
00:18:18,898 --> 00:18:20,600
AND MUST THEREFORE
BE APPROACHED

447
00:18:20,633 --> 00:18:22,235
THE UTMOST CAUTION.

448
00:18:22,268 --> 00:18:24,437
- BUT ALSO, GAMERA--
- HE'S ON THE WRONG CAMERA.

449
00:18:24,472 --> 00:18:26,840
- ...IS EXPECTED TO DIE SHORTLY
DUE TO RADIOACTIVITY.
- PSST! PSST!

450
00:18:26,873 --> 00:18:29,242
AND SO, I SAY--

451
00:18:29,275 --> 00:18:31,245
- I PRAY THAT
THIS WILL HAPPEN SOON--
- [BOTS WHISPER]

452
00:18:31,278 --> 00:18:32,847
FOR THE PEACE
OF THE ENTIRE WORLD.

453
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:34,380
- SO SEND
YOUR DOLLARS TO CARE.
- AND THAT THE MONSTER WILL

454
00:18:34,413 --> 00:18:37,217
VANISH ONCE AND FOR ALL
IN THE DEPTHS OF THE SEA.

455
00:18:37,250 --> 00:18:38,752
AMEN. THE END.

456
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:41,788
ONLY, AS A ZOOLOGIST,

457
00:18:41,822 --> 00:18:43,423
I GREATLY REGRET THE LOSS

458
00:18:43,457 --> 00:18:46,927
OF A CREATURE ORIGINATING
IN THE DAWN OF TIME.

459
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,628
- THANK YOU.
- YOU'RE WELCOME.

460
00:18:48,662 --> 00:18:50,297
- AAH!
- HEY, VARIETY!

461
00:18:50,330 --> 00:18:52,265
SMASH! CRASH! TURBO-BASH!

462
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:53,867
ZACK NORMANY IS SAMMY
IN CHIEF ZABU!

463
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:55,835
THE NEW YORK TIMES
SAYS GOD IS DEAD,

464
00:18:55,868 --> 00:18:58,238
AND THE WAR'S BEGUN,
AND ALVIN TOSTIG

465
00:18:58,272 --> 00:19:01,575
HAS A SON TODAY.

466
00:19:01,608 --> 00:19:02,943
NO COMICS.

467
00:19:02,977 --> 00:19:05,345
- WHAT'S THIS?
- [MAN HUMS]

468
00:19:05,378 --> 00:19:08,782
OH, THIS IS THE UNIVERSAL
UNSUSPECTING DRUNKARD

469
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:10,683
ABOUT TO HAVE A BRUSH
WITH THE SUPERNATURAL.

470
00:19:10,717 --> 00:19:12,285
MY LEGS ARE OLD.

471
00:19:12,318 --> 00:19:14,420
MY TEETH ARE GRAY.
MY ARMS ARE GNARLED.

472
00:19:14,453 --> 00:19:17,958
FOSTER BROOKS-SAN.

473
00:19:17,992 --> 00:19:19,325
HUH?

474
00:19:19,358 --> 00:19:20,593
UH?

475
00:19:20,627 --> 00:19:22,528
OH, THAT OLD THING.

476
00:19:22,562 --> 00:19:24,363
OH! BALL OF FIRE!

477
00:19:24,397 --> 00:19:26,500
OH, ANDY, IT'S A BALL OF FIRE.

478
00:19:26,533 --> 00:19:29,737
TELL AUNT...

479
00:19:29,770 --> 00:19:31,738
OH, IT'S ONE OF THOSE PESKY
LITTLE FLYING PIES.

480
00:19:31,772 --> 00:19:35,375
I THINK THAT'S
WHAT IT IS, YES.

481
00:19:35,408 --> 00:19:38,278
THAT'S VERY STRANGE.

482
00:19:38,312 --> 00:19:40,747
I NEVER SAW
A BALL OF FIRE BEFORE

483
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:43,217
THAT CHANGED ITS COURSE!

484
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:45,352
I'VE NEVER SEEN
A BALL OF FIRE!

485
00:19:45,385 --> 00:19:46,720
MAYBE IT'S THE FLYING SAUCER

486
00:19:46,753 --> 00:19:49,455
THAT I HEARD THEM TALK ABOUT

487
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:52,258
SO MUCH LATELY.

488
00:19:52,292 --> 00:19:54,360
- [ALL APPLAUD] BRAVO, BRAVO.
- WE HAVE A SPECIAL
NEWS BULLETIN TONIGHT.

489
00:19:54,393 --> 00:19:55,962
FLYING SAUCERS
HAVE BEEN SIGHTED

490
00:19:55,995 --> 00:19:57,497
IN VARIOUS PARTS
OF THE WORLD.

491
00:19:57,530 --> 00:19:59,567
OVER LONDON, NEW YORK,
AND CAPE TOWN.

492
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:02,468
EVEN AN OLD FARMER OUTSIDE
OF TOKYO CLAIMS HE SAW ONE.

493
00:20:02,502 --> 00:20:04,337
AND HE'S OLD,
GOOFY, AND DRUNK.

494
00:20:07,673 --> 00:20:09,743
WOULD YOU CARE FOR A MAGAZINE
OR A NEWSPAPER, SIR?

495
00:20:09,777 --> 00:20:12,445
- I'LL TAKE ANYTHING FROM YOU.
- OH, THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

496
00:20:12,478 --> 00:20:14,615
THE CAPTAIN HAS TURNED OFF
THE NO-DUBBING SIGN.

497
00:20:14,648 --> 00:20:16,417
YOU ARE FREE TO SPEAK
ANY LANGUAGE YOU CHOOSE.

498
00:20:16,450 --> 00:20:19,352
FLYING SAUCERS ARE
THE SOLE TOPIC OF CONVERSATION.

499
00:20:19,385 --> 00:20:20,987
GAMERA HAS LOST
HIS POPULARITY.

500
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,755
OH, THEY PUT HIM
IN A BAD TIME-SLOT,

501
00:20:22,788 --> 00:20:24,792
- FOLLOWING "SUNDAY BEST."
- GAMERA WAS HIT BY RADIATION.

502
00:20:24,825 --> 00:20:27,693
- OOH, WHAT A KILLER.
- MAYBE HE'S DEAD BY NOW.

503
00:20:27,727 --> 00:20:30,030
ANYHOW, I WISH HE HAD
BEEN DONE AWAY WITH

504
00:20:30,063 --> 00:20:31,998
FOR GOOD AND FOR
THE PEACE OF THE WORLD.

505
00:20:32,032 --> 00:20:33,667
- OW-- WAKE UP!
- YOU REALLY MEAN

506
00:20:33,700 --> 00:20:36,002
EVERYONE ON THE JIDORI MARU
WAS KILLED?

507
00:20:36,035 --> 00:20:38,505
AND THAT THE THREE OF US
ARE THE ONLY SURVIVORS?

508
00:20:38,538 --> 00:20:40,673
YES, MY DEAR.

509
00:20:40,707 --> 00:20:42,675
IT HAPPENED WHEN WE WERE
AT THE ESKIMO VILLAGE,

510
00:20:42,708 --> 00:20:45,645
STUDYING THE ANCIENT CARVINGS
ON THAT STONE.

511
00:20:45,678 --> 00:20:48,748
DOCTOR, THERE'S SOMETHING
THAT I WANTED TO TELL YOU.

512
00:20:48,782 --> 00:20:50,450
- THERE'S NO SMOKING
ON THIS FLIGHT.
- BEFORE WE STARTED OUT

513
00:20:50,483 --> 00:20:52,987
FOR THE ESKIMO VILLAGE,
WHILE WE WERE STILL ONBOARD,

514
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:54,855
THE PHOTOGRAPHERS
AND REPORTERS

515
00:20:54,888 --> 00:20:56,690
DREW LOTS FOR
THIS ASSIGNMENT.

516
00:20:56,723 --> 00:20:58,525
- TO SEE WHO WOULD
ACCOMPANY YOU.
- LOTS AND LOTS.

517
00:20:58,558 --> 00:21:00,693
AND YOU'RE THE LUCKY MAN
WHO WON THE DRAW, RIGHT?

518
00:21:00,727 --> 00:21:02,562
LUCKY, INDEED.

519
00:21:02,595 --> 00:21:04,363
THERE WERE AT LEAST
SEVEN OR EIGHT

520
00:21:04,397 --> 00:21:06,467
CAMERAMEN ALONG WITH US.

521
00:21:06,500 --> 00:21:08,535
- NOW THEY'RE GAMERA-MEN.
- THEY WERE NOT SO LUCKY.

522
00:21:08,568 --> 00:21:11,070
- GAMERA.
- ALL OF THEM PERISHED
IN THE ARCTIC OCEAN.

523
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:13,840
- ALL OF THEM EXCEPT
PETER ARNETT.
- YES.

524
00:21:13,873 --> 00:21:15,742
IT WAS A LOTTERY
WITH HUMAN LIVES.

525
00:21:15,775 --> 00:21:18,578
WRITTEN BY SHIRLEY JACKSON.

526
00:21:18,612 --> 00:21:20,447
EXCUSE ME.

527
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,082
ONE OF THOSE PHOTOGRAPHERS

528
00:21:22,115 --> 00:21:23,517
MADE ME AN OFFER.

529
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:24,952
WE WERE TO BE MARRIED
IN MAY.

530
00:21:24,985 --> 00:21:26,920
- A BOTTLE OF WHISKEY
TO EXCHANGE PLACES.
- OH.

531
00:21:26,953 --> 00:21:28,388
BUT I DIDN'T ACCEPT IT.

532
00:21:28,422 --> 00:21:30,557
I GUESS RUNNING AROUND
ON THE ICE

533
00:21:30,590 --> 00:21:31,792
SOUNDED A LOT MORE
INTERESTING

534
00:21:31,825 --> 00:21:33,593
THAN STAYING ONBOARD, RIGHT?

535
00:21:33,627 --> 00:21:35,962
- YES, THAT'S PARTLY IT.
- THAT'S A CHEAP SHOT.

536
00:21:35,995 --> 00:21:39,065
ONLY, I HAD
SOMETHING ELSE IN MIND.

537
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:40,533
- CATHERINE--
- WHOA.

538
00:21:40,567 --> 00:21:42,568
THE REAL REASON IS THAT
I WANTED TO BE WITH YOU.

539
00:21:42,602 --> 00:21:44,603
- WHAT?
- OH, WOULD YOU LAY OFF HER?

540
00:21:44,637 --> 00:21:47,440
...LUCKY CHARM
OF THE EXPEDITION.

541
00:21:47,473 --> 00:21:50,910
CATHERINE, I'LL ALWAYS CONSIDER
THAT YOU SAVED MY LIFE.

542
00:21:50,943 --> 00:21:52,812
BUT... YOU CAN'T.

543
00:21:52,845 --> 00:21:55,582
- YES, YES!
- OH, A MAGICIAN!

544
00:21:55,615 --> 00:21:57,483
...I'LL ALWAYS FEEL THAT WAY,
YOU BROUGHT ME LUCK.

545
00:21:57,517 --> 00:21:59,820
AND YOU BROUGHT ME
A PORTERHOUSE.

546
00:21:59,853 --> 00:22:01,755
MEANWHILE, ON CAPE COD.

547
00:22:01,788 --> 00:22:03,890
PEPPERIDGE FARM REMEMBERS.

548
00:22:06,927 --> 00:22:08,762
- HELLO
- [ALL] HI.
- NICE TO SEE YOU.

549
00:22:08,795 --> 00:22:10,397
[ALL] THANK YOU.

550
00:22:10,430 --> 00:22:12,132
I WAS ACTUALLY
COMING TO SEE YOU.

551
00:22:12,165 --> 00:22:14,667
IS THAT SO? HAS KENNY
DONE ANYTHING WRONG?

552
00:22:14,702 --> 00:22:17,003
NOT REALLY, BUT HE'S DONE
A VERY STRANGE DRAWING.

553
00:22:17,037 --> 00:22:18,538
I THOUGHT YOU SHOULD SEE IT.

554
00:22:18,572 --> 00:22:20,673
UH, THAT'S ME WITH
THE ARROWS THROUGH MY HEAD.

555
00:22:20,707 --> 00:22:22,875
- IT LOOKS LIKE A TURTLE.
- YES.

556
00:22:22,908 --> 00:22:24,077
THAT'S ALL HE EVER DRAWS.

557
00:22:24,110 --> 00:22:25,778
HE REPEATS IT EVERY DAY.

558
00:22:25,812 --> 00:22:28,382
A TYPE OF OBSESSION.

559
00:22:28,415 --> 00:22:30,017
- KENNY'S NOT A BAD STUDENT.
- HE'S JUST TWISTED.

560
00:22:30,050 --> 00:22:32,452
ONLY HE'S VERY MOODY.

561
00:22:32,485 --> 00:22:34,822
HE EVEN HAS A LITTLE TURTLE
THAT HE CARRIES EVERYWHERE.

562
00:22:34,855 --> 00:22:36,590
OH NO, HE BRINGS IT
TO SCHOOL WITH HIM?

563
00:22:36,623 --> 00:22:38,992
YES, HE SEEMS
TO CLING TO IT.

564
00:22:39,025 --> 00:22:40,593
THE OTHER STUDENTS
MAKE FUN OF HIM.

565
00:22:40,627 --> 00:22:41,895
THEY THINK
THAT HE'S STRANGE.

566
00:22:41,928 --> 00:22:43,630
KIDS ARE PERCEPTIVE
THAT WAY.

567
00:22:43,663 --> 00:22:45,865
I REALIZE THAT KENNY'S HAD
A DIFFICULT CHILDHOOD.

568
00:22:45,898 --> 00:22:48,735
YES, HE'S ALL ALONE.

569
00:22:48,768 --> 00:22:50,870
HIS MOTHER DIED
WHEN HE WAS VERY YOUNG.

570
00:22:50,903 --> 00:22:52,738
SHE WAS MAULED BY TURTLES.

571
00:22:52,772 --> 00:22:54,775
...NO MORE TURTLES,
AT LEAST NOT AT SCHOOL.

572
00:22:54,808 --> 00:22:56,042
YES, I'LL TALK TO HIM.

573
00:22:56,075 --> 00:22:57,610
- DON'T WORRY.
- BYE.

574
00:22:57,643 --> 00:23:00,513
OH, AND ASK HIM TO BATHE.
WE MUST HAVE SOME RULES.

575
00:23:00,547 --> 00:23:04,550
HMM, THAT LITTLE SCOUNDREL.

576
00:23:04,583 --> 00:23:07,587
LET ME OUT!
LET ME OUT! PLEASE!

577
00:23:07,620 --> 00:23:09,757
- I MET KENNY'S TEACHER TODAY.
- [ALL MAKE BARF SOUNDS]

578
00:23:09,790 --> 00:23:11,992
- WELL, WHAT DID HE SAY?
- THAT KENNY WAS QUITE AN EXPERT

579
00:23:12,025 --> 00:23:13,560
AT DRAWING TURTLES.

580
00:23:13,593 --> 00:23:15,795
WHEN I WAS HIS AGE,
I USED TO DRAW GIRLS.

581
00:23:15,828 --> 00:23:17,897
OH, DADDY, YOU'RE SO RANDY.

582
00:23:17,930 --> 00:23:20,200
I'M FINISHED EATING.

583
00:23:20,233 --> 00:23:21,835
HMM.

584
00:23:21,868 --> 00:23:23,803
AH, NOW FOR SOME REAL FOOD.

585
00:23:23,837 --> 00:23:26,707
- KENNY?
- UH-OH.

586
00:23:26,740 --> 00:23:28,775
[ALL] BUSTED!

587
00:23:28,808 --> 00:23:30,143
WHAT ARE YOU DOING
WITH THAT?

588
00:23:30,177 --> 00:23:32,178
EVIL THINGS.
HORRIBLE THINGS.

589
00:23:32,212 --> 00:23:33,813
WHO'S ALL THIS FOOD FOR?

590
00:23:33,847 --> 00:23:36,115
SAURON, THE DARK LORD.

591
00:23:36,148 --> 00:23:39,018
DADDY, KENNY'S TAKEN
SOME FOOD AGAIN.

592
00:23:39,052 --> 00:23:41,555
- HIT HIM! HIT HIM NOW!
- KENNY.

593
00:23:41,588 --> 00:23:44,023
I TOLD YOU I DIDN'T WANT THAT
PET IN THE HOUSE ANYMORE.

594
00:23:44,057 --> 00:23:46,960
IT'S MAKING YOU
NEGLECT YOUR SCHOOLWORK.

595
00:23:46,993 --> 00:23:48,795
- AND GIRLS.
- COME INSIDE.

596
00:23:48,828 --> 00:23:50,863
- I THOUGHT WE WERE INSIDE.
- COME ON.

597
00:23:50,897 --> 00:23:52,765
I KNOW HOW MUCH
YOU LOVE YOUR TURTLE.

598
00:23:52,798 --> 00:23:55,535
BUT THERE ARE OTHER THINGS
IN LIFE JUST AS IMPORTANT.

599
00:23:55,568 --> 00:23:57,037
LIKE HAVING FRIENDS.

600
00:23:57,070 --> 00:23:58,738
YOU DON'T WANT
TO LIVE ALONE, DO YOU?

601
00:23:58,772 --> 00:24:01,107
- [SERVO COUGHS]
- SET THAT TURTLE FREE.

602
00:24:01,140 --> 00:24:03,210
LET HIM RETURN
TO HIS NATURAL HOME.

603
00:24:03,243 --> 00:24:05,878
IT'D BE BETTER FOR YOU
TO FORGET TURTLES.

604
00:24:05,912 --> 00:24:08,080
KENNY, IF YOU GET RID
OF THE TURTLE,

605
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:10,650
DADDY WILL GET YOU
ANYTHING YOU WANT, ALL RIGHT?

606
00:24:10,683 --> 00:24:13,085
- HMM, IT'S A PROMISE.
- YES?

607
00:24:13,118 --> 00:24:14,620
TELL ME WHAT
YOU'D LIKE BEST OF ALL.

608
00:24:14,653 --> 00:24:15,988
DIFFERENT PARENTS.

609
00:24:16,022 --> 00:24:17,923
WHAT I'D LIKE
BEST OF ALL IS...

610
00:24:17,957 --> 00:24:21,093
WHAT? TELL US.

611
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:22,228
TO KEEP IT.

612
00:24:22,262 --> 00:24:24,097
[ALL] WAH WAAH WAAAAAH.

613
00:24:24,130 --> 00:24:27,533
TIMMY, IT'S FOR
YOUR OWN GOOD.

614
00:24:27,567 --> 00:24:29,168
IF YOU DON'T, I'LL THROW IT AWAY
WHEN YOU'RE AT SCHOOL.

615
00:24:29,202 --> 00:24:30,937
I'LL SWALLOW IT WHOLE
WITH BEER.

616
00:24:30,970 --> 00:24:32,105
AND YOU KNOW I'LL DO IT.

617
00:24:32,138 --> 00:24:33,240
YOU'D BETTER
GET USED TO THE IDEA

618
00:24:33,273 --> 00:24:35,808
AND GET RID OF IT.

619
00:24:35,842 --> 00:24:37,710
AWW.

620
00:24:37,743 --> 00:24:39,712
I KNOW IT'S HARD.

621
00:24:39,745 --> 00:24:42,115
BUT IT'S REALLY
ALL FOR THE BEST, RIGHT?

622
00:24:42,148 --> 00:24:43,617
AND SOON YOU WON'T
THINK OF IT.

623
00:24:43,650 --> 00:24:44,683
WE'RE GETTING YOU
A LOBOTOMY.

624
00:24:44,717 --> 00:24:46,085
YOU UNDERSTAND, HUH?

625
00:24:46,118 --> 00:24:48,020
MM-HMM.

626
00:24:48,053 --> 00:24:51,525
HE CUT YOUR BRAKE LINE.

627
00:24:51,558 --> 00:24:52,725
[SERVO MAKES FLUSHING NOISE]

628
00:24:52,758 --> 00:24:54,827
SEE YOU ON THE OTHER SIDE,
SWEET FRIEND.

629
00:24:57,797 --> 00:25:00,000
ALL RIGHT, YOU'RE GETTING
IN THAT TOILET BOWL.

630
00:25:00,033 --> 00:25:02,668
HERE'S LOOKING AT YOU,
TURTLE.

631
00:25:02,702 --> 00:25:03,970
SO SAD.

632
00:25:04,003 --> 00:25:05,738
GOODBYE, TIBBY.

633
00:25:05,772 --> 00:25:07,807
OH, TIBBY, IT'S--
I CAN'T WATCH, THIS IS TOO SAD.

634
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,043
I NEVER LIKED YOU,
YOU CAME IN DARKNESS
AND BROUGHT ONLY PAIN.

635
00:25:10,077 --> 00:25:12,878
LET'S GO, I GOTTA GO.
I'M SO SAD.

636
00:25:12,912 --> 00:25:14,747
- I WANNA SEE HIM
KILL THE TURTLE.
- SHH!

637
00:25:26,693 --> 00:25:28,828
MORE FISH FLAKES,
SWEET FRIEND?

638
00:25:30,763 --> 00:25:33,767
♪ OH, TIBBY, MY TIBBY ♪

639
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:37,170
♪ MY HEART IS A MESS ♪

640
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:40,773
♪ I DON'T HAVE
A PROTECTIVE SHELL ♪

641
00:25:40,807 --> 00:25:43,677
♪ OVER MY CHEST ♪

642
00:25:43,710 --> 00:25:46,713
♪ SO PEOPLE CAN HURT ME ♪

643
00:25:46,747 --> 00:25:49,950
♪ WITH THE CRUEL THINGS
THEY DO ♪

644
00:25:49,983 --> 00:25:53,320
♪ YET SOMEHOW, SWEET TIBBY ♪

645
00:25:53,353 --> 00:25:56,823
♪ I KNOW YOU HURT, TOO ♪

646
00:25:56,857 --> 00:25:59,758
♪ OH, TIBBY, MY TIBBY ♪

647
00:25:59,792 --> 00:26:03,128
♪ REALITY'S HARD♪

648
00:26:03,162 --> 00:26:04,663
♪ SO TIBBY ♪

649
00:26:04,697 --> 00:26:08,200
♪ LET'S PLAY IN THE YARD...♪

650
00:26:08,233 --> 00:26:09,802
♪ OH... ♪

651
00:26:09,835 --> 00:26:12,338
♪ TIBBY OH TIBBY ♪

652
00:26:12,372 --> 00:26:15,975
♪ HE RUNS LIKE THE WIND ♪

653
00:26:16,008 --> 00:26:19,145
♪ A COUPLE OF INCHES ♪

654
00:26:19,178 --> 00:26:21,715
♪ AND THEN BACK AGAIN ♪

655
00:26:21,748 --> 00:26:24,017
♪ OH-DOH-DOH ♪

656
00:26:24,050 --> 00:26:26,018
UH, MAY I TAKE A VERSE?

657
00:26:26,052 --> 00:26:28,153
WELL, IF YOU FEEL IT, CROW.

658
00:26:28,187 --> 00:26:30,157
OH, I DO.

659
00:26:30,190 --> 00:26:32,858
- [CROW CLEARS THROAT]
- WELL, CROW,
THEN BY ALL MEANS.

660
00:26:32,892 --> 00:26:34,193
JOIN ME, WON'T YOU?

661
00:26:34,227 --> 00:26:35,928
FIVE, SIX, SEVEN, EIGHT.

662
00:26:35,962 --> 00:26:37,730
- TIPPY--
- IT'S TIBBY! TIBBY!

663
00:26:37,763 --> 00:26:39,165
OH, SORRY.
SORRY, SORRY.

664
00:26:39,198 --> 00:26:42,902
♪ I LOVE YOU
MY FINE LITTLE FELLA ♪

665
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:44,170
♪ EVEN THOUGH YOU GAVE ♪

666
00:26:44,203 --> 00:26:47,673
♪ THE WHOLE FAMILY
SALMONELLA ♪

667
00:26:47,707 --> 00:26:49,375
NO! NO!
IT'S NOT THEIR FAULT!

668
00:26:49,408 --> 00:26:50,777
IT ISN'T THEIR FAULT!

669
00:26:50,810 --> 00:26:51,912
CROW, YOU TAKE
EVERYTHING GOOD

670
00:26:51,945 --> 00:26:54,713
AND YOU RIP MY HEART OUT!

671
00:26:54,747 --> 00:26:56,348
- [SERVO SOBS]
- JEEZ, I'M SORRY.

672
00:26:56,382 --> 00:26:59,252
COME ON, CROW, LET HIM
FINISH HIS SONG.

673
00:26:59,285 --> 00:27:00,953
OH, OKAY.

674
00:27:00,987 --> 00:27:02,388
- GO AHEAD, TOM.
- IT'S JUST A STUPID
OLD TURTLE.

675
00:27:02,422 --> 00:27:03,890
GO AHEAD, TOM.

676
00:27:03,923 --> 00:27:06,058
THANK YOU, CAMBOT.

677
00:27:06,092 --> 00:27:08,795
♪ TIBBY, MY TIBBY ♪

678
00:27:08,828 --> 00:27:12,665
♪ YOUR BLOOD MAY BE COLD ♪

679
00:27:12,698 --> 00:27:16,002
♪ BUT I KNOW THAT
YOUR HEART BURNS ♪

680
00:27:16,035 --> 00:27:19,905
♪ AS HOT AS A COAL ♪

681
00:27:19,938 --> 00:27:22,808
♪ IT BURNS WITH THE LOVE ♪

682
00:27:22,842 --> 00:27:24,910
♪ ONLY TURTLES ♪

683
00:27:24,943 --> 00:27:27,180
♪ CAN FEEL ♪

684
00:27:27,213 --> 00:27:29,448
♪ TIBBY ♪

685
00:27:29,482 --> 00:27:32,685
IS OUR LOVE REAL?

686
00:27:32,718 --> 00:27:36,155
MY TIBBY, I'LL NEVER LET
THE DOG NOSE AROUND YOUR BOWL.

687
00:27:36,188 --> 00:27:37,957
BUT YOU KNOW THAT,
DON'T YOU?

688
00:27:37,990 --> 00:27:40,060
I CAN SEE IT IN YOUR
BEADY LITTLE EYES!

689
00:27:40,093 --> 00:27:42,128
IF YOU HIGH-CENTER
ON YOUR ROCK, TIBBY,

690
00:27:42,162 --> 00:27:45,365
I'LL BE THERE
TO HELP YOU DOWN!

691
00:27:45,398 --> 00:27:48,435
♪ THE TOILET'S NOT
YOUR FATE, FRIEND ♪

692
00:27:48,468 --> 00:27:51,270
♪ YOU'LL ALWAYS
RUN FREE... ♪

693
00:27:52,805 --> 00:27:54,173
♪ TIBBY ♪

694
00:27:54,207 --> 00:27:56,843
♪ LONG AS YOU HAVE ♪

695
00:27:56,877 --> 00:27:59,745
♪ ME... ♪

696
00:28:03,048 --> 00:28:06,485
DO YOU REALIZE A ROBOT JUST
SANG A LOVE SONG TO A TURTLE?

697
00:28:06,518 --> 00:28:08,220
THAT WAS REALLY GOOD, TOM.

698
00:28:08,253 --> 00:28:10,022
[SERVO SOBS]
THANK YOU.

699
00:28:10,057 --> 00:28:11,390
WE GOT COMMERCIAL SIGN.

700
00:28:19,298 --> 00:28:21,067
- THAT WAS GREAT, TOM.
- THANK YOU.

701
00:28:21,100 --> 00:28:22,835
[SERVO SOBS]

702
00:28:22,868 --> 00:28:25,105
TIBBY.

703
00:28:25,138 --> 00:28:26,807
PSST!

704
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:31,143
PSST! HEY, KENNY!

705
00:28:31,177 --> 00:28:32,412
WHO SAID THAT?

706
00:28:32,445 --> 00:28:35,013
WHO'S CALLING MY NAME?
THAT'S NOT FUNNY!

707
00:28:38,452 --> 00:28:39,785
HUH?

708
00:28:39,818 --> 00:28:41,187
WHAT GIVES?

709
00:28:41,220 --> 00:28:43,857
THIS IS STRANGE.

710
00:28:43,890 --> 00:28:45,425
HOWDY, HOWDY-- HUH?

711
00:28:45,458 --> 00:28:48,428
OH.

712
00:28:48,462 --> 00:28:50,230
NEAT.

713
00:28:50,263 --> 00:28:52,298
THOSE KIDS AT SCHOOL,
THEY TEASE YOU, KENNY,

714
00:28:52,332 --> 00:28:54,233
BECAUSE THEY'VE NEVER
TASTED HELL.

715
00:28:54,267 --> 00:28:58,170
- TODAY WE TURN THE TABLES!
- KENNY?

716
00:28:58,203 --> 00:29:00,005
KNOW WHAT I JUST SAW?
LOOK!

717
00:29:00,038 --> 00:29:02,942
HUH? UH,
THAT'S THE OCEAN, KENNY.

718
00:29:04,243 --> 00:29:06,847
I DON'T SEE ANYTHING.

719
00:29:06,880 --> 00:29:09,148
YOU'RE SEEING THINGS.

720
00:29:09,182 --> 00:29:10,550
[EARTH RUMBLES]

721
00:29:10,583 --> 00:29:11,852
OH, NOW YOU'RE
FEELING THINGS.

722
00:29:11,885 --> 00:29:13,085
KENNY, STOP IT.

723
00:29:13,118 --> 00:29:15,255
KENNY, NORA!

724
00:29:15,288 --> 00:29:16,322
- QUIT SHAKING.
- WHAT'S GOING ON?

725
00:29:16,355 --> 00:29:18,123
LOOK, DADDY!

726
00:29:20,393 --> 00:29:21,962
WHAT'S ALL THIS ABOUT

727
00:29:21,995 --> 00:29:25,432
NOT LETTING KENNY
KEEP HIS TURTLE?

728
00:29:25,465 --> 00:29:27,000
GAMERA.

729
00:29:27,033 --> 00:29:28,968
- GAMERA!
- GAMERA!

730
00:29:29,002 --> 00:29:31,103
GAMERA! GET THE CAMERA!

731
00:29:31,137 --> 00:29:33,138
[SERVO CHUCKLES]
LITTLE PLAY ON WORDS.

732
00:29:33,172 --> 00:29:35,808
- KENNY!
- NO, KENNY'S OVER THERE.

733
00:29:35,842 --> 00:29:37,310
THAT'S GAMERA.

734
00:29:42,482 --> 00:29:44,450
[GAMERA ROARS]

735
00:29:44,483 --> 00:29:47,353
OH, HE WANTS TO MARRY
A LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER.

736
00:29:47,387 --> 00:29:49,388
AAH!

737
00:29:49,422 --> 00:29:52,825
KENNY!

738
00:29:52,858 --> 00:29:55,595
- HEY, HEY.
- [ALL] JUMP! JUMP! JUMP!

739
00:29:55,628 --> 00:29:56,528
- JUMP! JUMP!
- JUMP!

740
00:29:56,562 --> 00:29:59,565
N-- GO, DROP!

741
00:29:59,598 --> 00:30:02,368
- DADDY!
- JINX.

742
00:30:02,402 --> 00:30:05,405
- DON'T YOU CRUSH ME!
- DADDY!

743
00:30:05,438 --> 00:30:07,507
SLIP! COME ON! FALL, SLIP!

744
00:30:07,540 --> 00:30:09,108
AAH!

745
00:30:09,142 --> 00:30:11,077
I WILL PET HIM AND HUG HIM

746
00:30:11,110 --> 00:30:14,047
AND SQUEEZE HIM
AND CALL HIM GEORGE.

747
00:30:21,353 --> 00:30:22,522
- HE ALL RIGHT?
- AAH.

748
00:30:22,555 --> 00:30:24,990
KENNY! KENNY!

749
00:30:25,023 --> 00:30:26,325
- KENNY--
- YEAH, QUICK,

750
00:30:26,358 --> 00:30:28,427
MOVE HIS SPINE AROUND,
HE'S HAD A BAD FALL.

751
00:30:28,460 --> 00:30:30,230
KENNY!

752
00:30:30,263 --> 00:30:31,865
HUH?

753
00:30:31,898 --> 00:30:34,300
- [GAMERA ROARS]
- KENNY!

754
00:30:34,333 --> 00:30:36,468
I LOVE YOU!

755
00:30:36,502 --> 00:30:39,372
HMM.

756
00:30:39,405 --> 00:30:41,340
KENNY, KENNY.

757
00:30:41,373 --> 00:30:43,977
YOU'RE SAFE NOW.
YOU'RE SAFE NOW.

758
00:30:44,010 --> 00:30:45,278
KENNY, WHAT IS IT?

759
00:30:45,312 --> 00:30:49,248
I'M PARALYZED
FROM THE NECK DOWN!

760
00:30:49,282 --> 00:30:51,450
AH.

761
00:30:51,483 --> 00:30:53,018
I WAS SO SCARED.

762
00:30:53,052 --> 00:30:54,620
GAMERA SAVED ME, DIDN'T HE?

763
00:30:54,653 --> 00:30:56,055
- YES.
- SURE HE DID.

764
00:30:56,088 --> 00:30:58,157
- GAMERA SAVED YOUR LIFE.
- YEAH, OF COURSE.

765
00:30:58,190 --> 00:31:00,393
- YOU CAN KEEP HIM AS A PET.
- BECAUSE HE KNOWS
I LIKE TURTLES.

766
00:31:00,427 --> 00:31:02,362
THAT'S RIGHT, HE'S A NICE
TURTLE, YOU LITTLE LOON.

767
00:31:02,395 --> 00:31:03,963
GAMERA MUST HAVE
A GOOD HEART.

768
00:31:03,997 --> 00:31:06,032
YES, GAMERA'S A GOOD TURTLE.

769
00:31:06,065 --> 00:31:08,033
- YEAH, WHATEVER.
- YES, HE IS GOOD.

770
00:31:08,067 --> 00:31:09,468
HE IS GOOD.

771
00:31:09,502 --> 00:31:10,970
YES, HE IS.

772
00:31:11,003 --> 00:31:12,605
OW, MY SPINE!

773
00:31:15,375 --> 00:31:16,542
EXCUSE ME, DR. HIDAKA.

774
00:31:16,575 --> 00:31:18,077
I HAVE THIS STABBING PAIN
IN MY BACK.

775
00:31:18,110 --> 00:31:19,345
...TELL US WHAT YOUR
NEXT EXPEDITION IS.

776
00:31:19,378 --> 00:31:20,480
NO, I DON'T KNOW YET.

777
00:31:20,513 --> 00:31:23,348
WILL YOU BE RETURNING
TO THE ARCTIC ON ANOTHER SHIP?

778
00:31:23,382 --> 00:31:25,050
DR. HIDAKA IS WANTED
ON THE TELEPHONE.

779
00:31:25,083 --> 00:31:26,452
EXCUSE ME, I MUST
TAKE THAT CALL.

780
00:31:26,485 --> 00:31:29,188
I'M REALLY HAPPENING
RIGHT NOW, PARDON ME.

781
00:31:29,222 --> 00:31:30,690
- THERE YOU ARE, SIR.
- THANK YOU.

782
00:31:30,723 --> 00:31:32,225
UH, KENNY'S BEEN
BADLY WOUNDED.

783
00:31:32,258 --> 00:31:33,993
YOU MAY WANT
TO KNOW ABOUT IT.

784
00:31:34,027 --> 00:31:36,028
HE'S BEEN REALLY HURT.

785
00:31:36,062 --> 00:31:37,930
- HE REALLY IS.
- THAT'S FANTASTIC, YES,
I'LL COME RIGHT AWAY.

786
00:31:37,963 --> 00:31:40,032
BOY, I'M REALLY SURPRISED
THAT YOU--

787
00:31:40,065 --> 00:31:42,068
IT'S INCREDIBLE--
THAT WAS THE UNIVERSITY.

788
00:31:42,102 --> 00:31:43,637
- SPIELBERG OFFERED HIM $250.
- GAMERA HAS JUST BEEN SIGHTED

789
00:31:43,670 --> 00:31:45,438
- NEAR HOKKAIDO.
- [THEY GASP]

790
00:31:45,472 --> 00:31:47,007
- PLEASE ARRANGE
FOR PLANE TICKETS.
- YES.

791
00:31:47,040 --> 00:31:48,473
DR. HIDAKA, MAY I--

792
00:31:48,507 --> 00:31:49,708
I'LL SEE YOU VERY SHORTLY.

793
00:31:49,742 --> 00:31:51,677
- DR. HIDAKA!
- BUT DOCTOR, I LOVE YOU!

794
00:31:51,710 --> 00:31:53,312
MORE AND MORE REPORTS
ARE COMING IN

795
00:31:53,345 --> 00:31:56,282
ABOUT THE DEVASTATION
CAUSED BY GAMERA.

796
00:31:56,315 --> 00:31:58,550
THOUGHT SOME OF THESE
COME FROM UNRELIABLE SOURCES.

797
00:31:58,583 --> 00:32:00,653
- LIKE KENNY?
- GAMERA IS SAID
TO BE SEEN EVERYWHERE.

798
00:32:00,687 --> 00:32:02,388
MORE ABOUT GAMERA.

799
00:32:02,422 --> 00:32:03,422
...DOES HE DISAPPEAR
IN ONE AREA--

800
00:32:03,455 --> 00:32:06,458
- IS KENNY SLEEPING?
- YES, HE WAS VERY TIRED.

801
00:32:06,492 --> 00:32:08,662
- ... COMPLETELY
OPPOSITE DIRECTION.
- AWW.

802
00:32:10,597 --> 00:32:14,467
SOUNDS LIKE CHARO MUSIC.

803
00:32:14,500 --> 00:32:17,070
KENNY, ALTHOUGH
CONSIDERED CHUNKY,

804
00:32:17,103 --> 00:32:20,507
IS QUITE AGILE.

805
00:32:20,540 --> 00:32:22,242
[SERVO HUMS ALONG]

806
00:32:22,275 --> 00:32:24,077
OH, IT'S TIBBY'S BURIAL MOUND.

807
00:32:24,110 --> 00:32:26,445
SHUT UP! THAT'S NOT FUNNY.

808
00:32:26,478 --> 00:32:28,280
YOU THERE?

809
00:32:28,313 --> 00:32:30,282
OH, TIBBY.

810
00:32:30,317 --> 00:32:31,483
TIBBY?

811
00:32:31,517 --> 00:32:33,118
OR NOT TIBBY.

812
00:32:33,152 --> 00:32:34,553
IT'S NOT-- STOP IT.
SHUT UP.

813
00:32:34,587 --> 00:32:37,690
- TIBBY?
- TIBBY?

814
00:32:37,723 --> 00:32:39,158
TIBBY?

815
00:32:39,192 --> 00:32:41,360
SQUISH! OH, TIBBY.

816
00:32:41,393 --> 00:32:43,028
THAT'S NOT FUNNY!
JOEL, TELL HIM TO STOP!

817
00:32:43,062 --> 00:32:45,097
TIBBY! TIBBY!

818
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:47,167
WHAT'RE YOU WORRIED ABOUT?
TIBBY'S LONG-DEAD, TOM.

819
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:50,235
- TIBBY?
- I'M LEAVING, I CAN'T...
THIS IS TERRIBLE.

820
00:32:50,268 --> 00:32:52,138
COME ON BACK, COME ON.

821
00:32:52,172 --> 00:32:54,673
- WILL YOU STOP
WITH THE JOKES?
- YEP.

822
00:32:54,707 --> 00:32:58,410
TIBBY?

823
00:32:58,443 --> 00:33:01,047
TIBBY?

824
00:33:01,080 --> 00:33:04,483
♪ AND TIBBY, I MISS YOU ♪

825
00:33:04,517 --> 00:33:07,420
HOW DOES HE EXPECT TIBBY
TO SIGNAL HIM? LIGHT A FLARE?

826
00:33:07,453 --> 00:33:09,488
JEEZ.

827
00:33:09,522 --> 00:33:10,790
TIBBY?

828
00:33:10,823 --> 00:33:14,360
TIBBY?

829
00:33:14,393 --> 00:33:17,363
- OH.
- TIBBY, WHY ARE YOU HIDING?

830
00:33:17,397 --> 00:33:19,765
I DON'T HAVE THE MONEY
I OWE YOU, MAN.

831
00:33:19,798 --> 00:33:22,535
NOW LISTEN, I'LL BE
BACK FOR YOU TOMORROW.

832
00:33:22,568 --> 00:33:24,303
RULE NUMBER TWO?
NEVER WORK WITH CHILDREN.

833
00:33:26,838 --> 00:33:29,642
MAN, THEY'VE BEEN
ON THAT PLANE FOR 48 HOURS.

834
00:33:29,675 --> 00:33:32,778
LUCKILY, THE IN-FLIGHT FILM
IS BERLIN ALEXANDERPLATZ.

835
00:33:32,812 --> 00:33:34,713
- HI!
- [ALL] AAH!
- DON'T DO THAT.

836
00:33:34,747 --> 00:33:36,315
HOW DID YOU GET HERE?

837
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:38,117
IT WASN'T VERY FRIENDLY
OF THE TWO OF YOU

838
00:33:38,150 --> 00:33:39,818
- TO GIVE ME THE SLIP.
- AND MAKE ME WEAR IT.

839
00:33:39,852 --> 00:33:42,155
DIDN'T THEY MISS YOU
BACK AT YOUR OFFICE?

840
00:33:42,188 --> 00:33:44,557
NOPE, I'M SUPPOSED
TO COVER THE GAMERA STORY.

841
00:33:44,590 --> 00:33:46,125
MY ARM-BAND FOR THE AIRPORT.

842
00:33:46,158 --> 00:33:47,560
IT CLASHES WITH MY TIE.

843
00:33:47,593 --> 00:33:49,428
CATHERINE, YOU'RE
STILL MY INSPIRATION.

844
00:33:49,462 --> 00:33:51,297
I'LL FOLLOW YOU ANYWHERE.
ANYWHERE!

845
00:33:51,330 --> 00:33:52,798
I'LL SLAP A RESTRAINING ORDER
ON YOU.

846
00:33:52,832 --> 00:33:54,133
WHAT'S THE LATEST ON GAMERA?

847
00:33:54,167 --> 00:33:56,602
- STILL NOT FOUND.
- HMM.

848
00:33:56,635 --> 00:33:58,772
WE MUST FIND HIM SOON,

849
00:33:58,805 --> 00:34:00,607
OR THERE'LL BE CHAOS
EVERYWHERE.

850
00:34:00,640 --> 00:34:02,508
LET'S SEE, THERE'S, UM,

851
00:34:02,542 --> 00:34:04,743
CHAOS HERE, CHAOS THERE.

852
00:34:04,777 --> 00:34:06,245
UH... HMM.

853
00:34:06,278 --> 00:34:08,113
HE'S RIGHT,
CHAOS EVERYWHERE.

854
00:34:08,147 --> 00:34:09,782
- FELLAS?
CHECK THIS OUT-- CHAOS.

855
00:34:09,815 --> 00:34:12,452
- WHAT'S THAT NOISE?
- I DON'T KNOW,
MAYBE AN EARTH TREMOR.

856
00:34:12,485 --> 00:34:13,753
TRY TO TRACE IT.

857
00:34:13,787 --> 00:34:15,220
AND TRY TO DRESS THE SAME.

858
00:34:22,195 --> 00:34:24,097
GAMERA SIGHTED.

859
00:34:24,130 --> 00:34:25,732
HEADING FOR THE GEOTHERMAL
POWER PLANT.

860
00:34:25,765 --> 00:34:27,567
AND HE'S WITH HELEN HAYES.

861
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:29,402
COME IN, COME IN!
COME IN!

862
00:34:29,435 --> 00:34:32,205
GAMERA SIGHTED! COME IN!

863
00:34:32,238 --> 00:34:34,173
FOLLOW ME.
TO EMERGENCY STATIONS!

864
00:34:34,207 --> 00:34:35,575
QUICK.

865
00:34:35,608 --> 00:34:37,577
AND LET'S REMEMBER TO CALL
EACH OTHER IN THE MORNING.

866
00:34:37,610 --> 00:34:39,545
- WE ALL WORE
THE SAME THING.
- CAREFUL!

867
00:34:39,578 --> 00:34:40,780
DON'T GET TOO CLOSE.

868
00:34:40,813 --> 00:34:42,715
HOLD IT!

869
00:34:42,748 --> 00:34:45,818
NOW, HOLD IT UP
TO THE LIGHT.

870
00:34:45,852 --> 00:34:48,220
- FLY'S OPEN.
- THANK YOU-- OH, DARN.

871
00:34:51,357 --> 00:34:53,458
- HELLO.
- HI, HOW YOU DOING? HI.

872
00:34:55,462 --> 00:34:57,297
HOW DO YOU DO, COMMANDER?

873
00:34:57,330 --> 00:34:58,898
- I'M DOCTOR HIDAKA,
TOKYO UNIVERSITY.
- OH, I DO ALL RIGHT.

874
00:34:58,932 --> 00:35:01,367
- HELLO.
- AND I'M HIS ASSISTANT.

875
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:04,370
- WHO ARE YOU?
- OH, I'M FROM
A TOKYO NEWSPAPER.

876
00:35:04,403 --> 00:35:07,407
I'M SORRY, BUT REPORTERS
ARE NOT ALLOWED HERE.

877
00:35:07,440 --> 00:35:09,242
- EXCUSE ME, COMMANDER--
- BUT I'M A BAD REPORTER.

878
00:35:09,275 --> 00:35:10,543
BUT THIS GENTLEMAN
IS A FRIEND.

879
00:35:10,577 --> 00:35:13,312
HE WAS ON THE ARCTIC
EXPEDITION WITH US,

880
00:35:13,345 --> 00:35:16,248
AND HE KNOWS A GREAT DEAL
ABOUT GAMERA.

881
00:35:16,282 --> 00:35:17,717
I'M SURE YOU'LL
FIND HIS PRESENCE

882
00:35:17,750 --> 00:35:19,485
AND COLLABORATION
VERY USEFUL.

883
00:35:19,518 --> 00:35:22,588
OH, I SEE, YOU CAN STAY THEN.
YOU CAN START.

884
00:35:22,622 --> 00:35:24,257
- YES, SIR.
- OOH, MAY I?

885
00:35:24,290 --> 00:35:25,925
YESTERDAY MORNING,
GAMERA DESTROYED

886
00:35:25,958 --> 00:35:28,160
A LIGHTHOUSE
NEAR THIS SEAPORT.

887
00:35:28,193 --> 00:35:29,862
AND RIGHT AFTERWARDS,

888
00:35:29,895 --> 00:35:31,597
- IT DIVED INTO THE SEA.
- DOVE.

889
00:35:31,630 --> 00:35:34,400
THEN IT WAS SEEN HEADING FOR
THE GEOTHERMAL POWER PLANT.

890
00:35:34,433 --> 00:35:36,635
A GEOTHERMAL POWER PLANT?
WHAT IS THAT?

891
00:35:36,668 --> 00:35:38,603
ALLOW ME TO EXPLAIN.

892
00:35:38,637 --> 00:35:41,373
HE WHO HOLDS THE POINTER
GETS TO THE TOP.

893
00:35:41,407 --> 00:35:44,577
...AND HIGH TEMPERATURE VAPORS
USED TO RISE FROM BELOW.

894
00:35:44,610 --> 00:35:46,312
BY DRILLING
THROUGH THE VOLCANO,

895
00:35:46,345 --> 00:35:48,813
WE TRAP STEAM AT
1,000 DEGREES CENTIGRADE.

896
00:35:48,848 --> 00:35:50,750
AND GENERATE ELECTRICITY
WITH IT.

897
00:35:50,783 --> 00:35:52,552
YOU MEAN THE STEAM
ACTUALLY REACHES

898
00:35:52,585 --> 00:35:54,353
A THOUSAND DEGREES
CENTIGRADE?

899
00:35:54,387 --> 00:35:56,222
MM, HOTTER THAN
THE SANTA MONICA FREEWAY,

900
00:35:56,255 --> 00:35:57,590
BUFFALO DRIVE.

901
00:35:57,623 --> 00:36:00,392
...HIGH INTENSITY TEMPERATURES,
DON'T YOU THINK--

902
00:36:00,425 --> 00:36:02,295
WRONG AGAIN, PONY-BREATH.

903
00:36:02,328 --> 00:36:04,730
- ...DESTROY GAMERA?
- I'M NOT SO SURE
IT'S POSSIBLE.

904
00:36:04,763 --> 00:36:08,600
GAMERA HAS SURVIVED
EVEN AFTER ATOMIC RADIATION,

905
00:36:08,633 --> 00:36:10,837
AND A THOUSAND DEGREES
WOULDN'T AFFECT HIM.

906
00:36:10,870 --> 00:36:12,805
DR. HIDAKA,
DO YOU KNOW OF ANY

907
00:36:12,838 --> 00:36:14,607
COUNTER-MEASURES
TO DESTROY HIM?

908
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:16,508
NO, NOT YET.

909
00:36:16,542 --> 00:36:18,210
WHAT'S THE STATION'S
MAXIMUM CAPACITY?

910
00:36:18,243 --> 00:36:19,845
ABOUT 350,000 KILOWATTS.

911
00:36:19,878 --> 00:36:23,282
WELL-SPOKEN, MY FAITHFUL
INDIAN COMPANION.

912
00:36:23,315 --> 00:36:24,550
THERE'S JUST A CHANCE
IT MIGHT WORK.

913
00:36:24,583 --> 00:36:25,618
THANKS, JOHNNY.

914
00:36:33,358 --> 00:36:36,262
MM, WELCOME BACK
TO OUR TEA-TIME MOVIE.

915
00:36:36,295 --> 00:36:37,997
TED BESSELL
AND GEORGIE JESSEL

916
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:40,667
IN LANCE THE WONDER DOG.

917
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:42,335
[SERVO CLEARS THROAT]

918
00:36:42,368 --> 00:36:43,802
STOP. PLEASE.

919
00:36:43,835 --> 00:36:46,472
- COMMANDER.
- YOU CAN BE REPLACED
BY LENO, YOU KNOW.

920
00:36:46,505 --> 00:36:48,440
COMMANDER HERE, WHAT IS IT?

921
00:36:48,473 --> 00:36:49,675
WE'RE READY, STANDING BY.

922
00:36:49,708 --> 00:36:51,910
ROGER.

923
00:36:51,943 --> 00:36:54,680
OH, JUST DOING SOME
SIGHT-SEEING.

924
00:36:57,850 --> 00:36:59,752
EVERYTHING'S SET.
WE CAN ATTACK NOW, DOCTOR.

925
00:36:59,785 --> 00:37:01,553
IT'S SO BUMPY.

926
00:37:01,587 --> 00:37:03,255
MAYBE WE CAN DO IT
WITHOUT A SHOT.

927
00:37:03,288 --> 00:37:04,623
IT'LL BE A LOT BETTER
FOR ALL.

928
00:37:04,657 --> 00:37:06,625
YOU THINK WE CAN?

929
00:37:06,658 --> 00:37:08,460
[ALARM RINGS]

930
00:37:08,493 --> 00:37:09,695
QUITTIN' TIME AT THE QUARRY!

931
00:37:09,728 --> 00:37:11,830
YABBA-DABBA-DOO!

932
00:37:14,700 --> 00:37:16,335
SOUNDS LIKE FLINTSTONES,
YOU SEE.

933
00:37:16,368 --> 00:37:19,705
- MM-HMM. I GOT IT.
- OKAY.

934
00:37:19,738 --> 00:37:20,973
THOUGHT IT WAS A STRETCH.

935
00:37:21,007 --> 00:37:24,410
- EVERYTHING READY?
- YES, SIR.

936
00:37:24,443 --> 00:37:26,012
WOULD YOU GUYS HURRY UP?

937
00:37:26,045 --> 00:37:28,047
HERE YOU ARE, SIR.

938
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:30,315
- THANK YOU.
- IT'S APPROACHING
THE WIRES.

939
00:37:32,485 --> 00:37:34,020
THROW THE SWITCHES!

940
00:37:34,053 --> 00:37:36,755
100,000 KILOWATTS!

941
00:37:36,788 --> 00:37:38,523
PUMP UP THE VOLUME!

942
00:37:38,557 --> 00:37:41,060
THROW THE SWITCHES AGAIN.
THIS TIME, MAXIMUM POWER.

943
00:37:41,093 --> 00:37:44,530
HEY, I DID ALREADY. WHAT?

944
00:37:44,563 --> 00:37:46,432
OOH.

945
00:37:46,465 --> 00:37:48,567
THE ELECTRICAL SHOCKS DON'T
SEEM TO BOTHER GAMERA AT ALL.

946
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:49,968
INCREDIBLE.

947
00:37:50,002 --> 00:37:51,870
HMM, AND I WAS COUNTING
VERY HEAVILY ON THEM.

948
00:37:51,903 --> 00:37:53,338
...STRONGER THAN BEFORE.

949
00:37:53,372 --> 00:37:55,642
AS IF THE ELECTRICITY
GIVES IT RENEWED ENERGY.

950
00:37:55,675 --> 00:37:57,643
OH, SHUT UP.

951
00:37:57,677 --> 00:37:59,612
IT CHARGES IT
LIKE A BATTERY.

952
00:37:59,645 --> 00:38:00,980
- COMMANDER?
- YES, SIR?

953
00:38:01,013 --> 00:38:03,648
- I THINK YOU
SHOULD ATTACK NOW.
- YES, SIR.

954
00:38:03,682 --> 00:38:04,983
- I'VE GOTTA GET A SANDWICH.
- ATTACK!

955
00:38:05,017 --> 00:38:08,520
YES, SIR.
FIRE ALL CANNONS!

956
00:38:08,553 --> 00:38:09,988
OOH!

957
00:38:12,425 --> 00:38:13,458
TURTLE STORM.

958
00:38:13,492 --> 00:38:16,528
OOPS! I'M CLUMSY, SORRY.

959
00:38:16,562 --> 00:38:19,698
SORRY. I'M SORRY.

960
00:38:19,732 --> 00:38:21,967
GAMERA,
STEAMING MAD AT DIRT.

961
00:38:25,805 --> 00:38:27,873
THREE MILE ISLAND.
THE REAL STORY.

962
00:38:30,977 --> 00:38:33,645
OH, HAH, I'M SO...

963
00:38:33,678 --> 00:38:35,013
WHERE ARE THOSE KEYS?
[CROW CHUCKLES]

964
00:38:38,483 --> 00:38:39,985
SLOW.

965
00:38:40,018 --> 00:38:41,653
I CAN NEVER
FIND SHOES THAT FIT.

966
00:38:41,687 --> 00:38:43,822
- HE'S HARD ON SHOES.
- OH, THAT ONE.

967
00:38:43,855 --> 00:38:45,423
- YEP.
- THAT ONE.

968
00:38:52,898 --> 00:38:54,133
BIG TROUBLE.

969
00:38:54,167 --> 00:38:55,667
BULLETS BOUNCE RIGHT OFF.

970
00:38:58,737 --> 00:39:00,038
[GAMERA ROARS]

971
00:39:00,072 --> 00:39:02,508
KENNY!

972
00:39:02,542 --> 00:39:04,043
GUY...

973
00:39:10,448 --> 00:39:11,883
KENNY...

974
00:39:11,917 --> 00:39:14,853
DOESN'T HE KIND OF LOOK LIKE
GODZILLA WITH A BACKPACK ON?

975
00:39:14,887 --> 00:39:16,488
- YEAH.
- JUST A LITTLE BIT.

976
00:39:18,957 --> 00:39:21,393
[CROW SLURPS]

977
00:39:21,427 --> 00:39:23,728
REALLY MAKES YOU THINK,
DON'T IT?

978
00:39:23,762 --> 00:39:26,098
COMMANDER, IT LOOKS
LIKE WE FAILED.

979
00:39:26,132 --> 00:39:28,433
WE MUST FIND
A STRONGER WEAPON.

980
00:39:28,467 --> 00:39:30,535
I'LL HAVE TO GO BACK
TO THE UNIVERSITY.

981
00:39:30,568 --> 00:39:32,505
- YOU STAY HERE.
- YES, BUT--
- DON'T WORRY--

982
00:39:32,538 --> 00:39:34,107
IS THAT THE ORKIN MAN
BACK THERE IN THE BACK?

983
00:39:34,140 --> 00:39:35,875
...CONSULT A COLLEAGUE,
AND IN THE MEANTIME,

984
00:39:35,908 --> 00:39:37,777
I WANT YOU TO EVACUATE
EVERYBODY.

985
00:39:37,810 --> 00:39:39,578
- UNDERSTAND, COMMANDER?
- YES, SIR.
- GOOD, THANK YOU.

986
00:39:39,612 --> 00:39:41,980
MEANWHILE, AT JACKIE CHAN
TECHNICAL COLLEGE.

987
00:39:43,982 --> 00:39:47,687
AND THAT'S HOW THINGS DONE,
PROFESSOR MURASE.

988
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:49,888
HMM, SO, EXTRA CRISPY
OR REGULAR?

989
00:39:49,922 --> 00:39:53,558
...LEGENDS DID MENTION
FIRE-EATING TURTLES.

990
00:39:53,592 --> 00:39:55,560
BUT IN THE 20TH CENTURY,

991
00:39:55,593 --> 00:39:58,730
I MUST ADMIT IT'S
VERY DIFFICULT TO BELIEVE.

992
00:39:58,763 --> 00:39:59,965
BUT IT'S TRUE.

993
00:39:59,998 --> 00:40:01,767
GAMERA DOESN'T SEEM
TO HAVE ANY WEAKNESS.

994
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:02,968
EXCEPT FOR BETTING ON DOGS.

995
00:40:03,002 --> 00:40:04,837
THERE IS SOMETHING I CAN SAY.

996
00:40:04,870 --> 00:40:06,638
[SERVO MUMBLES]

997
00:40:06,672 --> 00:40:08,940
GAMERA'S BODY MUST BE
STRONGER THAN METAL.

998
00:40:08,973 --> 00:40:10,508
AND IF THAT'S TRUE,
THE SITUATION

999
00:40:10,542 --> 00:40:12,912
IS EVEN MORE SERIOUS
THAN WE THOUGHT.

1000
00:40:12,945 --> 00:40:14,980
IT HAS THE POWER
TO CONVERT ORGANIC MATTER

1001
00:40:15,013 --> 00:40:16,882
- INTO INORGANIC MATTER.
- LIKE McDONALDS.

1002
00:40:16,915 --> 00:40:18,050
AND THAT MEANS
NUCLEAR WEAPONS

1003
00:40:18,083 --> 00:40:19,885
ARE TOTALLY USELESS
AGAINST IT.

1004
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:21,920
- YES, THAT'S IT.
- QUITE.

1005
00:40:21,953 --> 00:40:24,490
THE ENERGY PRODUCED
BY NUCLEAR EXPLOSIONS

1006
00:40:24,523 --> 00:40:26,058
ONLY SEEMS TO REVITALIZE IT,

1007
00:40:26,092 --> 00:40:27,893
GIVING IT UNLIMITED
ENERGY RESOURCES.

1008
00:40:27,927 --> 00:40:30,028
- SOME JERKY?
- MM, PICKLED EGGS.

1009
00:40:30,062 --> 00:40:33,232
...FIND SOME COUNTER-FORCE
THAT WILL NEUTRALIZE IT, RIGHT?

1010
00:40:33,265 --> 00:40:36,468
AND AS FOR THE MARKINGS
ON THIS STONE HERE,

1011
00:40:36,502 --> 00:40:38,570
I'M NOT SURE
THEY REPRESENT WAVES.

1012
00:40:38,603 --> 00:40:40,105
BUT THE ESKIMO
SAID THEY WERE.

1013
00:40:40,138 --> 00:40:42,040
- OH, WHAT DO THEY KNOW?
- THE ESKIMO WAS ONLY

1014
00:40:42,073 --> 00:40:44,543
REPEATING OLD STORIES
AND FOLK TALES.

1015
00:40:44,577 --> 00:40:47,713
BUT PERHAPS THESE CARVINGS
CAN UNRAVEL A GREAT MYSTERY.

1016
00:40:47,747 --> 00:40:50,548
THE SECRET INGREDIENT IN K.C.
MASTERPIECE BARBECUE SAUCE.

1017
00:40:50,582 --> 00:40:52,885
IT'S ROGER RAMJET
AND HIS AMERICAN EAGLES!

1018
00:40:55,053 --> 00:40:56,622
KENNY!

1019
00:40:56,655 --> 00:40:58,857
MY DARLING KENNY!

1020
00:40:58,890 --> 00:41:01,560
HE'S IN PAIN, ISN'T HE?

1021
00:41:01,593 --> 00:41:03,862
[ALL MAKE SLURPING SOUNDS]

1022
00:41:05,865 --> 00:41:09,168
COMMANDER, I BELIEVE WE OUGHT
TO CALL U.N. HEADQUARTERS.

1023
00:41:09,202 --> 00:41:11,970
OH, SO YOU'RE IN CHARGE NOW?

1024
00:41:12,003 --> 00:41:13,205
YOU'RE RIGHT.

1025
00:41:13,238 --> 00:41:14,740
CONTACT THEM IMMEDIATELY.

1026
00:41:14,773 --> 00:41:15,908
- YES, SIR.
- OH, RIGHT,

1027
00:41:15,942 --> 00:41:17,242
"GOOD MORNING. YEAH, U.N.?

1028
00:41:17,275 --> 00:41:18,677
"THIS IS JOE
DOWN AT THE BASE.

1029
00:41:18,710 --> 00:41:20,847
CAN WE USE YOUR
MISSILES? NOT!"

1030
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:22,180
- GOOD MORNING!
- RISE AND SHINE.

1031
00:41:22,213 --> 00:41:25,683
GOOD MORNING, EVERYBODY.

1032
00:41:25,717 --> 00:41:27,587
GO, GAMERA!

1033
00:41:27,620 --> 00:41:28,753
GO AWAY, GAMERA!

1034
00:41:28,787 --> 00:41:30,755
OH, PUT A SOCK IN IT, KID!
HE'S FISH-FOOD.

1035
00:41:30,788 --> 00:41:32,558
NO!

1036
00:41:33,925 --> 00:41:35,793
- I'M DOCTOR MURASE.
- SIR.

1037
00:41:35,827 --> 00:41:36,695
- HAVE YOU ALL
YOUR WEAPONS--
- I'M THE COLONEL.

1038
00:41:36,728 --> 00:41:38,163
YES, SIR. I GUARANTEE

1039
00:41:38,197 --> 00:41:40,665
THAT GAMERA WON'T
ESCAPE US AGAIN.

1040
00:41:40,698 --> 00:41:43,602
- WE HAVE EVEN REQUESTED EXTRA
MISSILES FROM THE U.S. FORCES.
- UH-HUH.

1041
00:41:43,635 --> 00:41:45,770
COMMANDER, ALL THE MISSILES
ARE IN FIRING POSITION.

1042
00:41:45,803 --> 00:41:48,007
GOOD, START FIRING.

1043
00:41:48,040 --> 00:41:49,242
- IF YOU REMEMBER
THE COLONEL, WHY COOK?

1044
00:41:49,275 --> 00:41:52,177
DON'T SHOOT GAMERA!

1045
00:41:52,210 --> 00:41:53,912
DON'T SHOOT GAMERA!

1046
00:41:53,945 --> 00:41:55,180
HE'S GOOD, HE'S GOOD!

1047
00:41:55,213 --> 00:41:56,682
LET'S LISTEN TO WHAT
KENNY HAS TO SAY.

1048
00:41:56,715 --> 00:41:59,585
YES, IT MIGHT BE A MISTAKE.

1049
00:41:59,618 --> 00:42:02,253
MAYBE WE SHOULDN'T
USE THOSE MISSILES.

1050
00:42:02,287 --> 00:42:04,623
WHY NOT? IT'S THE ONLY WAY
TO KILL THAT MONSTER.

1051
00:42:04,657 --> 00:42:05,790
BECAUSE KENNY SAID SO.

1052
00:42:05,823 --> 00:42:07,993
GAMERA IS A CREATURE
THAT FEEDS ON FIRE.

1053
00:42:08,027 --> 00:42:09,295
USING MISSILES WOULD
NOT DO ANY GOOD.

1054
00:42:09,328 --> 00:42:11,597
IT WOULD ONLY CAUSE
UNNECESSARY DESTRUCTION.

1055
00:42:11,630 --> 00:42:14,032
NO, DON'T USE MISSILES.

1056
00:42:14,065 --> 00:42:16,268
I SEE. SERGEANT?
CALL IT OFF.

1057
00:42:16,302 --> 00:42:18,303
- YES, SIR.
- HUH.

1058
00:42:18,337 --> 00:42:20,940
- JUST LIKE THAT, HUH?
- SIR, THANKS A LOT.

1059
00:42:20,973 --> 00:42:22,808
GAMERA SAVED MY LIFE
FOR ME, ONCE.

1060
00:42:22,842 --> 00:42:25,843
YEAH, GREAT.
GUARDS? GUARDS?

1061
00:42:25,877 --> 00:42:27,847
GAMERA IS A GOOD TURTLE,
ISN'T HE, SIR?

1062
00:42:27,880 --> 00:42:29,982
WELL, SON, I JUST PRAY
THAT YOU'RE RIGHT.

1063
00:42:30,015 --> 00:42:31,650
YEP, WHAT HE'S DONE TODAY

1064
00:42:31,683 --> 00:42:34,820
HAS BEEN A BENEFIT
TO ALL, KENNY.

1065
00:42:34,853 --> 00:42:36,322
[SERVO WHISTLES]

1066
00:42:36,355 --> 00:42:37,923
- HEY, SATURDAY
MYSTERY MOVIE!
- COMMANDER?

1067
00:42:37,957 --> 00:42:39,190
- WHAT IS IT?
- THEY PUT PEPPERONI
ON YOUR PIZZA.

1068
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:41,593
THE PLANT
IS COMPLETELY DESTROYED.

1069
00:42:41,627 --> 00:42:42,795
I TOLD YOU
TO WATER THE PLANT!

1070
00:42:42,828 --> 00:42:45,363
- I SEE.
- YOU'RE FIRED.

1071
00:42:45,397 --> 00:42:47,733
YOU HEARD THAT, DOCTOR.
EVERYTHING'S DESTROYED.

1072
00:42:47,767 --> 00:42:49,935
THERE'S NOTHING WE CAN DO
AGAINST SUCH TERRIFYING FORCES--

1073
00:42:49,968 --> 00:42:51,370
EXCEPT HAVE ANOTHER DRINK.

1074
00:42:51,403 --> 00:42:53,972
DR. HIDAKA, IS THERE
ANYTHING ELSE WE CAN TRY?

1075
00:42:54,005 --> 00:42:56,108
- LOVE. WHAT ABOUT LOVE?
- THERE IS ONE THING

1076
00:42:56,142 --> 00:42:58,777
THAT HAS JUST
OCCURRED TO ME.

1077
00:42:58,810 --> 00:43:00,947
- IT'S LOVE.
- NATURE WORKS
IN MYSTERIOUS WAYS.

1078
00:43:00,980 --> 00:43:03,682
GAMERA IS A CREATURE
THAT FEEDS ON FIRE.

1079
00:43:03,715 --> 00:43:05,283
IT WITHSTANDS GREAT HEAT

1080
00:43:05,317 --> 00:43:07,920
I WONDERED IF IT WOULD
SUCCUMB TO THE OPPOSITE.

1081
00:43:07,953 --> 00:43:09,688
I MEAN VERY LOW
TEMPERATURES.

1082
00:43:09,722 --> 00:43:11,090
TEMPERATURES BELOW ZERO.

1083
00:43:11,123 --> 00:43:13,058
SOMETHING LIKE
A DEEP-FREEZE TREATMENT.

1084
00:43:13,092 --> 00:43:15,127
CARVEL!
MOST FRESH ICE CREAM

1085
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:16,662
- AT HOME.
- ...HAVEN'T USED YET.

1086
00:43:16,695 --> 00:43:19,030
- CUTE.
- THIS IS STILL
A MILITARY SECRET.

1087
00:43:19,063 --> 00:43:21,900
BUT THE ARMY HAS A BOMB THAT
CAN FREEZE JUST ABOUT ANYTHING.

1088
00:43:21,933 --> 00:43:24,202
YOU MEAN, IT CAN
REALLY FREEZE ANYTHING?

1089
00:43:24,235 --> 00:43:25,972
- YES.
- EVEN A MAN'S PASSION?

1090
00:43:26,005 --> 00:43:27,940
IT WAS ONLY
DEVELOPED RECENTLY.

1091
00:43:27,973 --> 00:43:29,642
THEY TRIED IT
IN THE JUNGLE TO FREEZE

1092
00:43:29,675 --> 00:43:31,377
ALL SORTS OF ANIMALS
AND PLANTS.

1093
00:43:31,410 --> 00:43:33,278
I THINK IT'S THE BEST CHANCE
WE'VE GOT LEFT.

1094
00:43:33,312 --> 00:43:34,813
SO I THINK WE SHOULD TRY IT.

1095
00:43:34,847 --> 00:43:36,648
- DO YOU AGREE?
- YES.

1096
00:43:36,682 --> 00:43:38,850
- MM, SURE, WHY NOT?
- I SEE.

1097
00:43:38,883 --> 00:43:40,418
DO YOU REALLY THINK
IT MIGHT WORK?

1098
00:43:40,452 --> 00:43:42,688
IT'S WORKED
VERY WELL SO FAR.

1099
00:43:42,722 --> 00:43:44,757
MM-HMM. COLONEL?

1100
00:43:44,790 --> 00:43:46,925
IN THAT CASE,
WE SHOULD USE IT

1101
00:43:46,958 --> 00:43:48,293
AGAINST GAMERA, COMMANDER.

1102
00:43:48,327 --> 00:43:50,295
- YES.
- THERE IS ONE THING.

1103
00:43:50,328 --> 00:43:52,998
- IT'S REALLY PRICEY.
- IT'S ONLY EFFECTIVE
FOR TEN MINUTES.

1104
00:43:53,032 --> 00:43:54,733
ONLY TEN MINUTES?

1105
00:43:54,767 --> 00:43:56,835
IT'S STILL EXPERIMENTAL,
AND AFTER THAT,

1106
00:43:56,868 --> 00:43:59,037
THINGS THAW QUICKLY.

1107
00:43:59,070 --> 00:44:02,107
SO WE'VE ONLY GOT TEN MINUTES
IN WHICH TO TRAP GAMERA.

1108
00:44:02,140 --> 00:44:03,308
SO IT'S TEN MINUTES, THEN.

1109
00:44:03,342 --> 00:44:06,012
WHAT HAPPENS IF GAMERA
REVIVES BEFOREHAND?

1110
00:44:06,045 --> 00:44:07,412
- FREEZER BURN.
- I DON'T KNOW.

1111
00:44:07,445 --> 00:44:08,980
IT'S A CHANCE
WE'VE GOT TO TAKE.

1112
00:44:09,013 --> 00:44:10,982
THEN IT'S TEN MINUTES.

1113
00:44:11,017 --> 00:44:14,185
NEXT WEEK ON SKY KING...

1114
00:44:14,218 --> 00:44:16,422
THAT GUY MOVES
LIKE GEORGE JEFFERSON.

1115
00:44:16,455 --> 00:44:18,190
- MM-HMM.
- YEAH.

1116
00:44:20,958 --> 00:44:22,862
GAMERA HAS STARTED MOVING.

1117
00:44:22,895 --> 00:44:24,730
AND A-GROOVIN'.
HE BE FUNKY.

1118
00:44:24,763 --> 00:44:26,465
- HE'S SHAKING HIS GROOVE THING.
- GAMERA IS MOVING.

1119
00:44:26,498 --> 00:44:28,333
[EQUIPMENT BEEPING]

1120
00:44:28,367 --> 00:44:30,035
DAMN.

1121
00:44:33,272 --> 00:44:34,807
WE MUSTN'T LOSE ANY TIME.

1122
00:44:34,840 --> 00:44:36,242
YES. YOU'RE RIGHT.

1123
00:44:36,275 --> 00:44:38,077
WE'VE ONLY TEN MINUTES,
NOT ANOTHER SECOND.

1124
00:44:38,110 --> 00:44:40,445
UH, IS THAT TEN MINUTES
STARTING NOW,

1125
00:44:40,478 --> 00:44:42,948
OR WHEN YOU WERE IN THE ROOM?

1126
00:44:42,982 --> 00:44:45,417
GAMERA HAS JUST STARTED
TO HEAD TOWARD DEVIL'S MOUNTAIN.

1127
00:44:45,450 --> 00:44:47,252
ROGER.

1128
00:44:47,285 --> 00:44:49,922
I JUST HOPE THIS PLAN'S
GOING TO WORK.

1129
00:44:49,955 --> 00:44:52,858
- THERE'S A RESORT TOWN BELOW.
- WE HAVE TO WORK QUICKLY.

1130
00:44:52,892 --> 00:44:54,993
WE'RE NEVER GONNA GET
ANY RESERVATIONS.

1131
00:44:55,027 --> 00:44:58,097
- MM-MM.
- I'M COMING, KENNY.

1132
00:44:59,398 --> 00:45:00,998
HI. HOW YOU DOIN'?

1133
00:45:03,335 --> 00:45:06,472
CIGARS! IT'S A BOY!

1134
00:45:06,505 --> 00:45:09,073
THE FREEZER BOMBS
ONLY LAST FOR TEN MINUTES.

1135
00:45:09,107 --> 00:45:12,410
- AND KIDS WANT MORE.
- WE HAVE TO DEACTIVATE GAMERA
WITHIN THAT TIME.

1136
00:45:12,443 --> 00:45:14,212
- IS THAT CLEAR?
- UH-HUH.

1137
00:45:14,245 --> 00:45:16,248
SO BE CAREFUL.
IF WE MAKE A MISTAKE,

1138
00:45:16,282 --> 00:45:17,850
THE WHOLE PLAN WILL FAIL.

1139
00:45:17,883 --> 00:45:19,985
NO PRESSURE, THOUGH.
DON'T WORRY.

1140
00:45:20,018 --> 00:45:21,853
WHO KNOWS WHAT'LL HAPPEN THEN?
REMEMBER, WE'VE ONLY
GOT ONE CHANCE.

1141
00:45:21,887 --> 00:45:23,422
- TIME TO GO, GUYS.
- LET'S GET OUTTA HERE.

1142
00:45:23,455 --> 00:45:26,425
- DR. HIDAKA,
EVERYTHING IS READY.
- GOOD.

1143
00:45:26,458 --> 00:45:28,160
[MISSILE WHISTLING]

1144
00:45:38,570 --> 00:45:39,538
[LAUGHTER]

1145
00:45:39,572 --> 00:45:41,207
YEAH, BOY, EAT IT.

1146
00:45:41,240 --> 00:45:44,208
I'VE BEEN WAITING TO DO THIS
THE WHOLE MOVIE!

1147
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:47,345
THAT'S IT, CROW.
DO DO THAT VOODOO THAT YOU DO
SO WELL.

1148
00:45:47,378 --> 00:45:49,147
WATCH ME, SERVO.
WATCH ME DANCE!

1149
00:45:49,180 --> 00:45:51,450
- SHH!
- WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING?

1150
00:45:51,483 --> 00:45:54,953
OH, WE'RE JUST, UH, SINGING
A COLE PORTER MEDLEY,
THAT'S ALL.

1151
00:45:54,987 --> 00:45:56,822
- YEAH. YEAH, THAT'S IT.
- NO, YOU'RE NOT.

1152
00:45:56,855 --> 00:45:58,823
YOU'RE UNLEASHING A BUNCH
OF NEGATIVE ENERGY ON KENNY

1153
00:45:58,857 --> 00:46:00,492
VIA MY JIM VARNEY DOLL.

1154
00:46:00,525 --> 00:46:02,160
THAT'S WHAT YOU'RE DOING.

1155
00:46:02,193 --> 00:46:04,863
OH, I WOULDN'T EXACTLY
CALL IT "NEGATIVE ENERGY," JOEL.

1156
00:46:04,897 --> 00:46:06,998
- UH, YEAH.
WE JUST HATE HIM, THAT'S ALL.
- YEAH.

1157
00:46:07,032 --> 00:46:08,567
HOW MANY TIMES
HAVE I TOLD YOU GUYS?

1158
00:46:08,600 --> 00:46:11,170
IN THE FACE OF ALL
THESE TERRIBLE MOVIES
WE GOTTA WATCH,

1159
00:46:11,203 --> 00:46:13,838
YOU GOTTA KEEP
A POSITIVE ATTITUDE.

1160
00:46:13,872 --> 00:46:16,908
- HAVE COMPASSION.
- OH, I GUESS SO.

1161
00:46:16,942 --> 00:46:20,812
GOSH, DAVEY.
I NEVER THOUGHT OF IT THAT WAY.

1162
00:46:20,845 --> 00:46:22,848
- [LAUGHING]
- THAT'S RIGHT, GOLIATH.
WELL, ANYWAY,

1163
00:46:22,882 --> 00:46:25,083
NOW, WHAT I WANT YOU TO DO
IS VISUALIZE KENNY
IN A GOOD LIGHT.

1164
00:46:25,117 --> 00:46:26,418
- COME ON. COME ON.
- OH...

1165
00:46:26,452 --> 00:46:27,920
- DO THE--
- OHM.

1166
00:46:27,953 --> 00:46:29,955
THAT'S RIGHT. COME ON.
DO THE EXERCISE. OKAY.

1167
00:46:29,988 --> 00:46:32,858
- OHM.
- NOW BRING KENNY
INTO YOUR HEART.

1168
00:46:32,892 --> 00:46:34,292
- YOU SEE THAT LITTLE
JAPANESE GUY IN THERE?
- OHM.

1169
00:46:34,325 --> 00:46:36,228
HE'S WAVING BACK AT YOU.
OKAY.

1170
00:46:36,262 --> 00:46:38,830
- NOW, REMEMBER THE TOMMY JAMES
AND THE SHONDELLS SONG--
- OHM.

1171
00:46:38,863 --> 00:46:40,898
- ..."CRYSTAL BLUE PERSUASION"?
- OHM.

1172
00:46:40,932 --> 00:46:43,368
PEACE AND GOOD BROTHERHOOD.
"CRYSTAL BLUE PERSUASION."

1173
00:46:43,402 --> 00:46:45,470
- NOW SHOOT THAT CRYSTAL BLUE--
- I HATE HIM, I HATE HIM!

1174
00:46:45,503 --> 00:46:47,973
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

1175
00:46:48,007 --> 00:46:52,010
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.
WHAT IS IT THAT YOU HATE
SO MUCH ABOUT KENNY?

1176
00:46:52,043 --> 00:46:55,247
OH, HE'S A CHILD OF PRIVILEGE
AND THE WHOLE WORLD
REVOLVES AROUND HIM AND STUFF,

1177
00:46:55,280 --> 00:46:59,183
AND HE CAN WALK INTO
A RESTRICTED MAXIMUM SECURITY
MILITARY SITUATION,

1178
00:46:59,217 --> 00:47:02,320
AND THEY TREAT HIM LIKE AN ADULT
JUST BECAUSE HE BEFRIENDED
A STUPID OLD TURTLE.

1179
00:47:02,353 --> 00:47:04,355
YEAH, YEAH, YEAH.
AND HE NEVER GETS INTO TROUBLE

1180
00:47:04,388 --> 00:47:07,258
EVEN THOUGH HIS FRIENDSHIP
WITH GAMERA IS CAUSING
THE DEATH OF MILLIONS,

1181
00:47:07,292 --> 00:47:09,493
AND HE SKIPS SCHOOL
WHENEVER HE WANTS TO,

1182
00:47:09,528 --> 00:47:12,030
AND HE NEVER SO MUCH
AS GETS SENT TO HIS ROOM.

1183
00:47:12,063 --> 00:47:15,000
YEAH, AND HE CAN WALK
INTO ANY BOOK WITH
HIS PONY PAL POKEY TOO.

1184
00:47:15,033 --> 00:47:18,237
UH, CROW, I THINK
YOU'RE THINKING OF GUMBY.

1185
00:47:18,270 --> 00:47:20,238
- OH.
- WELL, WHAT ABOUT HIS VOICE?

1186
00:47:20,272 --> 00:47:22,942
HAVE YOU EVER HEARD ANYTHING
SO ANNOYING?

1187
00:47:22,975 --> 00:47:24,610
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
YEAH. WHAT DID YOU DO
WITH MY ROCKS?

1188
00:47:24,643 --> 00:47:27,312
DADDY! DADDY!
GAMERA HAS A GOOD HEART.

1189
00:47:27,345 --> 00:47:29,213
NOW, COME ON.
AS YOU GUYS GET OLDER,

1190
00:47:29,247 --> 00:47:31,617
YOU'LL REALIZE THAT PEOPLE
DON'T MEAN TO BE OBNOXIOUS,

1191
00:47:31,650 --> 00:47:34,318
IT'S JUST THAT THEY'RE ALL
SCREWED UP INSIDE.

1192
00:47:34,352 --> 00:47:35,387
OH. IN OTHER WORDS,

1193
00:47:35,420 --> 00:47:38,957
AS THE GREAT FRENCH FILM
DIRECTOR JOHN RENOIR SAID,

1194
00:47:38,990 --> 00:47:40,992
[FRENCH ACCENT]
"EVERY MAN HAS HIS REASONS."

1195
00:47:41,025 --> 00:47:43,328
- EXACTLY.
- OH. GEE.

1196
00:47:43,362 --> 00:47:45,497
I'M STARTING TO SEE
THINGS DIFFERENTLY.

1197
00:47:45,530 --> 00:47:47,565
NOW WHEN I VISUALIZE KENNY,
I WANNA GO UP TO HIM

1198
00:47:47,598 --> 00:47:50,102
AND GIVE HIM A BIG
SNUGGLY HUGGLY.

1199
00:47:50,135 --> 00:47:51,503
- THAT'S GOOD.
- AND THEN SQUEEZE HIM--

1200
00:47:51,537 --> 00:47:53,205
- MM-HMM. YEAH.
- ...AND SQUEEZE HIM

1201
00:47:53,238 --> 00:47:56,975
AND SQUEEZE AND SQUEEZE
AND SQUEEZE...

1202
00:47:57,008 --> 00:48:00,678
ALL RIGHT. YOU GOT
A TIME-OUT COMING, YOUNG MAN.

1203
00:48:00,712 --> 00:48:02,948
- LET'S GET OUTTA HERE.
COME ON. YOU'RE COMING WITH--
- AND SQUEEZE...

1204
00:48:02,982 --> 00:48:04,082
- HEY.
- [YELLS]

1205
00:48:04,115 --> 00:48:05,617
[CLEARS THROAT]
WHAT DO YOU,

1206
00:48:05,650 --> 00:48:07,485
THE VIEWERS AT HOME, THINK?

1207
00:48:07,518 --> 00:48:08,953
- [CROW] YOU'RE NOT
MY REAL FATHER.
- SHH!

1208
00:48:08,987 --> 00:48:10,488
WHAT'S THE DEAL WITH KENNY?

1209
00:48:10,522 --> 00:48:12,323
IS HE A CONFUSED,
PRECOCIOUS KID

1210
00:48:12,357 --> 00:48:14,358
WHO'S FALLEN IN
WITH THE WRONG SPECIES?

1211
00:48:14,392 --> 00:48:16,595
- I HATE YOU.
- IS HE A STARRY-EYED DREAMER

1212
00:48:16,628 --> 00:48:18,663
LOOKING FOR
HIS LONG-LOST MOTHER?

1213
00:48:18,697 --> 00:48:20,332
IS HE A JUVENILE DELINQUENT

1214
00:48:20,365 --> 00:48:22,133
WHO SHOULD HAVE THE BOOK
THROWN AT HIM

1215
00:48:22,167 --> 00:48:24,202
BEFORE MILLIONS MORE
NEEDLESSLY PERISH?

1216
00:48:24,235 --> 00:48:26,170
SEND YOUR THOUGHTS TO...

1217
00:48:28,240 --> 00:48:30,608
...CARE OF MYSTERY SCIENCE
THEATER 3000,

1218
00:48:30,642 --> 00:48:33,045
POST OFFICE BOX 5325,

1219
00:48:33,078 --> 00:48:36,315
HOPKINS, MINNESOTA, 55343.

1220
00:48:36,348 --> 00:48:38,217
- STOP IT!
- AND WHILE WE'RE AT IT,

1221
00:48:38,250 --> 00:48:39,383
WHAT'S ALL THIS
ABOUT JIM VARNEY?

1222
00:48:39,417 --> 00:48:41,553
- I HATE HIM TOO!
- AND WHAT ABOUT
SCARECROW'S BRAIN?

1223
00:48:41,587 --> 00:48:43,555
- AAHH! [SHOUTS]
- AND KIM CATTRALL?

1224
00:48:43,588 --> 00:48:45,923
- [ALARM BLARES]
- [CLAMORING]

1225
00:48:57,135 --> 00:48:59,705
- WELL, I THINK YOU WERE
A LITTLE HARD ON HIM.
- COME ON, CROW. COME ON.

1226
00:48:59,738 --> 00:49:01,640
[ROARS]

1227
00:49:01,673 --> 00:49:03,075
OOH.

1228
00:49:03,108 --> 00:49:04,977
HEY, KENNY, HELP ME.
I'M STUCK.

1229
00:49:07,312 --> 00:49:09,748
- COME ON IN, CROW.
- COME ON. SIT DOWN. I'M SORRY.

1230
00:49:09,782 --> 00:49:11,450
- CAN WE BE FRIENDS?
- YEAH.

1231
00:49:15,253 --> 00:49:17,255
- HI. HOW YOU DOING?
- WHAT A PITCH!

1232
00:49:17,288 --> 00:49:18,723
THIS IS THE SCOOP
OF THE CENTURY!

1233
00:49:18,757 --> 00:49:21,292
NO. CARVEL IS THE SCOOP
OF THE CENTURY.

1234
00:49:21,327 --> 00:49:22,660
WORLD'S FRESHEST ICE CREAM.

1235
00:49:22,693 --> 00:49:24,697
- AGAIN WITH THE CARVEL?
- MISS, TELL US WHEN TO START.

1236
00:49:24,730 --> 00:49:27,432
- IT'S FUNNY.
- DOCTOR, TEN MINUTES,
BEGINNING NOW.

1237
00:49:27,465 --> 00:49:29,200
- OH. NOW TEN MINUTES.
- START.

1238
00:49:29,233 --> 00:49:30,635
START!

1239
00:49:33,205 --> 00:49:37,075
- THEY'RE IN.
- MM-HMM.

1240
00:49:37,108 --> 00:49:38,543
OOH!

1241
00:49:38,577 --> 00:49:40,745
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1242
00:49:40,778 --> 00:49:44,348
HERE AT TOHO INDUSTRIES,
WE'RE WORKING TO KEEP
YOUR TRUST.

1243
00:49:44,382 --> 00:49:47,085
IF WE CAN'T FREEZE GAMERA,
NO ONE CAN.

1244
00:49:47,118 --> 00:49:49,320
♪♪ [HUMMING]

1245
00:49:49,353 --> 00:49:51,757
- OKAY, HE'S DOING CHARADES,
I THINK.
- FIRST WORD, UH--

1246
00:49:51,790 --> 00:49:54,425
- SWIMMING?
- IT LOOKS LIKE
HE'S GONNA MOVE AGAIN.

1247
00:49:54,458 --> 00:49:56,060
THE FREEZING BOMBS
ARE NEARLY SET.

1248
00:49:56,093 --> 00:49:57,795
THEY'LL BEGIN TO GO OFF SOON.

1249
00:49:57,828 --> 00:50:00,798
- HOW MANY MINUTES?
- EIGHT MORE MINUTES.

1250
00:50:00,832 --> 00:50:02,800
- YOU MEAN OUT OF TEN?
- OH, CRAP.

1251
00:50:02,833 --> 00:50:05,770
I'M HIGH-CENTERED.
HEY, KENNY, HELP ME.

1252
00:50:05,803 --> 00:50:07,772
HMM.

1253
00:50:07,805 --> 00:50:10,175
- PRECISION.
- HURRY, COMMANDER.

1254
00:50:10,208 --> 00:50:11,510
ALL RIGHT.
EVERYONE CLEAR OUT!

1255
00:50:11,543 --> 00:50:13,678
- LET'S GO!
- LET'S GO!

1256
00:50:13,712 --> 00:50:15,813
COME ON! COME ON!

1257
00:50:15,847 --> 00:50:17,648
- LET'S GET OUTTA HERE!
- HUH?

1258
00:50:17,682 --> 00:50:19,718
- COME ON!
- HEY, DRINKS ARE ON ME!

1259
00:50:19,752 --> 00:50:22,620
LET'S GO! WHOO-HOO!

1260
00:50:22,653 --> 00:50:25,157
- UH, I'M WITH HIM.
- HOW'S IT GOING?

1261
00:50:29,862 --> 00:50:31,597
THERE ISN'T MUCH TIME LEFT.

1262
00:50:31,630 --> 00:50:33,298
LESS THAN TEN MINUTES,
I SUPPOSE.

1263
00:50:33,332 --> 00:50:34,532
- OH, YOU GOT A LITTLE,
UH-- ECHH!
- YECH!

1264
00:50:36,568 --> 00:50:39,437
WHAT ARE THEY GONNA DO,
TURN HIM INTO A KITE?
[CHUCKLES]

1265
00:50:39,470 --> 00:50:42,307
DR. HIDAKA, WE MUST HURRY.

1266
00:50:42,340 --> 00:50:44,175
DON'T WORRY.
WE'RE READY TO BLAST.

1267
00:50:44,208 --> 00:50:46,177
- SO AM I.
- YOU GOT TEN MINUTES.

1268
00:50:51,883 --> 00:50:53,685
- WHOO!
- OH! THAT SURPRISED EVEN ME.

1269
00:50:58,190 --> 00:51:01,493
- AW.
- AW. NOW, THAT'S SAD.

1270
00:51:01,527 --> 00:51:03,695
- [ROARING]
- AW.

1271
00:51:03,728 --> 00:51:06,163
I DON'T LIKE TO SEE THIS.

1272
00:51:07,232 --> 00:51:09,835
TELL KENNY I LOVED HIM.

1273
00:51:12,470 --> 00:51:14,840
- GOOD NIGHT, SWEET PRINCE.
- LOOK! IT WORKED.

1274
00:51:14,873 --> 00:51:17,108
- DUH.
- YES. IT'S ON ITS BACK NOW.

1275
00:51:17,142 --> 00:51:18,610
YES, BUT REMEMBER, COMMANDER,

1276
00:51:18,643 --> 00:51:21,713
TURTLES DO NOT HAVE
THE ABILITY TO TURN OVER
BY THEMSELVES,

1277
00:51:21,747 --> 00:51:24,715
SO IF WE'RE PATIENT
AND WAIT HERE A FEW MINUTES,

1278
00:51:24,748 --> 00:51:26,417
IT'S BOUND TO DIE.

1279
00:51:26,452 --> 00:51:27,885
- [SOLDIERS CHEERING]
- THAT'LL BE FUN.

1280
00:51:27,918 --> 00:51:30,788
PERMISSION TO FROLIC
GRANTED, SIR.

1281
00:51:30,822 --> 00:51:32,790
DR. HIDAKA,
YOUR PLAN WAS SUCCESSFUL.

1282
00:51:32,823 --> 00:51:35,193
YES. AND IF GAMERA
DIES ON THAT SPOT,

1283
00:51:35,227 --> 00:51:37,395
WE'LL HAVE A PRECIOUS SPECIMEN.

1284
00:51:37,428 --> 00:51:40,832
- ITS WHOLE BODY.
- AND SOUP FOR EVERYBODY.

1285
00:51:40,865 --> 00:51:44,535
I'M MELTING.
OH, WHAT A WORLD, WHAT A WORLD.

1286
00:51:44,568 --> 00:51:48,207
COMMANDER, LOOK!
IT'S PULLED IN ITS HEAD
AND FEET.

1287
00:51:48,240 --> 00:51:50,275
YOU SEE, DOCTOR,
IT DOESN'T FLY ANYMORE.

1288
00:51:50,308 --> 00:51:51,877
- [LAUGHTER]
- [CROW LAUGHS]

1289
00:51:51,910 --> 00:51:54,178
- I DON'T GET THAT.
- I GUESS YOU HAD TO BE THERE.

1290
00:51:54,212 --> 00:51:56,715
- YEAH.
- CROW GOT IT.

1291
00:51:56,748 --> 00:51:58,283
- NO. I'M JUST BEING POLITE.
- OH.

1292
00:52:00,652 --> 00:52:03,488
- WHOA!
- HEY, CHECK IT OUT.
IT'S THE BATMOBILE.

1293
00:52:03,522 --> 00:52:05,457
ATOMIC BATTERIES TO POWER.
TURBINES TO SPEED.

1294
00:52:05,490 --> 00:52:07,458
ROGER.
READY TO MOVE OUT.

1295
00:52:07,492 --> 00:52:11,162
- IT'S A BATTERY... SEE.
- YEAH. YEAH.

1296
00:52:11,195 --> 00:52:13,432
[MUTTERING]

1297
00:52:13,465 --> 00:52:14,765
- COMIC BOOK.
- OOH.

1298
00:52:14,798 --> 00:52:16,935
LIGHT BLOOMING GROUND FLOWER
AND GET AWAY.

1299
00:52:16,968 --> 00:52:19,270
IF LOUD, REPORT.

1300
00:52:19,303 --> 00:52:21,673
OH, I SAW THAT
ON ED SULLIVAN.

1301
00:52:21,707 --> 00:52:24,575
LIGHT SPINNER.

1302
00:52:24,608 --> 00:52:27,745
IT'S A BIG OLD FONDUE POT.

1303
00:52:27,778 --> 00:52:29,948
OOH.

1304
00:52:29,982 --> 00:52:32,317
IT'S ALMOST LIKE
A FLYING SAUCER.

1305
00:52:32,350 --> 00:52:34,685
- MM-HMM.
- IT IS.

1306
00:52:37,922 --> 00:52:40,925
UH, LOOKS LIKE A GIANT
TURTLE POTPIE TO ME, SIR.

1307
00:52:44,495 --> 00:52:47,898
DON'T WORRY, PEOPLE.
GAMERA'S ONLY A SHELL
OF HIS FORMER SELF.

1308
00:52:47,932 --> 00:52:49,868
- [CHUCKLES, MUTTERS]
- EW.

1309
00:52:49,902 --> 00:52:51,302
SORRY.

1310
00:52:53,003 --> 00:52:54,405
OOH.

1311
00:52:54,438 --> 00:52:56,808
- HEY, I CAN'T SEE.
- COME ON.

1312
00:52:56,842 --> 00:53:00,512
LOOKS LIKE IT'S BACK
TO VO-TECH FOR ME, FELLAS.

1313
00:53:00,545 --> 00:53:02,547
YEP.

1314
00:53:02,580 --> 00:53:05,583
- OH, BOY. I'VE DONE IT NOW.
- CATHERINE, HAVE YOU GOT
THE STONE?

1315
00:53:05,617 --> 00:53:07,452
- YES.
- [HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
YES. I PASSED IT LAST NIGHT.

1316
00:53:08,653 --> 00:53:10,888
[CROW GAGS]

1317
00:53:10,922 --> 00:53:13,358
- SMASH IT INTO MY FOREHEAD,
WILL YOU?
- SIR, THE MYSTERY IS SOLVED.

1318
00:53:13,392 --> 00:53:16,562
THE LINES DON'T REPRESENT WAVES
BUT CLOUDS.

1319
00:53:16,595 --> 00:53:19,965
THEY WERE TRYING TO TELL US
THAT GAMERA
WAS A FLYING CREATURE.

1320
00:53:19,998 --> 00:53:22,533
A LITTLE TOO LATE HERE, DOCTOR.

1321
00:53:22,567 --> 00:53:25,803
SMASH! NEWSPAPER
HITS JAPANESE IN FACE!

1322
00:53:25,837 --> 00:53:27,705
OOH, THAT STUNG.

1323
00:53:27,738 --> 00:53:30,508
WHY, IT'S THE SAME CREATURE
THAT I SAW.

1324
00:53:30,542 --> 00:53:33,478
OH, THEN THE FLYING OBJECT
YOU SAW WAS GAMERA.

1325
00:53:33,512 --> 00:53:36,247
- THANK YOU, MISS HATHAWAY.
- YES. EXACTLY.

1326
00:53:36,280 --> 00:53:38,817
OH, AS THE OLD SAYING GOES,

1327
00:53:38,850 --> 00:53:41,418
"WE SEE TERRIBLE THINGS
IF WE LIVE TOO LONG."

1328
00:53:41,452 --> 00:53:43,688
- AND GET TERRIBLE PARTS.
- IT'S TRUE.

1329
00:53:43,722 --> 00:53:45,490
- OH!
- [BRAKES SCREECH]

1330
00:53:45,523 --> 00:53:47,825
- ARE YOU HURT?
- NO, I'M ALL RIGHT.

1331
00:53:47,858 --> 00:53:50,928
- [DRIVER] OUT OF THE WAY!
- THE DRIVER IS EITHER
MISSING OR...

1332
00:53:50,962 --> 00:53:53,365
RIGHT. SORRY.

1333
00:53:53,398 --> 00:53:55,667
WHAT ARE ALL THESE STONES?

1334
00:53:55,700 --> 00:53:58,770
WHY ARE YOU CARRYING THEM
AROUND WITH YOU, KENNY?

1335
00:53:58,803 --> 00:54:00,905
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
TO HURT PEOPLE.
LIFE HURTS ME SO I HURT BACK.

1336
00:54:02,840 --> 00:54:05,543
I SUPPOSE THIS IS ANOTHER
FOOLISHNESS OF YOURS.

1337
00:54:05,577 --> 00:54:08,847
- I SUPPOSE NOW WE'RE GOING
TO BE ATTACKED BY A GIANT ROCK.
- NOW, KENNY--

1338
00:54:08,880 --> 00:54:10,982
- IT'S GAMERA'S NEW HOUSE.
- HUH?

1339
00:54:11,015 --> 00:54:12,883
- RIGHT.
- GAMERA'S NEW HOUSE?

1340
00:54:12,917 --> 00:54:13,952
YEAH.

1341
00:54:13,985 --> 00:54:15,887
TIBBY'S FROM GAMERA'S FAMILY.

1342
00:54:15,920 --> 00:54:18,357
- [JOEL MUTTERS]
- WHEE, THIS KID REALLY
STEPPED OFF THE CURB.

1343
00:54:18,390 --> 00:54:19,857
THAT'S RIGHT.

1344
00:54:19,890 --> 00:54:22,627
MEANWHILE, ON TRAPPER JOHN...

1345
00:54:22,660 --> 00:54:24,428
♪♪ [WHISTLING]

1346
00:54:24,462 --> 00:54:26,330
FOCUS, PLEASE.
CLEAR THE SHOT.

1347
00:54:26,363 --> 00:54:30,068
COME ON. WE'RE TRYING
TO SHOOT A MOVIE.

1348
00:54:30,102 --> 00:54:32,937
- [WOMAN] GAMERA'S BEEN FLYING
ALL OVER THE WORLD.
- ALL OVER THE WORLD!

1349
00:54:32,970 --> 00:54:36,875
BUT AS SOON AS IT'S SIGHTED,
IT MANAGES TO DISAPPEAR
IMMEDIATELY.

1350
00:54:36,908 --> 00:54:39,677
IT'S A SHAME WE CAN'T FIND
EXACTLY WHERE IT IS NOW.

1351
00:54:39,710 --> 00:54:41,378
[DR. HIDAKA]
YES. BUT LET'S BE THANKFUL

1352
00:54:41,412 --> 00:54:43,448
IT HASN'T ATTACKED
ANY PLACES YET.

1353
00:54:43,482 --> 00:54:45,717
- YES.
- WHOA! THAT'S QUITE A BEAK.

1354
00:54:45,750 --> 00:54:47,718
- WHAT AM I SAYING?
- [KNOCK ON DOOR]

1355
00:54:47,752 --> 00:54:50,022
- YES?
- WHAT COULD BE WORSE THAN THIS?

1356
00:54:50,055 --> 00:54:54,325
- HELLO.
- HOW DO YOU DO, CATHERINE?

1357
00:54:54,358 --> 00:54:57,795
- HOW DO YOU DO, SIR?
- [DR. HIDAKA] KENNY, THIS IS
A PLEASANT SURPRISE.

1358
00:54:57,828 --> 00:54:59,830
- NOT!
- YES, I TOLD KENNY THAT
WHEN HE WAS VISITING TOKYO,

1359
00:54:59,863 --> 00:55:01,532
HE OUGHT TO COME AND SEE US.

1360
00:55:01,565 --> 00:55:03,402
- OH, GOOD IDEA.
- I DIDN'T REALLY MEAN THAT.

1361
00:55:03,435 --> 00:55:05,603
- HOWEVER, IT IS SOONER
THAN I EXPECTED.
- YEAH.

1362
00:55:05,637 --> 00:55:08,873
YOU SEE, DOCTOR,
OUR TOWN HAD A LIGHTHOUSE,
AND GAMERA DESTROYED IT.

1363
00:55:08,907 --> 00:55:11,542
- AH.
- AND NOW IT'S BEEN BUILT AGAIN.

1364
00:55:11,575 --> 00:55:14,378
- OUR HOUSE WAS DESTROYED, TOO,
AND NOW THEY'RE BUILDING THAT.
- OH, THAT'S NEAT.

1365
00:55:14,412 --> 00:55:16,380
- HOW NICE FOR YOU.
- SO WE DECIDED
TO COME TO TOKYO--

1366
00:55:16,413 --> 00:55:18,983
- I GOTTA GET BACK TO WORK.
- ...TO STAY WITH AN UNCLE
WHO LIVES HERE.

1367
00:55:19,017 --> 00:55:21,687
- OH, SO YOU'RE A TOURIST NOW.
- THERE'S PLENTY TO SEE

1368
00:55:21,720 --> 00:55:24,022
AND LOTS OF MONUMENTS
TO VISIT.

1369
00:55:24,055 --> 00:55:26,725
DO YOU SEE THAT STRUCTURE THERE?
THAT'S TOKYO TOWER.

1370
00:55:28,727 --> 00:55:30,428
- DOCTOR?
- HMM?

1371
00:55:30,462 --> 00:55:32,397
- YOU'RE GOING TO DIE, SIR.
- IS GAMERA STILL IN HIDING?

1372
00:55:32,430 --> 00:55:34,565
YES.

1373
00:55:34,598 --> 00:55:37,768
- BUT WE'RE SEARCHING FOR HIM.
- HE'S DOING SOME SOCIAL WORK
ON THE SIDE.

1374
00:55:37,802 --> 00:55:40,038
GAMERA MUST
BE TERRIBLY LONELY.

1375
00:55:40,072 --> 00:55:42,940
- KENNY, HE'S A TURTLE.
GET A MITT AND CATCH A CLUE!
- GAMERA'S REALLY VERY KIND.

1376
00:55:42,973 --> 00:55:44,875
GAMERA LOVES ALL CHILDREN.

1377
00:55:44,908 --> 00:55:47,378
- YOU KNOW, KENNY HAS
A VIVID IMAGINATION.
- AW.

1378
00:55:47,412 --> 00:55:48,780
- THAT'S SO SAD.
- DIDN'T HE SAVE MY LIFE?

1379
00:55:48,813 --> 00:55:50,582
- HE'S SO SAD.
- GAMERA MUST BE VERY LONELY

1380
00:55:50,615 --> 00:55:52,783
- ...AND MUST NEED FRIENDS.
- [ALL MOCK CRYING]

1381
00:55:52,817 --> 00:55:55,820
- I'M SURE HE MUST BE
VERY HUNGRY TOO.
- [MOCK SNIFFLING]

1382
00:55:55,853 --> 00:55:58,690
- TIBBY'S LITTLE
AND GAMERA'S BIG.
- MMM. THAT'S SO TRUE.

1383
00:55:58,723 --> 00:56:00,925
EXCEPT THEY'RE BOTH
IN THE SAME FAMILY. I KNOW IT.

1384
00:56:00,958 --> 00:56:03,395
- I KNOW THEY ARE.
- THAT'S RIGHT.

1385
00:56:03,428 --> 00:56:06,563
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
GAMERA DEMANDS
YOUR INSTANT DEATH.

1386
00:56:06,597 --> 00:56:08,933
HEY, LOOK AT HIS NECK.
666.

1387
00:56:11,803 --> 00:56:13,538
AND THEY'RE BOTH GOOD
AND GENTLE.

1388
00:56:15,173 --> 00:56:17,475
YOUR PASSING WILL BE PAINLESS,
DOCTOR.

1389
00:56:19,143 --> 00:56:21,178
- SHE'S GOTTA COMMIT KENNY.
- YEAH.

1390
00:56:21,212 --> 00:56:24,582
HELLO, AKIRO.
YOU LOOK VERY BUSY.

1391
00:56:24,615 --> 00:56:27,118
- UH-HUH. SURE. YEAH, RIGHT.
- I SEE YOU'RE STILL CARRYING
THOSE HEAVY BOXES AROUND.

1392
00:56:27,152 --> 00:56:28,620
- [GIGGLES]
- YEAH, YEAH. WHATEVER.

1393
00:56:28,653 --> 00:56:30,422
- MUST BE NICE, HUH?
- ANY FRESH FISH TODAY?

1394
00:56:30,455 --> 00:56:31,890
FRESH FISH?
[CHUCKLES]

1395
00:56:31,923 --> 00:56:34,125
NOBODY EATS FRESH FISH,
JUST THAT CAN STUFF,

1396
00:56:34,158 --> 00:56:36,493
AND IT WEIGHS A TON,
BELIEVE ME.

1397
00:56:36,527 --> 00:56:38,863
- THAT'S BEER.
- COME BACK. GIVE ME MY STONE.

1398
00:56:38,897 --> 00:56:40,732
- KENNY!
- YOU WERE BORN OF A JACKAL!

1399
00:56:40,765 --> 00:56:42,667
- I DON'T HAVE YOUR STONES.
- YES, YOU'VE GOT THEM.

1400
00:56:42,700 --> 00:56:44,068
- I SAW YOU STEAL THEM.
- NO, I DIDN'T.

1401
00:56:44,102 --> 00:56:46,603
ALL RIGHT.
GIVE HIM BACK HIS STONES.

1402
00:56:46,637 --> 00:56:49,073
- I THREW THEM AWAY.
- THEN YOU'D BETTER GO
AND GET THEM,

1403
00:56:49,107 --> 00:56:50,675
IF YOU KNOW
WHAT'S GOOD FOR YOU.

1404
00:56:50,708 --> 00:56:53,077
GIVE THE LITTLE FREAK
HIS STONES!

1405
00:56:53,110 --> 00:56:56,047
ALL RIGHT.
YOU HEARD WHAT I SAID.

1406
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:58,450
[GROANS]
YOU SEE,

1407
00:56:58,483 --> 00:57:00,952
I THREW THEM OFF THE BRIDGE,
INTO THE RIVER.

1408
00:57:00,985 --> 00:57:03,020
- DIE, DIE, DIE!
- INTO THE RIVER?

1409
00:57:03,053 --> 00:57:06,825
♪♪ [ALL IMITATING FOREBODING
LATIN CHANTING FROM THE OMEN]

1410
00:57:06,858 --> 00:57:08,993
KENNY, I'LL GET YOU
OTHER STONES

1411
00:57:09,027 --> 00:57:10,862
JUST LIKE THOSE, ALL RIGHT?

1412
00:57:10,895 --> 00:57:13,665
- THERE AREN'T ANY LIKE THOSE.
- OHH.

1413
00:57:13,698 --> 00:57:16,000
KENNY!

1414
00:57:16,033 --> 00:57:19,037
- HE'S CRAZY, CRYING OVER
A COUPLE OF STONES.
- MM-HMM.

1415
00:57:19,070 --> 00:57:20,705
- SHUT UP. BEAT IT.
- [CRACKING SOUND]

1416
00:57:20,738 --> 00:57:21,705
- AAHH!
- MY SPINE!

1417
00:57:21,738 --> 00:57:23,207
IT'S ALL RIGHT.
THANK YOU.

1418
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:25,877
IN A WAY, I'M GLAD
HE THREW THE STONES AWAY.

1419
00:57:25,910 --> 00:57:28,445
BACK TO
GIDGET GOES TO JAPAN.

1420
00:57:30,182 --> 00:57:33,183
- ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?
- [DEMONIC VOICE] GO AWAY!

1421
00:57:33,217 --> 00:57:35,220
[DEMONIC GROWLING]

1422
00:57:35,253 --> 00:57:37,755
NOW, DON'T ACT LIKE THAT,
KENNY.

1423
00:57:37,788 --> 00:57:40,090
- YOU'RE A BIG BOY.
- [GROWLING CONTINUES]

1424
00:57:40,123 --> 00:57:42,993
SULKING LIKE THAT
ISN'T GONNA BRING THE STONES
BACK AGAIN, YOU KNOW.

1425
00:57:43,027 --> 00:57:44,895
AND THERE'S NO EASTER BUNNY
EITHER.

1426
00:57:44,928 --> 00:57:47,565
THERE ARE LOTS OF OTHER STONES.
I'LL GO LOOKING TOO.

1427
00:57:47,598 --> 00:57:51,268
ALL RIGHT, KENNY?
WE'LL LOOK TOGETHER.

1428
00:57:51,302 --> 00:57:54,272
- [GROWLING, BARKING]
- KENNY?

1429
00:57:54,305 --> 00:57:56,807
[IMITATING DOG PANTING]

1430
00:57:56,842 --> 00:57:59,243
[CHUCKLES]
SCOUNDREL.

1431
00:57:59,277 --> 00:58:02,280
[HIGH-PITCHED VOICE]
I AM THE DREAM WARRIOR.

1432
00:58:02,313 --> 00:58:04,282
[CHUCKLES]

1433
00:58:04,315 --> 00:58:05,817
GOOD RIDDANCE.

1434
00:58:08,720 --> 00:58:10,087
HMM.

1435
00:58:13,023 --> 00:58:14,625
- WHERE ARE THEY?
- BOSTON, I THINK.

1436
00:58:16,660 --> 00:58:18,630
THERE'S NO LOAD OF FISH TODAY.

1437
00:58:18,663 --> 00:58:21,165
WE'RE GOING TO HAVE TO
GO INTO ANOTHER BUSINESS.

1438
00:58:21,198 --> 00:58:22,733
- YEAH, SURE.
- YEAH, YOU'RE RIGHT.

1439
00:58:22,767 --> 00:58:25,035
I TELL YOU,
THERE'S SOMETHING WRONG
WITH THE WATER.

1440
00:58:25,068 --> 00:58:28,238
ALL THOSE NUCLEAR TESTS.
THEY'RE THROWING THE TIDES OFF.

1441
00:58:28,272 --> 00:58:30,308
IT'S THOSE SCIENTISTS.
IN A FEW YEARS,

1442
00:58:30,342 --> 00:58:32,177
THEY'LL KILL
EVERY LIVING CREATURE.

1443
00:58:32,210 --> 00:58:33,878
THEY ALREADY DRILLED
A HOLE IN MY THROAT.

1444
00:58:33,912 --> 00:58:35,547
THIS AFTERNOON,
A SERIES OF FLOODS,

1445
00:58:35,580 --> 00:58:38,583
CAUSED BY A REVERSAL
OF TIDAL WAVES,
INUNDATED TOKYO,

1446
00:58:38,617 --> 00:58:40,585
DEVASTATING WHOLE AREAS
OF THE CITY.

1447
00:58:40,618 --> 00:58:42,253
- NEAT.
- IT'S ESTIMATED
THAT NEARLY 3,000

1448
00:58:42,287 --> 00:58:44,122
SHOPS AND HOUSES
WERE DESTROYED.

1449
00:58:44,155 --> 00:58:46,057
WE'LL NOW SHOW YOU
FILM SEQUENCES.

1450
00:58:46,090 --> 00:58:48,860
- THE PASSWORD
IS "KOOKYGOOGOOWA."
- ACCORDING TO THE COMMUNIQUé--

1451
00:58:48,893 --> 00:58:50,127
- FOCUS, PLEASE. FOCUS.
- ...OF THE METEOROLOGICAL
OBSERVATORY,

1452
00:58:50,160 --> 00:58:52,230
THE SOURCE OF THE FLOOD
REMAINS A COMPLETE MYSTERY

1453
00:58:52,263 --> 00:58:53,765
AS PHENOMENA
OF THIS KIND--

1454
00:58:53,798 --> 00:58:55,867
- ♪ PHENOMENA ♪
- ♪ BA DEE BA-DEE-BEE ♪

1455
00:58:55,900 --> 00:58:57,635
- ♪ PHENOMENA ♪
- ♪ BA DEE-BEE-DEE ♪

1456
00:58:57,668 --> 00:59:00,037
...ARE NOW INVESTIGATING
THE ORIGIN OF THE TIDE,

1457
00:59:00,070 --> 00:59:02,640
WHICH HAS ALSO BROUGHT ABOUT
A DECREASE OF MARINE LIFE

1458
00:59:02,673 --> 00:59:04,342
ALONG THE PACIFIC COAST.

1459
00:59:04,375 --> 00:59:07,212
AH, THIS IS PEARL HARBOR.
HOW'D THIS GET IN HERE?

1460
00:59:07,245 --> 00:59:09,680
- HEY.
- NOT EVEN SUPPOSED TO...

1461
00:59:09,713 --> 00:59:11,715
...SERIOUS THREAT
TO THE FOOD SUPPLY.

1462
00:59:11,748 --> 00:59:14,185
- SNAFU.
- FURTHERMORE, THERE WERE
A NUMBER OF COLLISIONS AT SEA

1463
00:59:14,218 --> 00:59:16,120
CAUSED BY AN INTERRUPTION
OF COMMUNICATIONS

1464
00:59:16,153 --> 00:59:18,657
- AS A RESULT OF--
- THE ANDREA DORIA.

1465
00:59:18,690 --> 00:59:20,692
I KNEW HER.

1466
00:59:20,725 --> 00:59:21,825
HOWEVER, THIS IS STILL
BEING STUDIED.

1467
00:59:21,858 --> 00:59:23,293
POWDER.

1468
00:59:23,327 --> 00:59:25,062
THERE'S GOING TO BE
A SPECIAL CONFERENCE

1469
00:59:25,095 --> 00:59:26,932
LATER THIS EVENING
AT THE UNIVERSITY.

1470
00:59:26,965 --> 00:59:28,332
DURING WHICH,
DR. HIDAKA WILL TALK

1471
00:59:28,365 --> 00:59:30,835
- TO HIGH-RANKING OFFICERS--
- AND KENNY.

1472
00:59:30,868 --> 00:59:33,170
ARE YOU A MOD OR A ROCKER?

1473
00:59:33,203 --> 00:59:35,038
- UNFORTUNATELY--
- I'M A MOCKER.

1474
00:59:35,072 --> 00:59:37,242
...NOT YET CERTAIN WHAT
CAUSED THESE CATASTROPHES.

1475
00:59:37,275 --> 00:59:39,243
THOUGH VARIOUS THEORIES
HAVE BEEN PRESENTED

1476
00:59:39,277 --> 00:59:41,078
BY OUR LEADING SCIENTISTS.

1477
00:59:41,112 --> 00:59:44,015
HOWEVER, IF I MAY,
I SHOULD LIKE TO GIVE YOU

1478
00:59:44,048 --> 00:59:46,017
MY OWN PERSONAL OPINION
OF THE EVENTS.

1479
00:59:46,050 --> 00:59:48,653
- HOO-HAH!
- IT IS MY DEEPEST CONVICTION

1480
00:59:48,687 --> 00:59:51,957
THAT GAMERA IS THE TRUE CAUSE
OF ALL THESE SUDDEN DISASTERS.

1481
00:59:51,990 --> 00:59:53,825
HEY, SOMEBODY FROZE
THE OLD GUY.

1482
00:59:53,858 --> 00:59:56,227
HE MAY BE HIDING SOMEWHERE
ALONG OUR COASTS.

1483
00:59:56,260 --> 00:59:58,062
- MR. FREEZE.
- OR UNDER THIS TABLE.

1484
00:59:58,095 --> 01:00:00,298
...THEN GAMERA IS
WHAT IS UNDOUBTEDLY

1485
01:00:00,332 --> 01:00:03,300
DISTURBING THE NATURAL
SEQUENCE OF TIDES.

1486
01:00:03,333 --> 01:00:04,668
NOW, THIS COULD'VE
BEEN THE CAUSE

1487
01:00:04,702 --> 01:00:06,670
OF THESE RECENT FLOODS.

1488
01:00:06,703 --> 01:00:08,172
BUT FORGET THAT NOW!

1489
01:00:08,205 --> 01:00:10,273
LET'S ROLL TO RIO
WITH LAINIE KAZAN!

1490
01:00:10,308 --> 01:00:12,877
HOWEVER, TO INVESTIGATE
THE CASE MORE THOROUGHLY,

1491
01:00:12,910 --> 01:00:14,945
WE HAVE INVITED
LEADING SCIENTISTS...

1492
01:00:14,978 --> 01:00:16,813
[MURMURED INTRODUCTIONS]

1493
01:00:20,952 --> 01:00:22,820
- I AM--
- PULL MY BEARD!

1494
01:00:22,853 --> 01:00:24,255
--NOT ENCOURAGING.

1495
01:00:24,288 --> 01:00:26,057
EVERY METHOD USED SO FAR

1496
01:00:26,090 --> 01:00:28,258
HAS NOT LED TO ANY
CONCRETE RESULT.

1497
01:00:28,292 --> 01:00:30,160
GAMERA SEEMS ABLE
TO RESIST ATTACKS

1498
01:00:30,193 --> 01:00:33,798
BY ALL OFFENSIVE WEAPONS
KNOWN TO US.

1499
01:00:33,832 --> 01:00:35,298
THEREFORE,
I AM FORCED TO ADMIT

1500
01:00:35,333 --> 01:00:37,668
THERE MAY BE EVEN GREATER
CATASTROPHES AHEAD.

1501
01:00:37,702 --> 01:00:38,937
MORE GAMERA MOVIES?

1502
01:00:38,970 --> 01:00:41,238
PROFESSOR MURASHE,
BEFORE COMING HERE,

1503
01:00:41,272 --> 01:00:43,875
WE ATTENDED A SPECIAL MEETING
AT U.N. HEADQUARTERS.

1504
01:00:43,908 --> 01:00:45,142
- IT WAS NEAT.
- AND THEY HAVE RECOMMENDED

1505
01:00:45,175 --> 01:00:47,212
YOUR USING
A DIFFERENT STRATEGY.

1506
01:00:47,245 --> 01:00:48,847
AND WHAT IS THAT?

1507
01:00:48,880 --> 01:00:50,348
WELL, THEY BELIEVE THAT YOU

1508
01:00:50,382 --> 01:00:53,050
OUGHT TO PUT PLAN Z
INTO OPERATION IMMEDIATELY.

1509
01:00:53,083 --> 01:00:54,952
- BLUH-BLAH!
- USING THE FACILITIES

1510
01:00:54,985 --> 01:00:56,687
YOU'RE BUILDING AT OSHIMA
IN THE MOUNTAINS.

1511
01:00:56,720 --> 01:00:58,055
WELL, THAT INSTALLATION

1512
01:00:58,088 --> 01:01:00,458
IS STILL IN
THE EXPERIMENTAL STAGE YET.

1513
01:01:00,492 --> 01:01:03,795
USING IT ON GAMERA MIGHT
EXHAUST ITS RESOURCES.

1514
01:01:03,828 --> 01:01:04,962
ITS MAIN PURPOSE
IS TO ADVANCE--

1515
01:01:04,995 --> 01:01:07,332
- GILLIGAN!
- SKIPPER!

1516
01:01:07,365 --> 01:01:09,400
GILLIGAN!

1517
01:01:09,433 --> 01:01:11,435
SKIPPER!

1518
01:01:11,468 --> 01:01:14,072
AND IF WE FAILED, IT WOULD
SET OUR WORK BACK

1519
01:01:14,105 --> 01:01:16,173
- AT LEAST 20 YEARS.
- BUMMER.

1520
01:01:16,207 --> 01:01:18,710
FURTHERMORE, THE FACILITIES
ARE NOT OURS ALONE.

1521
01:01:18,743 --> 01:01:20,412
- IT'S A TIME-SHARE.
- THIS IS A JOINT VENTURE

1522
01:01:20,445 --> 01:01:22,713
CREATED WITH THE HELP
OF THE UNITED STATES

1523
01:01:22,747 --> 01:01:24,148
AND THE SOVIET UNION.

1524
01:01:24,182 --> 01:01:26,083
- MM-HMM.
- AND WE WOULD REQUIRE
THEIR PERMISSION.

1525
01:01:26,117 --> 01:01:28,052
WELL, SINCE YOU
OWN THEIR COUNTRIES,

1526
01:01:28,085 --> 01:01:29,920
I THINK YOU COULD
CONVINCE THEM.

1527
01:01:32,190 --> 01:01:33,758
HANEDA CONTROL TOWER!

1528
01:01:33,792 --> 01:01:35,225
PLEASE COME IN,
PLEASE COME IN!

1529
01:01:35,258 --> 01:01:36,993
HANEDA CONTROL TOWER!

1530
01:01:37,027 --> 01:01:38,963
HANEDA CONTROL TOWER,
PLEASE COME IN!

1531
01:01:38,997 --> 01:01:40,163
WHY DON'T YOU ANSWER?

1532
01:01:40,197 --> 01:01:42,032
BECAUSE YOU'RE SO REDUNDANT.

1533
01:01:42,067 --> 01:01:44,768
OH! LOOK OUT THERE.

1534
01:01:44,802 --> 01:01:48,038
IN THE SKY!

1535
01:01:48,072 --> 01:01:50,207
OOH, THAT BIG-SCREEN TV
IS COOL.

1536
01:01:50,240 --> 01:01:52,177
- WELL, THEY INVENTED IT.
- THAT'S TRUE.

1537
01:01:52,210 --> 01:01:54,345
THE ONE AND ONLY.

1538
01:01:54,378 --> 01:01:57,448
NOW WHAT?

1539
01:01:57,482 --> 01:02:00,383
NEAT!

1540
01:02:00,418 --> 01:02:03,888
OKAY...

1541
01:02:03,922 --> 01:02:05,490
HOLY TRINITRON!

1542
01:02:05,523 --> 01:02:07,192
[ALL] OOH!

1543
01:02:10,327 --> 01:02:12,330
I'LL JUST PULL OVER HERE
AND CHECK MY FLUIDS.

1544
01:02:12,363 --> 01:02:15,165
AND, UH, JUST FIND
A PLACE TO PARK--

1545
01:02:15,198 --> 01:02:16,933
OHP, A LITTLE
TOO CLOSE TO THE PUMP.

1546
01:02:16,967 --> 01:02:18,837
- SORRY, THAT WAS ME.
- SO MUCH ABOUT KENNY'S THEORY

1547
01:02:18,870 --> 01:02:19,937
ABOUT HIM BEING
GOOD-HEARTED.

1548
01:02:19,970 --> 01:02:23,240
- GAMERA!
- YEAH.

1549
01:02:23,273 --> 01:02:25,477
KENNY AND THE KEN-TONES!

1550
01:02:25,510 --> 01:02:27,478
GAMERA JAMERA!

1551
01:02:27,512 --> 01:02:29,480
♪ I'VE GOT A TURTLE THAT'S
AS BIG AS A WHALE ♪

1552
01:02:29,513 --> 01:02:31,348
♪ AND IT'S ABOUT
TO SET SAIL ♪

1553
01:02:31,382 --> 01:02:35,185
WHOO!

1554
01:02:35,218 --> 01:02:39,023
DO THE HOU-CHOU FINISH!

1555
01:02:39,057 --> 01:02:42,860
AT LEAST THEY'RE WEARING
PRACTICAL SHOES.

1556
01:02:42,893 --> 01:02:44,928
WHAT IS THIS, ARE THEY IN
FOOTLOOSE ALL OF A SUDDEN?

1557
01:02:46,897 --> 01:02:48,132
GAMERA IS COMING, EVERYONE--

1558
01:02:48,165 --> 01:02:49,433
NO DANCING, NOT ALLOWED.

1559
01:02:49,467 --> 01:02:50,535
NO DANCING.

1560
01:02:50,568 --> 01:02:51,935
EVERYBODY CLEAR OUT!

1561
01:02:51,968 --> 01:02:53,203
EVERYBODY CLEAR OUT!

1562
01:02:53,237 --> 01:02:56,373
AWW.

1563
01:02:56,407 --> 01:02:57,875
HURRY, YOU HEAR THAT?

1564
01:02:57,908 --> 01:03:00,277
IT'S GAMERA, HURRY!
HURRY! EVERYBODY RUN!

1565
01:03:00,310 --> 01:03:02,180
DON'T YOU WANT TO LIVE?
GET MOVING!

1566
01:03:02,213 --> 01:03:04,182
AH, COOL IT, WILL YOU?
GAMERA DOESN'T SCARE US.

1567
01:03:04,215 --> 01:03:06,150
GO TO BED, OLD MAN!

1568
01:03:06,183 --> 01:03:07,985
WE'RE NOT AFRAID
OF A TURTLE, ARE WE?

1569
01:03:08,018 --> 01:03:09,153
- COME ON! MUSIC, MUSIC!
- DUMB OLD TURTLE.

1570
01:03:09,187 --> 01:03:10,353
WILL YOU SHUT UP?

1571
01:03:10,387 --> 01:03:12,823
- I SAID EVERYBODY OUT!
- DISCO TURTLES.

1572
01:03:12,857 --> 01:03:14,892
HAVE ALL OF YOU GONE CRAZY?

1573
01:03:14,925 --> 01:03:17,162
DID SOMEONE SAY TURTLE?

1574
01:03:17,195 --> 01:03:19,863
LOOK, IT'S GAMERA!

1575
01:03:19,897 --> 01:03:21,498
LOOK!

1576
01:03:21,532 --> 01:03:24,468
DO THE GAMERA!

1577
01:03:24,502 --> 01:03:26,303
COOL.

1578
01:03:26,337 --> 01:03:29,173
- ALL RIGHT,
GREAT DRUM SOLO.
- WHOO!

1579
01:03:29,207 --> 01:03:32,210
[PEOPLE SCREAM]

1580
01:03:32,243 --> 01:03:33,878
HEY, HE'S REALLY BRINGING
THE HOUSE DOWN, HUH?

1581
01:03:33,912 --> 01:03:36,513
YEAH, ROCK THAT TOWN
INSIDE-OUT.

1582
01:03:41,318 --> 01:03:44,855
OOH, GOTTA HURT.

1583
01:03:44,888 --> 01:03:46,023
DAEIII!

1584
01:03:46,057 --> 01:03:47,558
AH, THAT ONE WAS EASY.

1585
01:03:47,592 --> 01:03:49,860
I HARDLY TOUCHED IT.

1586
01:03:49,893 --> 01:03:51,095
OOPS, SORRY, THAT WAS ME.

1587
01:03:51,128 --> 01:03:52,930
EVACUATE THE CITY
IMMEDIATELY!

1588
01:03:52,963 --> 01:03:55,900
EVERYONE IS TO EVACUATE
IMMEDIATELY!

1589
01:03:55,933 --> 01:03:58,068
YOU ARE ORDERED TO EVACUATE
TO THE SUBURBS.

1590
01:03:58,102 --> 01:04:01,105
LIVE THE GOOD LIFE
IN THE OFF-WORLD COLONIES.

1591
01:04:03,273 --> 01:04:06,110
WELL, THERE'S A BUILDING
OVERTURNED ON HIGHWAY FIVE.

1592
01:04:06,143 --> 01:04:09,080
YOU'LL WANNA TAKE
AN ALTERNATE ROUTE.

1593
01:04:09,113 --> 01:04:11,015
NEW TOKYO?
I DON'T THINK SO.

1594
01:04:14,152 --> 01:04:17,955
ANYONE SEEN KENNY?

1595
01:04:17,988 --> 01:04:19,390
HERE'S A HOT NEW DANCE.

1596
01:04:24,928 --> 01:04:26,563
OKAY, SO IF WE GET
AN 18-PIECE BUCKET.

1597
01:04:26,597 --> 01:04:28,132
OH, SOMETHING SPLASHY,

1598
01:04:28,165 --> 01:04:30,668
I DON'T KNOW,
EXTRA CRISPY-- HUH?

1599
01:04:30,702 --> 01:04:33,070
THE BEST-LAID PLANS
OF MICE AND MEN.

1600
01:04:33,103 --> 01:04:35,138
WE'LL HAVE IT CATERED.
LET'S GO.

1601
01:04:35,172 --> 01:04:37,342
WELP, HE SAW LONDON.
HE SAW FRANCE.

1602
01:04:37,375 --> 01:04:39,910
- HE SAW RODAN'S UNDERPANTS.
- [CROW LAUGHS]

1603
01:04:43,613 --> 01:04:46,150
OH, EXCUSE ME, JUST IGNORE--

1604
01:04:46,183 --> 01:04:47,685
MY FAULT, I'M SORRY,
JUST GET THIS--

1605
01:04:47,718 --> 01:04:50,353
I WONDER HOW MANY TIMES
TOKYO TOWER HAS GONE DOWN.

1606
01:04:50,387 --> 01:04:53,090
HE JUST HATES THE MEMPHIS
DESIGN GROUP, THAT'S ALL.

1607
01:04:54,692 --> 01:04:57,060
WELL, NOW THAT WE HAVE
ALL THE GRILLS GOING,

1608
01:04:57,093 --> 01:04:59,297
LET'S GET READY
TO SAUTEE SOME PEOPLE, HUH?

1609
01:05:02,533 --> 01:05:04,402
WHAT, ARE THEY IN SUPERCAR?

1610
01:05:04,435 --> 01:05:07,103
[ALL] ♪ SUPERCAR! ♪

1611
01:05:07,137 --> 01:05:10,040
♪ SUPERCAR ♪

1612
01:05:10,073 --> 01:05:11,542
HAVE YOU SEEN KENNY?

1613
01:05:11,575 --> 01:05:13,177
OOH.

1614
01:05:16,213 --> 01:05:17,448
HOT FOOT ON THE FREEWAY.

1615
01:05:17,482 --> 01:05:20,383
MAN, THE INSURANCE
MUST BE REALLY EXPENSIVE.

1616
01:05:20,417 --> 01:05:22,320
YEAH.

1617
01:05:22,353 --> 01:05:25,488
UH, I'D LIKE
A SINGLE ROOM, PLEASE.

1618
01:05:25,522 --> 01:05:27,925
ESCAPE! ESCAPE TO WISCONSIN!

1619
01:05:31,695 --> 01:05:33,230
CRUNCHY ON THE OUTSIDE.

1620
01:05:33,263 --> 01:05:36,667
ROAST 'EM, TENDERIZE 'EM,
DOWN YOU GO.

1621
01:05:36,700 --> 01:05:39,170
OH, HEY, DON'T
GET SO NEGATIVE.

1622
01:05:39,203 --> 01:05:41,438
EVACUATE THE CITY AT ONCE!

1623
01:05:41,472 --> 01:05:43,640
EVERYBODY IS ORDERED
TO LEAVE THE CITY AT ONCE!

1624
01:05:43,673 --> 01:05:45,408
- KENNY.
- [ALL] AAH!

1625
01:05:45,442 --> 01:05:47,345
- HURRY, WE MUST
LEAVE RIGHT AWAY.
- DON'T DO THAT.

1626
01:05:47,378 --> 01:05:49,647
HURRY!

1627
01:05:49,680 --> 01:05:52,350
THERE'S STILL SO MUCH WORK
TO BE DONE THOUGH, SISTER.

1628
01:05:54,285 --> 01:05:56,020
KENNY, DID YOU HEAR
WHAT I SAID?

1629
01:05:56,053 --> 01:05:58,022
[SERVO GROWLS]

1630
01:05:58,055 --> 01:06:00,523
GAMERA, IT'S ME, KENNY.

1631
01:06:00,557 --> 01:06:02,192
DON'T DO ANYTHING BAD.

1632
01:06:02,225 --> 01:06:03,995
I AM YOUR BRIDE.

1633
01:06:04,028 --> 01:06:06,430
I HEAR YOU, KENNY,
AND I OBEY.

1634
01:06:06,463 --> 01:06:08,698
I'M JUST A SOUL
WHOSE INTENTIONS ARE GOOD.

1635
01:06:08,732 --> 01:06:12,337
PLEASE LORD, DON'T LET ME
BE MISUNDERSTOOD.

1636
01:06:20,110 --> 01:06:22,547
HERE AT EXXON, WE TAKE
THE GREATEST PRECAUTIONS

1637
01:06:22,580 --> 01:06:26,383
FOR THE PRESERVATION
OF OUR FRAGILE ECOLOGY.

1638
01:06:26,417 --> 01:06:30,053
HERE'S THE EXXON VALDEZ
AT PORT.

1639
01:06:30,087 --> 01:06:33,223
THAT'S OUR PLUCKY CAPTAIN
AFTER A COUPLE OF COCKTAILS.

1640
01:06:33,257 --> 01:06:37,027
- N.Y.P.D.
- FRANK CONVERSE.

1641
01:06:37,060 --> 01:06:38,395
- JACK WARDEN.
- IS THAT EVERYTHING?

1642
01:06:38,428 --> 01:06:39,730
WELL, WE DON'T HAVE
KENNY'S ROCKS.

1643
01:06:39,763 --> 01:06:41,265
OH, DID YOU SEE KENNY?

1644
01:06:41,298 --> 01:06:43,600
NO, NOT SINCE YESTERDAY.

1645
01:06:43,633 --> 01:06:45,235
[SIRENS BLARE]

1646
01:06:47,438 --> 01:06:48,638
OH, COME ON,
WHO'S SHE KIDDING?

1647
01:06:48,672 --> 01:06:50,373
SHE'S BEEN WISHING FOR THIS
SINCE FRAME ONE.

1648
01:06:50,407 --> 01:06:52,042
KENNY!

1649
01:06:52,075 --> 01:06:55,245
DAMIAN? DAMIAN?

1650
01:06:55,278 --> 01:06:57,782
HAVE ANOTHER
DEVILED EGG, DAMIAN.

1651
01:07:00,785 --> 01:07:02,252
AAH, FORGET HIM.

1652
01:07:02,285 --> 01:07:04,322
- PRUNES!
- EXPLAIN TO ME,
DR. HIDAKA,

1653
01:07:04,355 --> 01:07:06,423
I THINK THE Z-PLAN
MUST BE SUPERVISED

1654
01:07:06,457 --> 01:07:08,525
ONLY BY UNITED NATIONS
SCIENTISTS.

1655
01:07:08,558 --> 01:07:11,362
- MM.
- I REALIZE THAT GAMERA
IS VERY DANGEROUS.

1656
01:07:11,395 --> 01:07:14,232
HOWEVER, WE MUST INSIST
ON TOTAL CONTROL.

1657
01:07:14,265 --> 01:07:16,467
AS FOR MY GOVERNMENT,
I ASSURE YOU, DOCTOR,

1658
01:07:16,500 --> 01:07:18,535
YOU HAVE OUR UTMOST SUPPORT.

1659
01:07:18,568 --> 01:07:20,137
- OH, THANK YOU, TOPOL.
- ONLY SUCH A DANGEROUS PLAN--

1660
01:07:20,170 --> 01:07:21,472
JEEZ, HE IS HARD
TO WORK WITH.

1661
01:07:21,505 --> 01:07:23,373
- BY THE UNITED NATIONS.
- I UNDERSTAND, THANK YOU.

1662
01:07:23,407 --> 01:07:24,442
AND I APPRECIATE
YOUR HELP.

1663
01:07:24,475 --> 01:07:26,677
MY COUNTRY WILL
ALWAYS BE INDEBTED.

1664
01:07:26,710 --> 01:07:28,378
NOW GET OFF MY FOOT.

1665
01:07:28,412 --> 01:07:30,080
THERE'S ONE THING--
WE CAN'T BE READY

1666
01:07:30,113 --> 01:07:32,082
FOR ANOTHER 24 HOURS.

1667
01:07:32,115 --> 01:07:33,417
AND THAT'S AT THE EARLIEST.

1668
01:07:33,450 --> 01:07:36,120
THE QUESTION IS,
WHAT ACTION CAN BE TAKEN

1669
01:07:36,153 --> 01:07:37,422
AGAINST GAMERA
IN THE MEANTIME?

1670
01:07:37,455 --> 01:07:39,857
- AUDITION!
- WELL, YOU SEE,
AS A ZOOLOGIST,

1671
01:07:39,890 --> 01:07:42,793
I BELIEVE THAT
GAMERA'S VIOLENT NATURE

1672
01:07:42,827 --> 01:07:45,628
STEMS MAINLY FROM A DEFICIENCY
IN HIS ENERGY SUPPLY.

1673
01:07:45,662 --> 01:07:47,197
- CROW?
- RIGHT NOW,

1674
01:07:47,230 --> 01:07:50,500
GAMERA IS AT A COAL-
PROCESSING PLANT

1675
01:07:50,533 --> 01:07:52,368
DEVOURING FLAMES,
ITS FAVORITE FOOD.

1676
01:07:52,402 --> 01:07:54,572
- MM.
- HE LIKES CAJUN, GO FIGURE.

1677
01:07:54,605 --> 01:07:56,307
--EIGHT HOURS,
AND AT THAT POINT,

1678
01:07:56,340 --> 01:07:58,142
GAMERA WILL BE IN A MUCH
WEAKER CONDITION.

1679
01:07:58,175 --> 01:07:59,643
I VOTE RED DOT.

1680
01:07:59,677 --> 01:08:03,347
IN THAT CASE, TO KEEP THE RISK
TO AN ABSOLUTE MINIMUM,

1681
01:08:03,380 --> 01:08:05,515
GAMERA SHOULD BE
KEPT THERE FOR 24 HOURS.

1682
01:08:05,548 --> 01:08:07,685
THAT'S RIGHT.
AND TO DO THAT,

1683
01:08:07,718 --> 01:08:09,587
- GOOD LUCK.
- ...WE MUST BRING PETROLEUM.

1684
01:08:09,620 --> 01:08:11,455
AND KEEP THE FIRES BURNING

1685
01:08:11,488 --> 01:08:14,090
- UNTIL WE ARE
TOTALLY READY WITH Z-PLAN.
- [SERVO HUMS]

1686
01:08:15,458 --> 01:08:18,528
INDUSTRY! RESPONDING
TO GOVERNMENT'S NEEDS!

1687
01:08:18,562 --> 01:08:21,765
[SERVO HUMS]

1688
01:08:21,798 --> 01:08:24,402
ONE SHINING STEEL RAIL.

1689
01:08:24,435 --> 01:08:26,470
RUN FROM KENNY!

1690
01:08:26,503 --> 01:08:28,605
[ALL SCREAM]

1691
01:08:28,638 --> 01:08:30,440
[PEOPLE CLAMOR]

1692
01:08:34,845 --> 01:08:37,848
WHY? WHY?

1693
01:08:37,882 --> 01:08:41,385
THIS WORLD WAS NEVER MEANT
FOR ONE AS BEAUTIFUL AS ME.

1694
01:08:41,418 --> 01:08:43,620
GAMERA, HONEY,
DON'T GO OUT TOO FAR.

1695
01:08:43,653 --> 01:08:44,855
YOU JUST ATE.

1696
01:08:47,858 --> 01:08:49,727
I BET IT'S LIKE BATHWATER
OUT THERE TOO.

1697
01:08:51,728 --> 01:08:55,265
WHOA.

1698
01:08:55,298 --> 01:08:56,500
IT'S DAY OVER THERE
AND NIGHT OVER THERE.

1699
01:08:56,533 --> 01:08:58,735
EVERY ONE OF OUR STORAGE TANKS
WILL BE WRECKED.

1700
01:08:58,768 --> 01:09:00,270
I THINK YOUR
HELMET'S TOO TIGHT.

1701
01:09:00,303 --> 01:09:03,740
I UNDERSTAND. OKAY.

1702
01:09:03,773 --> 01:09:06,543
[JOEL AS JOHN WAYNE]
COME ON, THE WAR'S
A-THIS-WAY, PILGRIM.

1703
01:09:06,577 --> 01:09:08,212
ALL RIGHT!

1704
01:09:12,415 --> 01:09:13,817
COME RIDE THE LITTLE TRAIN

1705
01:09:13,850 --> 01:09:16,153
THAT'S GOING DOWN
THE TRACKS TO HELL.

1706
01:09:21,758 --> 01:09:23,360
[CROW LAUGHS]

1707
01:09:23,393 --> 01:09:25,628
AND-- AND THAT'S
THE TANKS I GET?

1708
01:09:25,662 --> 01:09:28,432
- OH, THAT'S GREAT.
- OW! OW!

1709
01:09:28,465 --> 01:09:30,200
- HEY.
- THAT WAS HIS ARM.

1710
01:09:30,233 --> 01:09:33,503
I NEED THAT.

1711
01:09:33,537 --> 01:09:36,707
OUCH.

1712
01:09:36,740 --> 01:09:39,477
OOH, THAT WAS THE MIDNIGHT
TRAIN TO GAMERA.

1713
01:09:39,510 --> 01:09:40,878
♪ I'D RATHER LIVE
IN HIS WORLD ♪

1714
01:09:40,912 --> 01:09:42,378
♪ THEN LIVE
WITHOUT HIM IN MINE ♪

1715
01:09:42,412 --> 01:09:43,547
DID IT WORK?

1716
01:09:43,580 --> 01:09:44,648
THIS IS GAMERA,
KNOCK IT OFF.

1717
01:09:44,682 --> 01:09:47,417
OKAY, RIGHT AWAY.

1718
01:09:47,450 --> 01:09:49,287
ALL RIGHT, ANOTHER TANK.

1719
01:09:49,320 --> 01:09:50,787
THEY NEED ANOTHER 24 HOURS.

1720
01:09:50,820 --> 01:09:52,723
YOU'D BETTER GET GOING.
MOVE IT!

1721
01:09:56,960 --> 01:09:58,962
THEY WANNA SEND
ANOTHER TANK.

1722
01:09:58,995 --> 01:10:00,397
ARE YOU READY?

1723
01:10:00,430 --> 01:10:02,532
ALL TANKED UP, SIR!

1724
01:10:02,567 --> 01:10:04,335
WATCH IT.

1725
01:10:07,938 --> 01:10:10,307
GAMERA?

1726
01:10:10,340 --> 01:10:12,442
KENNY! WHAT TOOK SO LONG?

1727
01:10:16,647 --> 01:10:18,848
[SERVO GROWLS]

1728
01:10:18,882 --> 01:10:21,352
HUH, HEY,
THEY'RE IN SECTIONS,

1729
01:10:21,385 --> 01:10:22,787
SO YOU CAN JUST TAKE
AS MUCH AS YOU WANT.

1730
01:10:22,820 --> 01:10:24,655
TAKE ALL YOU WANT,
BUT EAT ALL YOU TAKE.

1731
01:10:24,688 --> 01:10:27,725
YEAH.

1732
01:10:27,758 --> 01:10:31,328
KENNY AS WOODY GUTHRIE
IN BOUND FOR GAMERA.

1733
01:10:31,362 --> 01:10:33,397
LOOK, THERE'S A BOY
THERE ON THE CAR.

1734
01:10:33,430 --> 01:10:34,832
HEY.

1735
01:10:34,865 --> 01:10:38,602
- YOU'LL GET KILLED!
- HUH?

1736
01:10:38,635 --> 01:10:40,370
HEY, THAT GUY'S
RISKING HIS LIFE,

1737
01:10:40,403 --> 01:10:41,538
AND HE'S NOT EVEN
THE STAR OF THE MOVIE.

1738
01:10:41,572 --> 01:10:44,442
GAMERA!

1739
01:10:44,475 --> 01:10:46,477
I HURT. I REALLY HURT.

1740
01:10:46,510 --> 01:10:47,543
KENNY!

1741
01:10:50,480 --> 01:10:53,383
WHEE! IT'S FUN.

1742
01:10:56,420 --> 01:10:57,988
GAMERA, I'M COMING TO BE
IN UNION WITH YOU!

1743
01:11:01,792 --> 01:11:03,427
HEY! COME HERE!

1744
01:11:03,460 --> 01:11:04,995
- COME HERE!
- LEAVE ME ALONE!

1745
01:11:05,028 --> 01:11:06,630
DON'T TOUCH ME! INFIDEL!

1746
01:11:06,663 --> 01:11:07,632
I DON'T WANNA GO!

1747
01:11:07,665 --> 01:11:09,433
I... SHALL MAKE YOU PAY!

1748
01:11:09,467 --> 01:11:10,733
COME BACK HERE!

1749
01:11:10,767 --> 01:11:12,602
I DON'T WANNA GET OFF!

1750
01:11:12,637 --> 01:11:14,672
- I'M A TOYS R US KID.
- LET GO OF ME!

1751
01:11:14,705 --> 01:11:17,007
AAH!

1752
01:11:17,040 --> 01:11:18,842
[ALL APPLAUD, WHISTLE]

1753
01:11:26,017 --> 01:11:29,420
KENNY?

1754
01:11:29,453 --> 01:11:31,822
COME ON.

1755
01:11:31,855 --> 01:11:33,423
ALL RIGHT.

1756
01:11:33,457 --> 01:11:34,992
COME ON.

1757
01:11:39,597 --> 01:11:40,797
- COME ON.
[SERVO MIMICS TRAIN]
- PUT ME DOWN!

1758
01:11:40,830 --> 01:11:42,398
WOW, THAT BLAST
REALLY SHOOK HIM UP.

1759
01:11:42,432 --> 01:11:44,100
HE THINKS HE'S A TRAIN NOW.

1760
01:11:44,133 --> 01:11:46,670
YEAH, I'D CURE HIM,
BUT I NEED THE RIDE.

1761
01:11:46,703 --> 01:11:48,405
RUN, BUD RYAN!

1762
01:11:48,438 --> 01:11:51,608
SPANKING MACHINE ON KENNY.

1763
01:11:51,642 --> 01:11:53,543
YOU KNOW, YOU NEARLY
GOT US BOTH KILLED.

1764
01:11:53,577 --> 01:11:54,745
YOU'D BETTER GO HOME.

1765
01:11:54,778 --> 01:11:56,780
NO, GAMERA'S MY FRIEND.
HE'S GOOD.

1766
01:11:56,813 --> 01:11:59,450
YEAH, I KNOW, I KNOW.
HERE, PUT THIS ON.

1767
01:11:59,483 --> 01:12:01,485
HEY KID, GET A DOG,
WOULD YOU?

1768
01:12:01,518 --> 01:12:03,120
- [ALL LAUGH AT KENNY]
- [SOLDIERS LAUGH]

1769
01:12:03,153 --> 01:12:05,388
I'LL SAY GOODBYE
TO GAMERA FOR YOU.

1770
01:12:05,422 --> 01:12:06,623
YOU GONNA CRY?

1771
01:12:06,657 --> 01:12:07,792
- ONE-TWO-THREE
- [ALL] CRY!

1772
01:12:07,825 --> 01:12:08,958
- ONE-TWO-THREE
- [ALL] CRY!

1773
01:12:08,992 --> 01:12:10,393
- GENTLEMEN.
- START YOUR ENGINES.

1774
01:12:10,427 --> 01:12:13,097
I HAVE EXCELLENT NEWS.
I AM PROUD TO ANNOUNCE

1775
01:12:13,130 --> 01:12:15,732
THAT Z-PLAN
HAS BEEN COMPLETED

1776
01:12:15,765 --> 01:12:17,667
AND IS AT YOUR DISPOSAL.

1777
01:12:17,702 --> 01:12:19,470
- SO?
- THE WORLD'S
LATEST TECHNOLOGY

1778
01:12:19,503 --> 01:12:22,505
STANDS READY FOR YOUR
STRUGGLE AGAINST GAMERA.

1779
01:12:22,538 --> 01:12:24,642
- THAT'S REALLY NEAT.
-THE QUESTION IS,

1780
01:12:24,675 --> 01:12:27,477
HOW CAN WE LURE GAMERA
TO OUR NEW INSTALLATION

1781
01:12:27,510 --> 01:12:29,012
LOCATED AT OSHIMA?

1782
01:12:29,045 --> 01:12:30,780
- SEND HIM AN INVITATION.
- I'M SURE IT'S QUITE OBVIOUS

1783
01:12:30,813 --> 01:12:32,382
TO EVERYONE PRESENT
THAT WE WILL

1784
01:12:32,415 --> 01:12:33,917
NOT BE ABLE
TO CARRY OUT OUR PLAN

1785
01:12:33,950 --> 01:12:36,387
IF WE CANNOT
GET GAMERA THERE.

1786
01:12:36,420 --> 01:12:38,788
PROFESSOR MURASE,
I HAVE A SUGGESTION.

1787
01:12:38,822 --> 01:12:42,658
- OKAY.
- DR. HIDAKA,
PLEASE CONTINUE.

1788
01:12:42,692 --> 01:12:44,962
TO MAKE CERTAIN
GAMERA GOES TO OSHIMA,

1789
01:12:44,995 --> 01:12:47,063
WE MUST USE SPECIAL TACTICS.

1790
01:12:47,097 --> 01:12:48,832
- OR USE THIS MAP.
- YOU SEE...

1791
01:12:48,865 --> 01:12:50,400
OH, HE IS.

1792
01:12:50,433 --> 01:12:51,835
RIGHT NOW, THE WHOLE CITY
OF OSHIMA--

1793
01:12:51,868 --> 01:12:53,737
- HEY, WHO'S TALKING?
- WHAT'S GOING ON?

1794
01:12:53,770 --> 01:12:55,872
THE CITY IS OFF-LIMITS
TO CIVILIANS.

1795
01:12:55,905 --> 01:12:58,808
NOT EVEN THE PRESS
IS ALLOWED TO ENTER THE AREA.

1796
01:12:58,842 --> 01:13:00,943
KENNY, HOWEVER, IS FREE
TO MOVE ABOUT.

1797
01:13:03,647 --> 01:13:06,083
- WELL, IT'S GOODBYE
FOR A WHILE.
- AWW.

1798
01:13:06,117 --> 01:13:08,085
IT'S NOT FAIR.
WE'VE ALWAYS WORKED TOGETHER.

1799
01:13:08,118 --> 01:13:09,820
SHUTTING ME OUT ISN'T NICE.

1800
01:13:09,853 --> 01:13:12,588
IT'S A PITY THEY JUST
DON'T WANT REPORTERS ALONG.

1801
01:13:12,622 --> 01:13:13,890
BUT WE'LL COME BACK SOON.

1802
01:13:13,923 --> 01:13:15,692
SURE. JUST THE SAME,

1803
01:13:15,725 --> 01:13:17,627
I HATE BEING SEPARATED
FROM MY GODDESS.

1804
01:13:17,660 --> 01:13:19,128
- [GIGGLES]
- WELL, GOODBYE.

1805
01:13:19,162 --> 01:13:20,563
I'LL BE STALKING YOU
AT NIGHT.

1806
01:13:20,597 --> 01:13:21,732
MURASE IS STAYING HERE.

1807
01:13:21,765 --> 01:13:23,467
IF YOU WANT NEWS OF US,

1808
01:13:23,500 --> 01:13:25,202
- CONTACT HIM
AT THE UNIVERSITY.
- RIGHT.

1809
01:13:25,235 --> 01:13:28,672
- GOODBYE.
- SEE YOU SOON.

1810
01:13:28,705 --> 01:13:31,708
LOVE ME... LOVE ME!

1811
01:13:31,742 --> 01:13:34,778
OMAHA BEACH.
JUNE 5TH, 1945.

1812
01:13:34,812 --> 01:13:36,947
McHALE!

1813
01:13:36,980 --> 01:13:38,915
HEY.

1814
01:13:38,948 --> 01:13:40,883
LOOKS LIKE THEY'RE
SETTING UP A WEDDING.

1815
01:13:40,917 --> 01:13:43,153
I HOPE THE CRAB PUFFS
HOLD OUT.
- [SERVO HUMS]

1816
01:13:43,187 --> 01:13:45,188
OKAY, EVERYBODY
OFF THE TRUCKS.

1817
01:13:45,222 --> 01:13:47,858
- LIKE THIS?
- MOVE IT! MOVE IT!

1818
01:13:47,892 --> 01:13:50,793
MOVE IT! LET'S GO, LET'S GO!

1819
01:13:50,827 --> 01:13:53,163
- [JOEL JOINS HUMMING]
- MOVE IT!

1820
01:13:53,197 --> 01:13:56,667
FOUR SCORE AND-- OH, SORRY.

1821
01:13:56,700 --> 01:13:59,470
HE'S GONNA GET PRUNE HANDS,
STAYING IN THE TUB LIKE THAT.

1822
01:13:59,503 --> 01:14:01,738
HAS DR. HIDAKA LEFT
FOR OSHIMA YET?

1823
01:14:01,772 --> 01:14:05,642
YES. HE WAS ON
THE VERY LAST FLIGHT.

1824
01:14:05,675 --> 01:14:08,778
I CERTAINLY HOPE GAMERA
GOES TO OSHIMA SOON.

1825
01:14:08,812 --> 01:14:10,747
GO TO OSHIMA.

1826
01:14:10,780 --> 01:14:13,717
MAN, APARTMENTS IN TOKYO
ARE HARD TO FIND.

1827
01:14:13,750 --> 01:14:15,652
YEAH.

1828
01:14:15,685 --> 01:14:17,520
[SERVO HUMS]

1829
01:14:17,553 --> 01:14:19,490
DON KNOTTS, A GIANT TURTLE,

1830
01:14:19,523 --> 01:14:23,160
AND A JAPANESE STOWAWAY
ADD UP TO KOOKY FUN IN--

1831
01:14:23,193 --> 01:14:24,695
COME ON, LET'S
GET OUT OF HERE.

1832
01:14:24,728 --> 01:14:25,928
UH, CAN I GET MY ARM--

1833
01:14:25,962 --> 01:14:28,032
OH, DON'T WORRY, CROW,
WE GOT A SPARE UPSTAIRS.

1834
01:14:41,645 --> 01:14:43,847
IT'S HIS CUTICLES, I WISH
I COULD STAY SO THIN.

1835
01:14:43,880 --> 01:14:46,015
WHAT?

1836
01:14:46,048 --> 01:14:47,783
BOY, THIS MAGAZINE KILLS ME.
LOOK AT THIS.

1837
01:14:47,817 --> 01:14:50,020
HELP FOR YOUR HIPS.

1838
01:14:50,053 --> 01:14:51,888
CUCUMBER POULTICE
YOU CAN MAKE AT HOME.

1839
01:14:51,922 --> 01:14:53,157
HUH, YEAH RIGHT.

1840
01:14:53,190 --> 01:14:54,223
WHAT? HUH?

1841
01:14:54,257 --> 01:14:57,660
I SAID, "CUCUMBER POULTICE."
CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

1842
01:14:57,693 --> 01:14:59,195
UH, WHAT? UH, OH...

1843
01:14:59,228 --> 01:15:01,063
GYPSY,
TURN THIS THING OFF.

1844
01:15:01,097 --> 01:15:03,967
- WHAT? OH, OKAY.
- YEAH.

1845
01:15:04,000 --> 01:15:06,135
OH, MAN, MY HEAD ITCHES.

1846
01:15:06,168 --> 01:15:07,737
GEE, I HOPE I DON'T GET
A RASH ON MY NECK.

1847
01:15:07,770 --> 01:15:09,005
OH, WILL YOU
LOOK AT THE TIME?

1848
01:15:09,038 --> 01:15:10,873
I GOTTA GET
TO THE STORE YET,

1849
01:15:10,907 --> 01:15:12,675
AND THEN I GOTTA
GRAB THE KIDS BY THREE,

1850
01:15:12,708 --> 01:15:13,610
- BECAUSE, YOU KNOW,
WILBUR'S GOT--
- WHOA.

1851
01:15:13,643 --> 01:15:15,212
FORGET THE KIDS, CROW.
WE GOT A VISITOR.

1852
01:15:15,245 --> 01:15:17,013
CAMBOT, LET'S CHECK OUT
ROCKET NUMBER NINE.

1853
01:15:17,047 --> 01:15:19,248
HEY, TURN ON
THAT VIEWSCREEN.

1854
01:15:23,087 --> 01:15:26,223
- IT'S GAMERA.
- BY GOLLY, IT IS GAMERA.

1855
01:15:26,257 --> 01:15:28,192
OH GREAT, THE VISIT
OF THE CENTURY

1856
01:15:28,225 --> 01:15:29,727
- AND ME IN ROLLERS.
- SHH!

1857
01:15:29,760 --> 01:15:31,127
HEY, BIG TURTLE GUY.

1858
01:15:31,160 --> 01:15:33,230
HI BOYS, I WAS
JUST FINISHING UP

1859
01:15:33,263 --> 01:15:34,898
SOME OF MY LAUNDRY HERE.

1860
01:15:34,932 --> 01:15:37,667
YOU KNOW, GREAT THING ABOUT
BEING A TURTLE IS, UH,

1861
01:15:37,700 --> 01:15:39,302
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO SEPARATE YOUR WASH.

1862
01:15:39,335 --> 01:15:40,903
BECAUSE IT'S ALL GREEN.

1863
01:15:40,937 --> 01:15:42,605
ANYWAY, I STOPPED IN, UH--

1864
01:15:42,638 --> 01:15:44,240
CAN I BORROW A, UH,
CLING-FREE?

1865
01:15:44,273 --> 01:15:46,710
- YOU GOT ONE LAYING AROUND?
- UH, WELL, SURE,

1866
01:15:46,743 --> 01:15:48,845
IF YOU WOULDN'T MIND
ANSWERING A COUPLE OF QUESTIONS

1867
01:15:48,878 --> 01:15:50,747
ABOUT LIFE AS
A SIX-STORY TURTLE.

1868
01:15:50,780 --> 01:15:52,048
NO, NO-- NO PROBLEM.
GO AHEAD.

1869
01:15:52,082 --> 01:15:53,750
OKAY, WELL,
WHY DO YOU GO ABOUT

1870
01:15:53,783 --> 01:15:55,318
STOMPING ON CITIES
AND STUFF?

1871
01:15:55,352 --> 01:15:57,053
WELL, IT'S NOT MY FAULT.

1872
01:15:57,087 --> 01:15:58,655
LISTEN,
I'M BIG-BONED, RIGHT?

1873
01:15:58,688 --> 01:16:00,990
AND LET'S FACE IT.
CITY PLANNERS DISCRIMINATE

1874
01:16:01,023 --> 01:16:02,592
AGAINST THESE
BIG-BONE TYPES, RIGHT?

1875
01:16:02,625 --> 01:16:04,795
THE OTHER DAY, I WENT INTO
A LIBRARY TURNSTILE.

1876
01:16:04,828 --> 01:16:07,130
GOT STUCK.
BEAR GREASE, JAWS OF LIFE.

1877
01:16:07,163 --> 01:16:08,898
FIRE DEPARTMENT CAME.
THE WHOLE MESS.

1878
01:16:08,932 --> 01:16:10,967
AND, UH, I WAS IN A LOT OF PAIN,
LET ME TELL YOU.

1879
01:16:11,000 --> 01:16:12,035
OF COURSE, YOU'D KNOW
ABOUT PAIN.

1880
01:16:12,068 --> 01:16:13,803
YOU'VE SEEN SPALDING GRAY.

1881
01:16:13,837 --> 01:16:15,305
- YOU KNOW WHAT I'M SAYING?
- UH-HUH.

1882
01:16:15,338 --> 01:16:17,240
WELL, SO WHAT'S THE DEAL
WITH THAT BOY KENNY?

1883
01:16:17,273 --> 01:16:19,308
YOU GUYS SEEM
TO BE SUCH CHUMS.

1884
01:16:19,342 --> 01:16:21,143
KENNY, KENNY KENNY KENNY.

1885
01:16:21,177 --> 01:16:22,878
LITTLE, SWEET KENNY.

1886
01:16:22,912 --> 01:16:24,682
THE DEAL WITH KENNY IS,
HE'S A GOOD KID.

1887
01:16:24,715 --> 01:16:26,082
GOOD-HEARTED,
DON'T GET ME WRONG.

1888
01:16:26,115 --> 01:16:28,718
BUT, UH, I'M USING HIM.

1889
01:16:28,752 --> 01:16:29,887
YOU KNOW,
'CAUSE LET'S FACE IT.

1890
01:16:29,920 --> 01:16:32,088
HE SOFTENS UP MY IMAGE,
YOU KNOW? RIGHT?

1891
01:16:32,122 --> 01:16:33,923
- KENNY.
- WELL, I--

1892
01:16:33,957 --> 01:16:35,392
WELL, LOOK, I CAN
SMASH A HUGE CITY,

1893
01:16:35,425 --> 01:16:37,827
TAKE OUT THOUSANDS
OF PEOPLE, RIGHT?

1894
01:16:37,860 --> 01:16:39,095
SAY, A SUBURB OF OSAKI.

1895
01:16:39,128 --> 01:16:40,763
KILL TEN MILLION.

1896
01:16:40,797 --> 01:16:43,200
AND THEN, UH, YOU KNOW,
WITH KENNY AT MY SIDE,

1897
01:16:43,233 --> 01:16:46,303
I LOOK LIKE JIMMY STEWART IN
MR. SMITH GOES TO WASHINGTON.

1898
01:16:46,337 --> 01:16:47,903
IT'S GREAT.
LET ME TELL YOU SOMETHING

1899
01:16:47,937 --> 01:16:49,707
ABOUT THAT UNCONDITIONAL
LOVE, CHILDREN.

1900
01:16:49,740 --> 01:16:51,675
IT FEELS REALLY GOOD.

1901
01:16:51,708 --> 01:16:53,110
- [PHONE RINGS]
- OH, EXCUSE ME.

1902
01:16:53,143 --> 01:16:56,045
GOTTA TAKE THIS.

1903
01:16:56,078 --> 01:16:57,747
HELLO?

1904
01:16:57,780 --> 01:16:59,950
GODZILLA,
HOW ARE YOU, BUDDY?

1905
01:16:59,983 --> 01:17:01,385
YEAH, YEAH,
READ THE SCRIPT, LOVE IT.

1906
01:17:01,418 --> 01:17:02,252
I GOT A TITLE SUGGESTION
FOR YOU.

1907
01:17:02,285 --> 01:17:05,288
SEE HOW THIS GRABS YOU
BY THE PO-PO.

1908
01:17:05,322 --> 01:17:08,258
UH, HOW ABOUT
GAMERA VS. GODZILLA?

1909
01:17:08,292 --> 01:17:09,927
YEAH.

1910
01:17:12,997 --> 01:17:14,397
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.
RIGHT. RIGHT.

1911
01:17:14,430 --> 01:17:16,032
WE-- YEAH, NO,
WE CAN CHANGE IT.

1912
01:17:16,065 --> 01:17:18,102
CALL MY AGENT.

1913
01:17:18,135 --> 01:17:20,970
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.
ALL RIGHT, BYE.

1914
01:17:21,003 --> 01:17:23,073
OH, LISTEN, I GOTTA GET GOING.
GOT A FEW MORE THINGS TO DO.

1915
01:17:23,107 --> 01:17:24,173
BUT, UH, IT'S BEEN NICE
TALKING TO YOU,

1916
01:17:24,207 --> 01:17:26,410
AND REMEMBER-- REMEMBER WHAT
THIS TURTLE TOLD YOU.

1917
01:17:26,443 --> 01:17:28,112
KEEP YOUR SHELL IN THE SUN,

1918
01:17:28,145 --> 01:17:30,847
AND ALWAYS KEEP REACHING
FOR THE STARS.

1919
01:17:30,880 --> 01:17:32,682
- BYE.
- BYE.
- IF YOU SEE TIBBY,

1920
01:17:32,715 --> 01:17:33,950
TELL HER I SAID HELLO.

1921
01:17:33,983 --> 01:17:35,218
HUH. NEAT.

1922
01:17:35,252 --> 01:17:36,887
FEEL I KIND OF LIKED
THAT TURTLE.

1923
01:17:36,920 --> 01:17:39,022
SEEMS LIKE SUCH A NICE GUY.

1924
01:17:39,055 --> 01:17:41,392
YEAH, SO NOBLE. SO PROUD.

1925
01:17:41,425 --> 01:17:44,060
SO BIG.

1926
01:17:44,093 --> 01:17:46,830
HEY, DO YOU THINK
I LOOK FAT?

1927
01:17:46,863 --> 01:17:48,165
- NO, NOT AT ALL.
- OH, I THINK I DO.

1928
01:17:55,872 --> 01:17:57,107
PROFESSOR MURASE,
A VISITOR FOR YOU.

1929
01:17:57,140 --> 01:17:58,342
HEY JOEL, YOU WON'T BELIEVE IT,
REALLY COOL.

1930
01:17:58,375 --> 01:17:59,743
WE JUST MET GAMERA.
HE'S REALLY COOL.

1931
01:17:59,777 --> 01:18:01,043
HE'S A REALLY NEAT GUY.

1932
01:18:01,077 --> 01:18:02,145
IT'S KENNY--

1933
01:18:02,178 --> 01:18:03,813
- WE JUST MET GAMERA--
- I HEARD.

1934
01:18:03,847 --> 01:18:05,148
- OH YEAH.
- YEAH, SURE.

1935
01:18:05,182 --> 01:18:07,417
AND YOU KNOW SNUFFLEUPAGUS
TOO, RIGHT?

1936
01:18:07,450 --> 01:18:09,753
- HE DOESN'T BELIEVE US.
- AND THEN HE SUDDENLY VANISHED.

1937
01:18:09,787 --> 01:18:11,788
YOU SEE, HE WAS ALWAYS
TALKING ABOUT GAMERA.

1938
01:18:11,822 --> 01:18:14,457
- SO I THOUGHT THAT MAYBE--
- KENNY? GAMERA?

1939
01:18:14,490 --> 01:18:16,760
HMM. ♪ DEATH TO THE WORLD ♪

1940
01:18:16,793 --> 01:18:19,228
♪ I SHALL BE QUICK
AND I'LL BE... ♪

1941
01:18:19,262 --> 01:18:21,832
YEAH, OKAY, I GOT IT.

1942
01:18:21,865 --> 01:18:23,933
SURE, OKAY.

1943
01:18:23,967 --> 01:18:26,035
- UH, PEPPERONI,
EXTRA CHEESE.
- LAST BOAT'S JUST ARRIVED.

1944
01:18:26,068 --> 01:18:27,370
RIGHT.

1945
01:18:27,403 --> 01:18:28,838
OKAY, THEY'LL
TAKE CARE OF IT.

1946
01:18:28,872 --> 01:18:30,273
30 MINUTES?

1947
01:18:30,307 --> 01:18:31,975
ONCE A GARDEN SPOT.

1948
01:18:32,008 --> 01:18:33,943
NOW A PLAYGROUND OF DEATH.

1949
01:18:36,413 --> 01:18:39,115
[SERVO HUMS]

1950
01:18:39,148 --> 01:18:40,883
AND DO YOU TAKE
THIS MAN TO BE

1951
01:18:40,917 --> 01:18:42,485
YOUR LAWFULLY
WEDDED HUSBAND?

1952
01:18:42,518 --> 01:18:44,187
LET GO OF ME!

1953
01:18:44,220 --> 01:18:45,822
- YOU'RE COMING WITH ME.
- LET GO!

1954
01:18:45,855 --> 01:18:47,090
- IS THAT WHO I THINK IT IS?
- WHAT'S GOING ON?

1955
01:18:47,123 --> 01:18:49,258
A STOWAWAY, SIR.
A LITTLE BOY.

1956
01:18:49,292 --> 01:18:51,462
- A LITTLE BOY?
- [ALL] OH NO.

1957
01:18:51,495 --> 01:18:53,097
- IT'S KENNY!
- KENNY.

1958
01:18:53,130 --> 01:18:55,432
- HERE HE IS, SIR.
- D'OH.

1959
01:18:55,465 --> 01:18:57,467
I WAS WORRIED ABOUT GAMERA.

1960
01:18:57,500 --> 01:19:00,470
[ALL] WAH-WAH-WAAAAH.

1961
01:19:00,503 --> 01:19:03,807
KENNY, YOU'RE A FRIEND
OF GAMERA, HUH?

1962
01:19:03,840 --> 01:19:05,142
- MM-HMM.
- OH, VERY MUCH SO.

1963
01:19:05,175 --> 01:19:08,778
- LET'S GO.
- I AM HIS KEYMASTER.

1964
01:19:08,812 --> 01:19:10,447
- WELL--
- TEA-TIME.

1965
01:19:10,480 --> 01:19:12,348
LET'S BEGIN.

1966
01:19:12,382 --> 01:19:13,983
DR. HIDAKA,

1967
01:19:14,017 --> 01:19:16,787
ARE YOU SURE IT'S POSSIBLE
TO BRING GAMERA HERE?

1968
01:19:16,820 --> 01:19:18,122
OF COURSE.

1969
01:19:18,155 --> 01:19:19,488
A TYPHOON'S APPROACHING.

1970
01:19:19,522 --> 01:19:20,923
IT'LL BE BEFORE THEN.

1971
01:19:20,957 --> 01:19:22,492
NOW, GET AWAY FROM ME,
YOU OLD FRUIT.

1972
01:19:22,525 --> 01:19:23,427
COME IN, PLEASE.

1973
01:19:23,460 --> 01:19:25,028
THIS IS OSHIMA.

1974
01:19:25,062 --> 01:19:27,330
YOU CAN START Z-PLAN.

1975
01:19:27,363 --> 01:19:29,432
ZE PLAN IZ STARTED.

1976
01:19:29,465 --> 01:19:30,800
[SERVO LAUGHS]

1977
01:19:30,833 --> 01:19:32,402
QUICKLY, TWIST
THE RUBBER BAND!

1978
01:19:32,435 --> 01:19:34,137
GET IT ON THAT LITTLE HOOK!

1979
01:19:34,170 --> 01:19:36,305
NOW, TURN THE PROPELLER!

1980
01:19:36,338 --> 01:19:37,873
TOY BOAT. TOY BOAT.

1981
01:19:37,907 --> 01:19:39,008
[ALL] TOY BOAT, TOY BOAT.

1982
01:19:39,042 --> 01:19:40,210
TOY BOAT. TOY BOAT.

1983
01:19:40,243 --> 01:19:43,213
- [ALL] TOY BOAT--
- TOY PLANE?

1984
01:19:43,247 --> 01:19:44,882
WAIT A MINUTE.

1985
01:19:44,915 --> 01:19:46,550
- OKAY--
- ALL RIGHT,

1986
01:19:46,583 --> 01:19:48,185
WE'RE FILLING THE BAY
WITH BREW!

1987
01:19:48,218 --> 01:19:49,853
[ALL] WHOO!

1988
01:19:56,627 --> 01:19:58,895
NORA, I HAVE GOOD NEWS.

1989
01:19:58,928 --> 01:20:00,397
- I JUST GOT AN ORDER
FOR CHICKEN LITTLES.
- THEY FOUND KENNY.

1990
01:20:00,430 --> 01:20:02,198
- HE'S IN OSHIMA.
- OH.

1991
01:20:02,232 --> 01:20:03,533
- AND THE GOOD NEWS?
- THANK GOD.

1992
01:20:03,567 --> 01:20:05,935
THANK GOD.

1993
01:20:05,968 --> 01:20:07,270
NOW, LET'S SEE,

1994
01:20:07,303 --> 01:20:10,440
WHAT COULD
I SCREW UP BIG-TIME?

1995
01:20:10,473 --> 01:20:12,442
YEAH, THAT'S IT. BOATS!

1996
01:20:12,475 --> 01:20:15,412
EVERYBODY NEEDS BOATS.

1997
01:20:15,445 --> 01:20:18,848
[PHONE RINGS]

1998
01:20:18,882 --> 01:20:20,017
- HELLO.
- YES, HELLO?

1999
01:20:20,050 --> 01:20:23,018
HIDAKA SPEAKING.
HIDAKA SPEAKING.

2000
01:20:23,052 --> 01:20:24,955
GAMERA WANTS $50,000 IN CASH

2001
01:20:24,988 --> 01:20:25,988
AND A GETAWAY...
[SERVO MUTTERS]

2002
01:20:26,022 --> 01:20:27,423
YOU CAN BEGIN.

2003
01:20:27,457 --> 01:20:31,227
YES, RIGHT NOW.

2004
01:20:31,260 --> 01:20:33,430
- YOU MAY GIVE THE ORDER.
- REGULAR OR CRISPY.

2005
01:20:33,463 --> 01:20:36,533
STAND BY.

2006
01:20:36,567 --> 01:20:38,100
TAKE YOUR POSITIONS.

2007
01:20:38,133 --> 01:20:40,003
[ALL]
AAH! SCATTER! EVERYBODY!

2008
01:20:42,038 --> 01:20:43,607
IT'S LIKE
A JERRY LEWIS PLATOON.

2009
01:20:46,577 --> 01:20:50,147
LIKE SHOOTIN' BARRELS
IN A FISH, OFFICER.

2010
01:20:51,313 --> 01:20:52,382
FLAME ON.

2011
01:20:52,415 --> 01:20:53,617
OOH.

2012
01:20:57,287 --> 01:20:58,522
YAY.

2013
01:20:58,555 --> 01:20:59,957
THAT'S NEAT.

2014
01:20:59,990 --> 01:21:01,658
WHAT, ARE THEY
WATCHING TENNIS?

2015
01:21:01,692 --> 01:21:04,493
OH, DEAR GOD.

2016
01:21:04,527 --> 01:21:06,062
THEY ARE WATCHING TENNIS.

2017
01:21:09,933 --> 01:21:12,435
SEE?

2018
01:21:12,468 --> 01:21:16,005
[GAMERA GROANS]

2019
01:21:16,038 --> 01:21:18,442
HEY, SMOKE ON
THE WATER, DUDE.

2020
01:21:18,475 --> 01:21:21,377
FIRE IN THE SKY.

2021
01:21:21,410 --> 01:21:23,480
- YOU DID IT.
- THE PLAN'S WORKING.

2022
01:21:29,685 --> 01:21:31,553
- NEAT.
- DR. HIDAKA, DR. HIDAKA!

2023
01:21:31,588 --> 01:21:33,957
GAMERA'S MOVING! HE'S PASSING
RIGHT IN FRONT OF US.

2024
01:21:33,990 --> 01:21:36,458
- WONDERFUL.
- MARVELOUS.

2025
01:21:36,492 --> 01:21:37,627
GAMERA IS HEADING THIS WAY.

2026
01:21:37,660 --> 01:21:39,162
- YEAH.
- HELLO?

2027
01:21:39,195 --> 01:21:41,097
- ALL RIGHT.
- HELLO?

2028
01:21:41,130 --> 01:21:44,500
YES, EVERYTHING'S READY.
ALL RIGHT.

2029
01:21:44,533 --> 01:21:46,135
EVERYBODY LOOK!

2030
01:21:50,040 --> 01:21:51,975
IS IT COMING?
IS IT COMING?

2031
01:21:52,008 --> 01:21:54,010
- PLEASE BE PATIENT.
- SHUT UP.

2032
01:21:56,345 --> 01:21:58,448
- HEY, HIS BINOCULARS FOGGED UP.
- WE BRING YOU THE LATEST NEWS

2033
01:21:58,482 --> 01:21:59,582
REGARDING THE TYPHOON.

2034
01:21:59,615 --> 01:22:01,718
THE TYPHOON SUDDENLY
CHANGED ITS COURSE

2035
01:22:01,752 --> 01:22:04,420
AND IS HEADING IN
A NORTHEASTERN DIRECTION.

2036
01:22:04,453 --> 01:22:06,488
IF IT CONTINUES
ON ITS PRESENT COURSE,

2037
01:22:06,522 --> 01:22:09,425
IT WILL VERY SHORTLY
HIT THE JAPANESE MAINLAND

2038
01:22:09,458 --> 01:22:11,962
CAUSING UNTOLD DEVASTATION
AND DESTRUCTION.

2039
01:22:11,995 --> 01:22:13,162
NOW, STICKS
ON THE TRAFFIC JAM.

2040
01:22:13,195 --> 01:22:14,597
- WHAT SHALL WE DO?
- RUUUUN!

2041
01:22:14,630 --> 01:22:17,367
THERE IS NOTHING WE CAN DO
BUT WAIT NOW.

2042
01:22:17,400 --> 01:22:19,368
GAMERA! GAMERA IS COMING!

2043
01:22:19,402 --> 01:22:21,437
GAMERA IS COMING!
GAMERA IS COMING!

2044
01:22:21,470 --> 01:22:23,205
♪ GAMERA'S COMING
GAMERA'S COMING ♪

2045
01:22:23,238 --> 01:22:25,342
♪ HEY EVERYBODY,
GAMERA'S COMING ♪

2046
01:22:25,375 --> 01:22:27,743
EMPEROR KENNY.
IT'S GOT A NICE RING TO IT.

2047
01:22:27,777 --> 01:22:29,712
I WILL SOON
BE CROWNED KING.

2048
01:22:35,018 --> 01:22:37,420
GAMERA! GAMERA!
DON'T COME!

2049
01:22:37,453 --> 01:22:40,390
GAMERA! GAMERA!
DON'T COME HERE!

2050
01:22:40,423 --> 01:22:41,758
KENNY?

2051
01:22:41,792 --> 01:22:43,427
KENNARINO! KENSTER!

2052
01:22:43,460 --> 01:22:45,295
THE KEN-MONSTER!
HEY.

2053
01:22:45,328 --> 01:22:47,030
- GAMERA!
- GAMERA, COME ON!

2054
01:22:47,063 --> 01:22:48,998
- COME ON, YOU LITTLE--
- COME ON, THAT'S IT!

2055
01:22:49,032 --> 01:22:51,100
HEEL TIME, BOY, COME ON.
[JOEL PATS KNEE]

2056
01:22:51,133 --> 01:22:52,502
- COME ON UP.
- ALLE, ALLE VI.

2057
01:22:52,535 --> 01:22:53,703
TALK ABOUT A BANACA BLAST.

2058
01:22:53,737 --> 01:22:55,505
OOF.

2059
01:22:57,407 --> 01:23:00,277
BOY, HOT BREATH.

2060
01:23:00,310 --> 01:23:02,512
THAT'S IT! THAT'S IT!

2061
01:23:02,545 --> 01:23:03,780
YES, OH YES.

2062
01:23:03,813 --> 01:23:05,582
YOU KNOW, HE DIDN'T
START THE FIRE.

2063
01:23:05,615 --> 01:23:07,650
IT WAS ALWAYS BURNING
SINCE THE WORLD WAS TURNING.

2064
01:23:07,683 --> 01:23:09,552
THANK YOU, UH, JOEL.

2065
01:23:11,688 --> 01:23:14,457
IT'S STOPPING.

2066
01:23:14,490 --> 01:23:16,125
KENNY!

2067
01:23:16,158 --> 01:23:18,060
KEN-NY!

2068
01:23:23,265 --> 01:23:25,568
PINEAPPLE BACK.

2069
01:23:25,602 --> 01:23:27,237
WE HAVE FAILED.

2070
01:23:27,270 --> 01:23:29,438
THERE HAS TO BE ANOTHER WAY.

2071
01:23:29,472 --> 01:23:31,173
DR. HIDAKA,

2072
01:23:31,207 --> 01:23:32,542
DON'T YOU THINK
IT'S ABOUT TIME

2073
01:23:32,575 --> 01:23:34,677
- WE START USING Z-PLAN?
- [SERVO MUMBLES]

2074
01:23:34,710 --> 01:23:36,378
- WE MUSTN'T.
- WHY NOT?

2075
01:23:36,412 --> 01:23:38,147
WE'RE SAVING IT FOR
THE NEXT FILM!

2076
01:23:38,180 --> 01:23:39,315
WE HAVEN'T ENOUGH FUEL.

2077
01:23:39,348 --> 01:23:42,452
TO ATTACK NOW
WOULD BE POINTLESS.

2078
01:23:42,485 --> 01:23:44,320
DARN.

2079
01:23:44,353 --> 01:23:45,322
WAIT A MINUTE.

2080
01:23:45,355 --> 01:23:48,090
DOCTOR!

2081
01:23:48,123 --> 01:23:50,127
NURSE.

2082
01:23:50,160 --> 01:23:52,228
H-- WHAT IS THIS,
FRANK BURNS?

2083
01:23:52,262 --> 01:23:54,663
MARGARET, I LOVE YOU!
I'M DOING IT FOR YOU!

2084
01:23:54,697 --> 01:23:57,100
STOP THAT! STOP THAT!

2085
01:23:57,133 --> 01:23:58,435
- STOP THAT MAN!
- WHO IS THAT MADMAN?

2086
01:23:58,468 --> 01:24:01,203
BUT-- DOCTOR, IT'S ALEX!

2087
01:24:01,237 --> 01:24:02,572
LET IT BURN! LET IT BURN!

2088
01:24:02,605 --> 01:24:04,707
BURN, BABY, BURN!
IT'S A DISCO INFERNO.

2089
01:24:04,740 --> 01:24:06,810
LET GO. CATHERINE.

2090
01:24:06,843 --> 01:24:09,312
ALEX, REPORTERS AREN'T ALLOWED
HERE. YOU KNOW THAT.

2091
01:24:09,345 --> 01:24:10,480
ESPECIALLY PYRO REPORTERS.

2092
01:24:10,513 --> 01:24:11,815
BUT I TAGGED ALONG ANYHOW.

2093
01:24:11,848 --> 01:24:13,617
BUT NOT JUST FOR THE STORY.

2094
01:24:13,650 --> 01:24:15,652
- I LOVE YOU.
- I SWEAR, I REALLY CAME ALONG

2095
01:24:15,685 --> 01:24:17,220
- ONLY TO HELP YOU.
- OH.

2096
01:24:17,253 --> 01:24:19,488
I CAME BY SEA ON
THAT TANKER THERE.

2097
01:24:19,522 --> 01:24:21,223
I WAS WORRIED ABOUT YOU.

2098
01:24:21,257 --> 01:24:22,825
BUT DID YOU
START THOSE FIRES?

2099
01:24:22,858 --> 01:24:25,228
- YEAH.
- I DID IT FOR YOU!

2100
01:24:25,262 --> 01:24:28,130
I STARTED WITH A SPARK
FROM MY HEART.

2101
01:24:28,163 --> 01:24:30,300
GAMERA IS DRAWN TO FIRE.

2102
01:24:30,333 --> 01:24:32,168
IT WILL NOTICE THE FIRE
AND THEN LAND HERE.

2103
01:24:32,202 --> 01:24:33,803
- YES, YES, I SEE.
- THAT'S RIGHT,
HE'LL KILL US ALL,

2104
01:24:33,837 --> 01:24:35,338
- THAT'S A GREAT IDEA.
- IT'S A GREAT IDEA.

2105
01:24:35,372 --> 01:24:37,340
COME ON, GIVE US A HAND!
GIVE US A HAND!

2106
01:24:37,373 --> 01:24:38,742
AAH! I LIKE IT!

2107
01:24:38,775 --> 01:24:40,410
WHOA. BURN EVERYTHING!

2108
01:24:44,213 --> 01:24:47,750
- WOO-HOO!
- I SCARED MYSELF,
I AM EVIL.

2109
01:24:47,783 --> 01:24:50,353
KENNY!

2110
01:24:50,387 --> 01:24:54,323
KENNY!

2111
01:24:54,357 --> 01:24:56,325
AND NOW GAMERA
IN A SCENE FROM...

2112
01:24:56,358 --> 01:24:57,693
HERE TO ETERNITY.

2113
01:24:57,727 --> 01:24:59,562
THAT'S MORE LIKE THE LENGTH
OF THIS MOVIE.

2114
01:24:59,595 --> 01:25:01,163
[SERVO CHUCKLES]

2115
01:25:03,767 --> 01:25:05,868
KENNY, JOIN ME, AND TOGETHER

2116
01:25:05,902 --> 01:25:09,272
- WE WILL RULE THE UNI-- OH.
- DARTH TURTLE?

2117
01:25:09,305 --> 01:25:10,607
- DIFFERENT FILM.
- KEEP THEM GOING.

2118
01:25:10,640 --> 01:25:12,275
FIRE THEM ALL!

2119
01:25:12,308 --> 01:25:15,412
HEY, IT'S JUST LIKE
A KLAN MEETING.

2120
01:25:15,445 --> 01:25:17,713
WITHOUT THE CHARM.

2121
01:25:17,747 --> 01:25:19,815
[GAMERA ROARS]

2122
01:25:21,217 --> 01:25:22,718
I'M HYSTERICAL AND WET!

2123
01:25:22,752 --> 01:25:24,220
OH, GREAT,
ALL THEY NEED NOW

2124
01:25:24,253 --> 01:25:26,857
IS A PLAGUE OF LOCUSTS,
YOU KNOW?

2125
01:25:26,890 --> 01:25:28,390
HEY EVERYBODY,
CATCH THE DROPS ON YOUR TONGUE.

2126
01:25:28,423 --> 01:25:31,293
READY? ROCK, LOCK...

2127
01:25:31,327 --> 01:25:33,362
MAN, THAT POOR
CROSS-COUNTRY TEAM.

2128
01:25:33,395 --> 01:25:34,597
THEY GOTTA GO
THROUGH EVERYTHING.

2129
01:25:34,630 --> 01:25:37,833
DOCTOR!

2130
01:25:37,867 --> 01:25:39,568
I'VE GOT IT.

2131
01:25:39,602 --> 01:25:41,503
WE'LL MOVE
THE PICNIC INSIDE.

2132
01:25:41,537 --> 01:25:42,772
YEAH.

2133
01:25:47,710 --> 01:25:49,378
THERE'S NO INSIDE LEFT.

2134
01:25:49,412 --> 01:25:50,780
GAMERA!

2135
01:25:50,813 --> 01:25:53,282
YOU NEVER LOVED ME, KENNY.

2136
01:25:53,315 --> 01:25:56,185
IT'S JUST THE ROCKS
THAT YOU CARED ABOUT!

2137
01:25:56,218 --> 01:25:57,553
IT'S TURNING AROUND.

2138
01:25:57,587 --> 01:25:58,822
WE FAILED AGAIN, I'M SORRY.

2139
01:25:58,855 --> 01:26:00,790
YOU DID EVERYTHING
YOU COULD, DOCTOR.

2140
01:26:00,823 --> 01:26:03,492
IT'S NO USE. LOUSY RAIN.

2141
01:26:03,527 --> 01:26:05,262
[ALL] SHAME. SHAME.

2142
01:26:05,295 --> 01:26:07,363
ETERNAL SHAME.

2143
01:26:16,572 --> 01:26:20,243
HERE'S SOMEONE
THAT CAN HELP YOU.

2144
01:26:20,277 --> 01:26:22,445
[GAMERA ROARS]

2145
01:26:22,478 --> 01:26:26,382
NOW WHAT?

2146
01:26:26,415 --> 01:26:28,517
BE AFRAID. BE VERY AFRAID...

2147
01:26:28,552 --> 01:26:31,820
OF KENNY.

2148
01:26:31,853 --> 01:26:33,957
I'M ONLY A SENTINEL
FOR KENNY.

2149
01:26:33,990 --> 01:26:35,825
I GET A LOT OF ATTENTION
BECAUSE I'M BIG.

2150
01:26:38,795 --> 01:26:42,532
LOOK! GAMERA'S TURNING!

2151
01:26:42,565 --> 01:26:45,200
HE'S TURNING JAPANESE.
I REALLY THINK SO.

2152
01:26:47,603 --> 01:26:51,007
I'LL HAVE WHAT
THE VOLCANO'S HAVING.

2153
01:26:51,040 --> 01:26:52,708
[GAMERA ROARS]

2154
01:26:57,713 --> 01:26:59,748
GEE, I DON'T KNOW IF
I SHOULD GO FOR THE PEOPLE,

2155
01:26:59,782 --> 01:27:02,618
THE VOLCANO,
OR WAIT FOR THE PIZZA.

2156
01:27:02,652 --> 01:27:04,487
HEY, NOTICE HOW THE WATER
ROLLS OFF HIS BACK.

2157
01:27:04,520 --> 01:27:06,322
IT'S THAT TURTLE WAX SHELL.

2158
01:27:11,393 --> 01:27:12,962
- WHERE'S THIS AT?
- END OF THE WORLD.

2159
01:27:12,995 --> 01:27:15,698
OH.

2160
01:27:15,732 --> 01:27:17,667
[CROW COUGHS]

2161
01:27:17,700 --> 01:27:19,568
UH, YOU'RE FLYING WITH
A LAWNMOWER HANDLE.

2162
01:27:19,602 --> 01:27:21,603
- PERMISSION TO LAND.
- REQUEST GRANTED.

2163
01:27:21,637 --> 01:27:22,872
YOU CAN COME IN.

2164
01:27:22,905 --> 01:27:24,307
THE VOLCANO
STOPPED ERUPTING.

2165
01:27:24,340 --> 01:27:26,042
- THAT WAS QUICK.
- OKAY, THANK YOU.

2166
01:27:26,075 --> 01:27:28,010
HEY, AARON SPELLING'S HOUSE.

2167
01:27:30,880 --> 01:27:33,650
- THERE IT IS.
- --N'T.

2168
01:27:33,683 --> 01:27:35,452
OOH, I HOPE THEY DON'T CRASH
INTO THE TOWER AGAIN.

2169
01:27:37,820 --> 01:27:40,523
KENNY, WAKE UP, KENNY.

2170
01:27:40,557 --> 01:27:44,293
NORA.

2171
01:27:44,327 --> 01:27:46,928
- NORA!
- NORA'S THEME.

2172
01:27:46,963 --> 01:27:48,330
I HAVE TO SCOLD YOU.

2173
01:27:48,363 --> 01:27:49,898
SCOLD ME LATER--
THERE'S NO TIME NOW.

2174
01:27:49,932 --> 01:27:51,533
- I'LL ENJOY IT MORE.
- ...THE Z-PLAN!

2175
01:27:55,037 --> 01:27:56,672
SAY.

2176
01:28:00,108 --> 01:28:01,010
- IT'S FANTASTIC!
- SO MUCH TO SEE,

2177
01:28:01,043 --> 01:28:02,878
- SO MUCH TO DO!
- ISN'T IT?

2178
01:28:02,912 --> 01:28:06,082
I CAN'T BELIEVE THAT
WE'RE REALLY HERE.

2179
01:28:06,115 --> 01:28:08,350
- KENNY!
- DRINK IT ALL IN, KENNY.

2180
01:28:08,383 --> 01:28:10,453
HURRY, OR YOU'LL
GET LEFT BEHIND!

2181
01:28:10,487 --> 01:28:12,655
OH, THEY'VE WALKED INTO
A BOSTON ALBUM COVER.

2182
01:28:12,688 --> 01:28:14,823
ACTUALLY, IT LOOKS
LIKE A MAD FOLD-IN.

2183
01:28:14,857 --> 01:28:16,492
[BOTS] YEAH.

2184
01:28:19,495 --> 01:28:21,030
MATTE PAINTING, GOING UP.

2185
01:28:25,435 --> 01:28:27,303
OH, AND MATTE PAINTING
TO THE RIGHT.

2186
01:28:31,740 --> 01:28:34,910
OKAY.

2187
01:28:34,943 --> 01:28:36,745
- DR. HIDAKA.
- PROFESSOR.
- CONGRATULATIONS.

2188
01:28:36,778 --> 01:28:38,613
A COMPLETE SUCCESS.

2189
01:28:38,647 --> 01:28:40,883
THANK YOU.

2190
01:28:40,917 --> 01:28:43,385
OH, GOOD, KENNY'S HERE.
WE CAN START.

2191
01:28:43,418 --> 01:28:45,722
STAND BY, PLEASE.

2192
01:28:45,755 --> 01:28:47,457
WELL, GIVE ME
A PHONE TO MOSCOW

2193
01:28:47,490 --> 01:28:50,993
AND A CHOCOLATE DONUT
FOR KENNY.

2194
01:28:51,027 --> 01:28:53,963
WE ARE READY TO PROCEED
WITH Z-PLAN.

2195
01:28:53,997 --> 01:28:55,698
START THE FLAMES.

2196
01:28:55,732 --> 01:28:57,367
AND THE MUSIC!

2197
01:29:00,970 --> 01:29:03,105
OH, UH,
THE KENNEDY MEMORIAL?

2198
01:29:03,138 --> 01:29:06,008
OR GREEK THEATER, MAYBE.
AMPHITHEATER.

2199
01:29:09,878 --> 01:29:11,513
HEY.

2200
01:29:11,547 --> 01:29:13,148
I KNOW IT'S A TRAP,
BUT I CAN'T RESIST.

2201
01:29:13,182 --> 01:29:15,685
I CAN'T HELP MYSELF.
I'M FLAWED.

2202
01:29:15,718 --> 01:29:18,420
- LET ME THROUGH.
- LET HIM THROUGH!
IT'S KENNY!

2203
01:29:18,453 --> 01:29:20,022
COME ON.
COME ON.

2204
01:29:20,055 --> 01:29:23,625
[GAMERA SCREAMS]

2205
01:29:23,658 --> 01:29:26,495
NOW, WATCH ME BUST A MOVE.

2206
01:29:26,528 --> 01:29:27,897
- [SERVO BEAT-BOXES]
- NINA PEEPLES, LOOK OUT.

2207
01:29:33,168 --> 01:29:35,772
- LOOK OUT.
- WATCH THE FLAME.

2208
01:29:35,805 --> 01:29:37,873
I AM IMPRESSED.

2209
01:29:40,843 --> 01:29:42,712
THERE'S A BIG PIECE
OF CHEESE IN THE MIDDLE.

2210
01:29:42,745 --> 01:29:46,015
UH...UH...

2211
01:29:46,048 --> 01:29:47,183
ARE THEY GONNA
FLUSH HIM NOW?

2212
01:29:47,217 --> 01:29:49,885
YEP.

2213
01:29:49,918 --> 01:29:52,855
AESCHYLUS IS STUNNING
AS THE GREAT GOD TORTOISE.

2214
01:29:52,888 --> 01:29:56,492
PHASE TWO. NOW, PHASE TWO.

2215
01:29:56,525 --> 01:29:57,793
[ALL] HUH?

2216
01:29:57,827 --> 01:30:01,597
HEY, SUDDENLY HE'S
A CHEWY NOUGAT CENTER.

2217
01:30:01,630 --> 01:30:04,033
WE'RE PUTTING GAMERA
IN THIS SOUNDPROOF BOOTH.

2218
01:30:04,067 --> 01:30:06,568
NOW WE'RE GONNA ASK HIS WIFE
A FEW QUESTIONS.

2219
01:30:06,602 --> 01:30:09,505
NOW PHASE THREE.

2220
01:30:09,538 --> 01:30:13,008
OH, THEY TURNED HIM INTO A GIANT
ANTI-PERSPIRANT ROLL-ON.

2221
01:30:13,042 --> 01:30:14,643
Z-PLAN.

2222
01:30:14,677 --> 01:30:16,845
BEGINNING COUNTDOWN.

2223
01:30:16,878 --> 01:30:18,580
- TEN...
- THREE.

2224
01:30:18,613 --> 01:30:20,015
- NINE.
- 42.

2225
01:30:20,048 --> 01:30:21,783
- EIGHT.
- ISH KABIBBLE.

2226
01:30:21,817 --> 01:30:23,118
- SEVEN.
- I FORGOT THIS NUMBER.

2227
01:30:23,152 --> 01:30:24,487
- SIX.
- PI.

2228
01:30:24,520 --> 01:30:25,788
- GOOGOLPLEX.
- FIVE.

2229
01:30:25,822 --> 01:30:27,022
- 666.
- FOUR.

2230
01:30:27,055 --> 01:30:28,892
- PLANCK'S CONSTANT.
- THREE.

2231
01:30:28,925 --> 01:30:30,760
- [SERVO MUMBLES]
- TWO.

2232
01:30:30,793 --> 01:30:31,927
- FIVE, SIR.
- NOONAN.

2233
01:30:31,960 --> 01:30:33,562
- NOONAN!
- ZERO.

2234
01:30:33,595 --> 01:30:34,897
[CROW] BLUGH.

2235
01:30:39,102 --> 01:30:41,537
HEY, JOEL,
REMIND YOU OF ANYTHING?

2236
01:30:41,570 --> 01:30:43,038
- YEAH, REMINDS ME OF THIS.
- AAH!

2237
01:30:43,072 --> 01:30:45,207
- HEY, CUT THAT OUT.
- HEY, JOEL.

2238
01:30:45,240 --> 01:30:47,777
♪ IN THE NOT-TOO-DISTANT
FUTURE ♪

2239
01:30:47,810 --> 01:30:49,878
[BOTS LAUGH]

2240
01:30:49,912 --> 01:30:51,513
YOU'LL GET SUED FOR THAT.

2241
01:30:51,547 --> 01:30:54,917
I'M GONNA SUE YOU
FOR USING THAT SONG.

2242
01:30:54,950 --> 01:30:56,585
[BOTS] BYE!

2243
01:30:56,618 --> 01:30:58,053
- [CROW MUTTERS]
- GOODBYE, TURTLE FRIEND.

2244
01:30:58,087 --> 01:30:59,488
I'M GOING TO MISS YOU.

2245
01:30:59,522 --> 01:31:00,957
HEY, HE'S GOT MY KEYS!

2246
01:31:04,660 --> 01:31:07,062
WELL, THEY LAUNCHED MERV
GRIFFIN'S MICROPHONE INTO SPACE.

2247
01:31:07,095 --> 01:31:08,730
- [ALL] OOH.
- A SPECIAL ANNOUNCEMENT.

2248
01:31:08,763 --> 01:31:10,500
THE MARS ROCKET
OF THE Z-PLAN,

2249
01:31:10,533 --> 01:31:12,535
CONSTRUCTED WITH
THE COMBINED EFFORTS

2250
01:31:12,568 --> 01:31:13,568
- OF THE WORLD'S SUPERPOWERS,
- IT'S HIM AGAIN.

2251
01:31:13,602 --> 01:31:15,872
WAS SUCCESSFULLY LAUNCHED
JUST NOW

2252
01:31:15,905 --> 01:31:18,240
WITH GAMERA
IMPRISONED INSIDE.

2253
01:31:18,273 --> 01:31:20,910
WE COULD NOT DESTROY
GAMERA ON EARTH,

2254
01:31:20,943 --> 01:31:23,278
BUT THE Z-PLAN,
THE LAST HOPE OF MANKIND--

2255
01:31:23,312 --> 01:31:24,980
- DESTROYED HIM IN SPACE.
- SUCCEEDED IN SENDING GAMERA

2256
01:31:25,013 --> 01:31:26,182
- UP TO MARS.
- HMM.

2257
01:31:26,215 --> 01:31:28,583
IT WAS MADE POSSIBLE ONLY
BY THE COOPERATION

2258
01:31:28,617 --> 01:31:30,118
OF THE MEMBER COUNTRIES
OF THE UNITED NATIONS--

2259
01:31:30,152 --> 01:31:32,722
- AND GOLAN-GLOBUS.
- PROVING ONCE AGAIN

2260
01:31:32,755 --> 01:31:34,157
- THAT SUCH GREAT
ACHIEVEMENTS--
- I LOVE YOU.

2261
01:31:34,190 --> 01:31:36,925
- CAN ONLY BE REALIZED
- KEEP COMING BACK. IT WORKS.

2262
01:31:36,958 --> 01:31:39,762
- THANK YOU.
- NICE JOB. GOOD WIN.

2263
01:31:41,697 --> 01:31:43,665
WELL, CATHERINE,

2264
01:31:43,698 --> 01:31:45,735
I SUGGEST YOU FORGET SCIENCE

2265
01:31:45,768 --> 01:31:48,203
AND INSTEAD REALLY BECOME
ALEX'S INSPIRATION.

2266
01:31:48,237 --> 01:31:49,938
YOU CAN'T DO BOTH,
YOU'RE A WOMAN.

2267
01:31:49,972 --> 01:31:53,175
- [THEY LAUGH]
- I ITCH.

2268
01:31:53,208 --> 01:31:55,912
WELL, KENNY,
GAMERA WILL BE SAFE THERE.

2269
01:31:55,945 --> 01:31:58,280
- YOU HAPPY?
- YES, I'M GLAD
HE WASN'T KILLED.

2270
01:31:58,313 --> 01:32:00,750
I'M GONNA BE AN ASTRONAUT
AND RIDE IN ROCKETS.

2271
01:32:00,783 --> 01:32:02,618
AND I'LL SEE GAMERA
AGAIN, RIGHT?

2272
01:32:02,652 --> 01:32:05,922
YEAH, THAT'S NEAT, BUT FIRST,
YOU'RE GROUNDED FOR LIFE, KID.

2273
01:32:05,955 --> 01:32:09,092
GAMERA! SEE YOU SOON!

2274
01:32:09,125 --> 01:32:10,793
HEY KENNY!

2275
01:32:10,827 --> 01:32:13,162
GET BENT!

2276
01:32:13,195 --> 01:32:16,132
YOU HEAR THAT?
IT'S GAMERA'S HEART BREAKING.

2277
01:32:16,165 --> 01:32:20,068
HE'S HEADING FOR
THAT STAIN UP THERE.

2278
01:32:20,102 --> 01:32:22,938
IT'S BEEN THERE
THE WHOLE MOVIE, TOO.

2279
01:32:22,972 --> 01:32:25,842
[SERVO HUMS]

2280
01:32:29,845 --> 01:32:31,680
- OH, NOW THAT WAS--
- GAMERA WILL BE BACK

2281
01:32:31,713 --> 01:32:33,348
IN THE BELLS OF ST. MARY!

2282
01:32:33,382 --> 01:32:35,918
NOW, VICTORY AT SEA!

2283
01:32:35,952 --> 01:32:38,020
[ALL] OR IS IT?

2284
01:32:38,053 --> 01:32:40,355
- LET'S GET OUT
OF HERE, YOU GUYS.
- LET'S BEAT IT.

2285
01:32:40,388 --> 01:32:42,792
WE HAVE TO--
WE CAN'T GET OUT YET.

2286
01:32:42,825 --> 01:32:43,858
THEY WON'T LET US OUT?

2287
01:32:43,892 --> 01:32:45,093
YOU MEAN THERE'S MORE?

2288
01:32:45,127 --> 01:32:47,663
WELL, THERE'S A LOT
OF END HERE.

2289
01:32:47,697 --> 01:32:49,365
- OH.
- AH.

2290
01:32:49,398 --> 01:32:52,668
- SANDY FRANK, THAT'S, UH...
- DIDN'T WANNA MISS THAT.

2291
01:32:52,702 --> 01:32:54,337
THE SOURCE OF ALL FILMS.

2292
01:32:56,972 --> 01:32:58,773
ROCK AND ROLL. THIS IS FUN.

2293
01:32:58,807 --> 01:33:01,177
- [ALL SIGH]
- THINK THEY'LL RUN
THE CREDITS AGAIN?

2294
01:33:01,210 --> 01:33:03,645
I DON'T KNOW, I THINK THEY'RE
JUST GONNA LET US DRIFT.

2295
01:33:05,715 --> 01:33:08,883
HEY, GET ME-- I'M A BUOY!

2296
01:33:08,917 --> 01:33:10,352
DING DING! DING DING!

2297
01:33:10,385 --> 01:33:12,288
DING DING! DING DING!

2298
01:33:12,322 --> 01:33:13,990
WHOA.

2299
01:33:14,023 --> 01:33:15,792
KIND OF LIKE LIFEBOAT.

2300
01:33:15,825 --> 01:33:18,827
YEAH.

2301
01:33:18,860 --> 01:33:22,097
SO.

2302
01:33:22,130 --> 01:33:23,765
- OH.
- LET'S GET OUT OF HERE.

2303
01:33:23,798 --> 01:33:25,000
- AH, FINALLY.
- LET'S GO.

2304
01:33:25,033 --> 01:33:26,635
- NEAT CROWN.
- JEEPERS.

2305
01:33:43,752 --> 01:33:45,287
YOU KNOW, FOLKS,
A QUALITY CAST

2306
01:33:45,320 --> 01:33:46,688
DESERVES A SECOND LOOK.

2307
01:33:46,722 --> 01:33:48,090
CAMBOT?

2308
01:33:48,123 --> 01:33:50,793
NO JAPANESE MONSTER MOVIE
WOULD BE COMPLETE

2309
01:33:50,827 --> 01:33:51,893
WITHOUT THIS GUY.

2310
01:33:51,927 --> 01:33:53,862
THE JAPANESE FOSTER BROOKS,

2311
01:33:53,895 --> 01:33:55,163
OUR OWN TAD HIROKUMA.

2312
01:33:55,197 --> 01:33:57,333
WATCH FOR HIM
ON THE CBS SPECIAL,

2313
01:33:57,367 --> 01:33:59,868
THE FLIAR'S ROAST:
AKIRA KUROSAWA.

2314
01:33:59,902 --> 01:34:01,837
HERE'S HIDEO FONTAINE,

2315
01:34:01,870 --> 01:34:03,405
ESTABLISHED CHARACTER ACTOR,

2316
01:34:03,438 --> 01:34:06,742
WHO TRAGICALLY DIED DURING THE
MAKING OF THIS FILM.

2317
01:34:06,775 --> 01:34:10,012
HERE'S LIGHT ROCK'S SENSATION
HARRY AND CARRIE

2318
01:34:10,045 --> 01:34:13,148
CARRIE'S GONE ON TO BE
AN ASSISTANT/SNAKE HANDLER

2319
01:34:13,182 --> 01:34:15,885
FOR LAS VEGAS MAGICIAN,
SEñOR REY.

2320
01:34:15,918 --> 01:34:17,118
WHILE HARRY HAS SUBSISTED
ON NOTHING

2321
01:34:17,152 --> 01:34:19,088
ON NOTHING BUT
GLADE MIST DEODORANT.

2322
01:34:19,122 --> 01:34:20,288
FOR THE LAST THREE YEARS

2323
01:34:20,322 --> 01:34:22,758
TO PROVE HIS LOVE
FOR COY CARRIE.

2324
01:34:22,792 --> 01:34:23,992
AND THERE'S SO MANY MORE.

2325
01:34:24,027 --> 01:34:26,362
THERE'S GENERAL CURLY
AND ESKIMO PETE.

2326
01:34:26,395 --> 01:34:28,930
THE KARNAK KNOCKOFF.
MARTHA GRAHAM.

2327
01:34:28,963 --> 01:34:31,800
COLONEL SANDERS-SAN.
MISTER EDDIE'S FATHER.

2328
01:34:31,833 --> 01:34:34,837
MAX, AND TROUSER
THE ARCTIC POOCH.

2329
01:34:34,870 --> 01:34:37,205
AND LET'S NOT FORGET
KENNY AND GAMERA,

2330
01:34:37,238 --> 01:34:39,408
WHO WILL BE APPEARING
IN THE BROADWAY REVIVAL

2331
01:34:39,442 --> 01:34:40,877
OF BOB CLAMPETT'S IMMORTAL

2332
01:34:40,910 --> 01:34:43,278
BEANY AND CECIL '91.

2333
01:34:43,312 --> 01:34:46,048
THIS IS TOM SERVO,
ANNOUNCING.

2334
01:34:46,082 --> 01:34:47,348
HEY, YOU DID A REALLY
GOOD JOB THERE, TOM.

2335
01:34:47,383 --> 01:34:48,783
GOOD JOB, TOM.

2336
01:34:48,817 --> 01:34:50,118
YEAH, YOU REALLY PUT
THAT ONE TO BED, SERVO.

2337
01:34:50,152 --> 01:34:51,353
OH, WELL,
I REALLY OWE IT ALL

2338
01:34:51,387 --> 01:34:53,155
TO GARY OLAN
AND HIS RADIO CLINIC

2339
01:34:53,188 --> 01:34:54,957
FOR BIG-VOICED MEN.

2340
01:34:54,990 --> 01:34:57,158
- GARY OLAN.
- YEOWCH! OH.

2341
01:34:57,192 --> 01:34:59,295
- HEY.
- THAT SMARTS.
- OKAY, WE GOT SOME LETTERS.

2342
01:34:59,328 --> 01:35:01,197
TO READ FROM PEOPLE
THAT'VE BEEN SENT UP HERE

2343
01:35:01,230 --> 01:35:03,165
BY THE VIETNAMADS.

2344
01:35:03,198 --> 01:35:05,968
AND THIS ONE IS--
COMES WITH A PHOTO.

2345
01:35:06,002 --> 01:35:08,070
UH, IT SAYS,
"DEAR JOEL, TOM SERVO,

2346
01:35:08,103 --> 01:35:10,205
- CROW AND GYPSY"--
- YAY!

2347
01:35:10,238 --> 01:35:12,475
"I FIRST SAW MST3K
ABOUT A YEAR AGO,

2348
01:35:12,508 --> 01:35:15,443
"AND I'VE LOVED IT
EVER SINCE.

2349
01:35:15,477 --> 01:35:18,513
"I SHOWED IT TO MY COUSINS,
AND HE LOVES IT TOO.

2350
01:35:18,547 --> 01:35:21,917
CROW IS MY FAVORITE,
ESPECIALLY HIS IMPERSONATIONS.

2351
01:35:21,950 --> 01:35:23,985
DO YOU KNOW WHICH ONE THAT ONE
IS, THE LLOYD BRIDGES HE'S GOT--

2352
01:35:24,018 --> 01:35:25,755
"BY THIS TIME,
MY LUNGS WERE,"

2353
01:35:25,788 --> 01:35:26,855
AND YOU KNOW HOW IT GOES.

2354
01:35:26,888 --> 01:35:29,158
- [GYPSY MUMBLES]
- YEAH, AND, UH,

2355
01:35:29,192 --> 01:35:31,060
"PLEASE SEND
MEMBERSHIP CARD INFORMATION

2356
01:35:31,093 --> 01:35:33,362
AND A PHOTO OF CROW
WITH HIS AUTOGRAPH."

2357
01:35:33,395 --> 01:35:35,765
BUT THIS GUY

2358
01:35:35,798 --> 01:35:38,767
WENT AND MADE A MODEL
OF TOM SERVO.

2359
01:35:38,800 --> 01:35:39,968
- OH, LOOK AT THAT.
- HEY, NEAT.

2360
01:35:40,002 --> 01:35:41,937
LET ME SEE THAT.
SAY, THAT'S PRETTY COOL.

2361
01:35:41,970 --> 01:35:43,238
LOOKS LIKE
A RASTER DRAWING OF ME.

2362
01:35:43,272 --> 01:35:45,273
YEAH, ANYWAY, LET'S PUT THAT
UP ON STILL-STORE.

2363
01:35:45,307 --> 01:35:47,142
LOOKS LIKE IT'S MADE
OUT OF LEGOS OVER THERE.

2364
01:35:47,175 --> 01:35:48,377
- [GYPSY] LEGO.
- THAT'S PRETTY NEAT.

2365
01:35:48,410 --> 01:35:50,312
THAT'S IT, SIRS.
WHAT'D YOU THINK?

2366
01:35:50,345 --> 01:35:51,813
AND-- AND THANKS
FOR NOT SENDING

2367
01:35:51,847 --> 01:35:53,548
- SUCH A BAD MOVIE
THIS TIME.
- YEAH.

2368
01:35:53,582 --> 01:35:55,117
WHAT DO YOU MEAN, THANKS?

2369
01:35:55,150 --> 01:35:58,120
OH, HERE. FILE THIS.

2370
01:35:58,153 --> 01:36:00,255
AND GIVE A JOEL A SHOCK
TO THE SHAMMIES.

2371
01:36:00,288 --> 01:36:02,858
ONLY LIVE TO SERVE YOU,
MY LORD.

2372
01:36:02,892 --> 01:36:04,527
OW! I GOT SHOCKED

2373
01:36:04,560 --> 01:36:07,497
IN THE SHAMMIES...

2374
01:36:09,198 --> 01:36:11,133
♪♪

2375
01:37:12,093 --> 01:37:14,062
BYE.
